{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2oN5R4e1FTLoASPLcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M8JLNnh6CT5g3rcMfkHCvW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":350},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9812,"cache_read_input_tokens":22631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9812},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"f7189ada-a8f4-4359-926f-f9754341b78a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:17:55.106Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2oMnYorimr3WK41NjL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M8JLNnh6CT5g3rcMfkHCvW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":350}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8JLNnh6CT5g3rcMfkHCvW","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t └──────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n301\t                ▼ typed events on EF.bus (goal, shot, pass, tackle, foul, card, whistle, bounce…)\n302\t   Presentation: Camera · Crowd · Commentary · Audio (sfx, music, crowd engine, babble) · HUD ·\n303\t                 Replay recorder · Rumble · Stats/Stickers · Network host (forwards events)\n304\t                ▼ draw(r)\n305\t   MatchView: pitch floor/walls, stands & crowd, goals & nets, actors (rigs), ball, effects, HUD overlay\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\t- **The Match is pure simulation.** It reads Intents, moves bodies, applies rules, and emits events. It never reads\n309\t  input devices, never plays sounds, never draws. Everything else reacts to its events and reads its state. This one\n310\t  rule makes the bots, the attract mode, replays, tests and the network host all work the same way.\n311\t- **Animation runs on the presentation side.** Rigs are updated from each footballer's state (`velocity`, `facing`,\n312\t  `action`, `actionU`, `pose`), not from input. A client on the network does the same from snapshot state.\n313\t- **The fixed step.** The engine runs `update(dt)` at 1/120 s. The sim uses `dt` everywhere and never `Math.random`:\n314\t  it uses `match.rng = E.rng(seed)`. Cosmetic randomness (crowd, particles, voices) uses `EF.fxRng`, a separate stream,\n315\t  so the same seed and inputs give the same match whatever the presentation does.\n316\t\n317\t### 4.2 Modules (src fragments, in load order)\n318\t\n319\t| File | Holds | Key names it exports (on `EF`) |\n320\t|---|---|---|\n321\t| `00-core.js` | the namespace `EF`, registries `EF.def/EF.get/EF.all`, the event bus `EF.bus.on/off/emit`, the tuning table `EF.T` and `EF.tune(key)`, RNG streams, small math helpers, deep-link parsing; then, in this order, the `broadcast` View, the `EF.KEYS` preset (§2.2), the `EF.SETTINGS` list (§6.31), and `new E.Game({...})` (§4.7), because the Game reads all three when it is created | `game`, `EF.def`, `EF.bus`, `EF.T`, `EF.tune`, `EF.fxRng`, `EF.KEYS`, `EF.SETTINGS` |\n322\t| `01-input.js` | `HumanController`, mouse aim, the euphoria chord, the intent recorder (for tests and attract), touch-only detection | `EF.Intent`, `EF.HumanController`, `EF.touchOnly()` |\n323\t| `02-glyphs.js` | glyph icons and `EF.prompt` (§2.3) | `EF.Glyphs`, `EF.prompt` |\n324\t| `03-audio.js` | SFX voices, songs, `EF.Crowd` audio (the crowd engine), `EF.Babble` (gibberish voices), `EF.Chant` (sung chants), rumble helpers; all no-ops headless | `EF.sfx`, `EF.music`, `EF.crowdAudio`, `EF.babble` |\n325\t| `04-art.js` | palettes, kits as rig colours, ball sprites, card/whistle/flag/glove sprites, crest painter, custom `E.SHAPES` (goal frame, corner flag, dugout, floodlight pylon, team bus, trophy, ad board, camera tower, podium) | `EF.kitColors`, `EF.drawCrest`, `EF.BALLS` |\n326\t| `05-anim.js` | the clip library (`Mocap.load(MOCAP.EF)`), `EF.Anim.play(rig, clip, o)`, procedural moves (body tilt recipes, keeper dives, header, bicycle, dive, celebrations), football kick specs | `EF.Anim`, `EF.KICKS` |\n327\t| `10-pitch.js` | pitch geometry constants, the TileMap (stands, boards, aprons, nets), floor textures by stadium (stripes, wear, mud, snow, wet sheen, puddles), lines, out-of-play tests | `EF.Pitch`, `P.X0 P.X1 P.Y0 P.Y1 P.CX P.CY P.GH P.BAR` |\n328\t| `11-ball.js` | ball physics (Body, surfaces, spin/curl, drag, posts and bar, net, boards), possession and dribble touches, ball trails, super-strike flight paths | `EF.Ball` |\n329\t| `12-footballer.js` | the Footballer entity: body, stats, stamina, state machine, action execution (pass, shoot, lob, through, skill, tackle, slide, barge, dive, air moves), contact and knockdowns | `EF.Footballer` |\n330\t| `13-keeper.js` | keeper positioning, shot reading, save decisions, dives, catches, parries, punches, distribution, rushing out | `EF.Keeper` |\n331\t| `14-team-ai.js` | `TeamBrain` (phase, formation spots, pressing, marking, runs), the ball-carrier decision model, set-piece routines, difficulty | `EF.TeamBrain`, `EF.BotController` |\n332\t| `15-rules.js` | the match state machine, the clock (game minutes, stoppage time), restarts, half time, full time, golden goal, shootout bookkeeping | `EF.Rules` |\n333\t| `16-referee.js` | the referee character, foul judgement, advantage, cards, theatrics judgement, VAR sequence, referee personalities | `EF.Referee` |\n334\t| `17-euphoria.js` | per-team Euphoria, gains and decay, Europhoria, Super Strikes (registry `super`), the Save Duel | `EF.Euphoria`, `EF.SaveDuel` |\n335\t| `18-setpieces.js` | kickoff, goal kick, corner, free kick, penalty, shootout controllers and their UIs' state | `EF.SetPiece` |\n336\t| `19-crowd.js` | stand layout, fans (sprites, and classic-style rigs in the front rows), crowd mood, crowd animation states, tifo, flares, Mexican wave, the crowd throw-back | `EF.CrowdView`, `EF.mood` |\n337\t| `20-events.js` | matchday events (registry `event`): seagull, beach ball, pitch invader, floodlight flicker, flare smoke, drone, fireworks | `EF.MatchEvents` |\n338\t| `21-camera.js` | the broadcast camera director (follow, lead, zoom by context, set-piece framing, cinematic moments, replay cameras) | `EF.Camera` |\n339\t| `22-replay.js` | the ring-buffer recorder and the replay player | `EF.Replay` |\n340\t| `23-commentary.js` | the commentary director (event to line pools, priority, cooldowns, pairs, variables), the radio box, the PA announcer | `EF.Commentary` |\n341\t| `24-hud.js` | score bug, clock, Euphoria gauges, name tags, stamina, power meter, reticles, radar, notices, prompts, the Save Duel ring, the fourth official's board | `EF.HUD` |\n342\t| `30-ui.js` | the 10-foot UI kit: a screen stack and widgets (Tile, Button, List, Slider, Toggle, Tabs, Card, Pager) with d-pad, stick, keyboard, mouse hover and click | `EF.UI` |\n343\t| `31-front.js` | scenes: `title`, `setup` (Kick-About), `penaltysetup`, `album`, `about`; the touch-only notice | scenes |\n344\t| `32-cup.js` | scenes: `cup` (bracket and story beat player: tabloid, travel map, talk, team talk, results), `tunnel` (walkout; also the AI Hub card), `ending` (ceremony, parade, credits) | scenes |\n345\t| `33-match.js` | scene `match`: builds a Match from options, runs it, MatchView drawing, half time, results overlay; deep-link parts | scene |\n346\t| `34-training.js` | scene `training`: drill select, the drill runner (registry `drill`) | scene |\n347\t| `40-attract.js` | the idle watcher (10 s on title and menu scenes) and scene `attract` (a scripted showcase, §6.29) | scene |\n348\t| `41-devmode.js` | the dev panel (tabs Tune, Cheats, Warp, Info), the pause-menu entry, F1, tuning persistence and reset | `EF.Dev` |\n349\t| `42-hub.js` | AI Hub sessions: scene `hubwait` (connecting), connect, card, ready, start, host role (sim, snapshots, events), client role (input, interpolation), server mode, leave, time-up, end, finish, the SESSION SETTINGS overlay | `EF.Hub` |\n350\t| `43-saves.js` | the save schema (cup progress, stickers, unlocks, records), `game.saves` hook-up, migrations | `EF.Save` |\n351\t| `50-teams.js` | team, formation, tactic and referee data (§7.1) | data |\n352\t| `51-stadiums.js` | stadium data (§7.2) | data |\n353\t| `52-story.js` | the cup's story beats, tabloids, team talk lines, challenges, stickers (§7.3, §7.5) | data |\n354\t| `53-commentary-lines.js` | the commentary line pools (§7.4) | data |\n355\t| `54-drills.js` | training drills (§7.6) | data |\n356\t| `55-audio-data.js` | songs and chants (§7.8, Appendix D) | data |\n357\t| `90-start.js` | `game.debug`, `EF.test` hooks, boot steps, the content validation run, `game.start({...})` | — |\n358\t\n359\t### 4.3 Core contracts\n360\t\n361\t**Intent** (what a controller asks of one footballer for this step):\n362\t\n363\t```js\n364\t{ move: [x, y],            // ground direction, length 0..1 (screen direction already turned to ground: view.screenDirToGround)\n365\t  aim: [x, y] | null,      // explicit aim (mouse reticle direction) or null (aim with move)\n366\t  aimPoint: {x, y} | null, // the reticle's ground point (mouse), for passes to a spot\n367\t  sprint: false,\n368\t  pass: B, shoot: B, lob: B, through: B, skill: B, sw: B, dive: B,   // B = { down, pressed, released, held (seconds) }\n369\t  euphoria: false,         // pressed this step (the key, or the chord)\n370\t  target: null }           // a teammate picked by a mouse click, or null\n371\t```\n372\t\n373\tEvery controller (human, bot, remote, script) returns one. `Footballer.act(intent, dt)` is the only way a footballer\n374\tdoes anything. Tests drive footballers by feeding Intents through `ScriptController`, or by pressing actions on\n375\t`game.input` (`input.tap('pass')`, `input.hold('shoot')`) through a `HumanController`.\n376\t\n377\t**Footballer state** (what the presentation, replays and the network read):\n378\t\n379\t```js\n380\t{ id, side, role, team, data /* roster entry */, body /* E.Body */, facing, stamina, ctl /* controller */,\n381\t  state: 'run' | 'kick' | 'slide' | 'poke' | 'barge' | 'skill' | 'air' | 'down' | 'stunned' | 'celebrate' | 'dive'\n382\t       | 'keeper-set' | 'keeper-dive' | 'keeper-hold' | 'off' /* sent off */ | 'setpiece',\n383\t  action: null | 'pass' | 'shot' | 'chip' | 'volley' | 'header' | 'bicycle' | 'divingHeader' | 'stepover' | ...,\n384\t  actionT, actionU /* 0..1 */, pose, expr, downT, cards: 0..2, sentOff: false, human: playerIndex | null }\n385\t```\n386\t\n387\t**Match state** (sim): `{ mode, half, clock /* real s */, minute /* game min */, stoppage, score: [a, b], possession,\n388\tlastTouch, euphoria: [a, b], europhoria: { side, t }, setpiece, shootout, cards, stats, rngSeed }`. Modes:\n389\t`'kickoff' | 'play' | 'stoppage' | 'setpiece' | 'goal' | 'celebrate' | 'replay' | 'var' | 'halftime' | 'fulltime' |\n390\t'extratime' | 'shootout' | 'over'`.\n391\t\n392\t**Events on `EF.bus`.** Each is `{ type, t /* match time */, side, who /* footballer id */, x, y, z, ...data }`. Types:\n393\t`kickoff whistle touch pass passDone intercept shot onTarget woodwork save catch parry tip goal ownGoal out corner\n394\tgoalKick crowdThrow tackleWon tackleFailed slide barge knockdown foul advantage card sendOff dive diveWon diveBooked var\n395\tvarDecision penaltyAwarded penaltyTaken shootoutKick skill nutmeg rainbow air header volley bicycle euphoriaGain\n396\teuphoriaFull europhoria superStrike saveDuel saveDuelResult celebrate replayStart replayEnd half fulltime extraTime\n397\tgoldenGoal shootoutStart shootoutEnd event stamina`. Listeners: audio, commentary, crowd, camera, HUD, stats, stickers\n398\tand challenges, replay markers, hub host, rumble.\n399\t\n400\t### 4.4 Scenes and flow\n401\t\n402\t```\n403\tboot ──► (AIHub.active?) ──yes──► hub: connect ─► tunnel (as the hub card) ─► match (session) ─► end screen\n404\t   └──no──► title ◄──────────────────────────────── any input ◄── attract (after 10 s idle on title/menus)\n405\t             ├─ CUP RUN ──► cup (bracket ▸ beats: tabloid ▸ travel ▸ talk ▸ team talk) ─► tunnel ─► match ─►\n406\t             │               cup (result ▸ tabloid ▸ stickers) ─► … ─► final ─► ending (ceremony ▸ parade ▸ credits) ─► title\n407\t             ├─ KICK-ABOUT ─► setup ─► tunnel (short) ─► match ─► results ─► setup | title\n408\t             ├─ PENALTIES ──► penaltysetup ─► match { shootoutOnly } ─► results\n409\t             ├─ TRAINING ───► training (drill list ▸ drill ▸ result)\n410\t             ├─ STICKER ALBUM ► album\n411\t             ├─ OPTIONS ────► game.menu('settings')\n412\t             └─ ABOUT & CREDITS ► about\n413\t```\n414\t\n415\t- Gameplay scenes (`match`, `training`) set `pausable: true` (when not in a hub session). Title, menus, cup screens,\n416\t  results and the attract mode do not.\n417\t- **Deep links** (for tests, `tools/check.mjs` and the dev Warp tab): `#title`, `#attract`, `#setup`, `#match`,\n418\t  `#match/<stadiumId>`, `#match/corner`, `#match/freekick`, `#match/penalty`, `#match/shootout`, `#match/super`,\n419\t  `#match/duel`, `#cup`, `#cup/r1`…`#cup/r5` (r1 the Qualifying Round … r5 the final; `#cup/final` works too),\n420\t  `#ending`, `#training/<drillId>`, `#album`, `#about`, `#dev/anim/<move>` (the animation gallery, §11.7). Queries:\n421\t  `?seed=N` (fixes the match RNG), `?touchonly=1` (forces touch-only mode), `?dev=1` (opens the dev panel at start).\n422\t\n423\t### 4.5 Simulation, presentation and network roles\n424\t\n425\t| Role | Runs the Match sim | Reads local input | Draws | Sends |\n426\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n427\t| Single machine (normal) | yes | yes (1–4 players) | yes | — |\n428\t| Hub host with a player | yes | its own player | yes | snapshots and events |\n429\t| Hub host as server (`AIHub.server`) | yes | no | no (draws nothing) | snapshots and events |\n430\t| Hub client | no: it applies snapshots to a mirror Match used for drawing | its own player | yes | its Intent |\n431\t\n432\tThe MatchView and the rig animation code are the same in all four. Only where the state comes from differs.\n433\t\n434\t### 4.6 Registries: the designers' language\n435\t\n436\t`EF.def(kind, id, spec)` registers content; `EF.get(kind, id)` and `EF.all(kind)` read it. Kinds: `team`, `formation`,\n437\t`tactic`, `referee`, `stadium`, `super`, `celebration`, `event`, `drill`, `beat`, `lines` (commentary pools), `chant`,\n438\t`song`, `sticker`, `challenge`, `ball`, `teamtalk`. Content refers to other content by id only. At boot,\n439\t`EF.validate()` checks every reference (a team's stadium, a player's super, a beat's team and photo, a line pool's\n440\tspeaker) and reports problems through `game.fail` (red box). The test suite runs the same check (§11.3). Adding a team,\n441\ta stadium or a cup round means adding entries, not code. Appendix C shows each shape.\n442\t\n443\t### 4.7 The Game object\n444\t\n445\t```js\n446\t// first: the Game resolves its view, preset and settings when it is created\n447\tE.VIEWS.broadcast = E.VIEWS.broadcast || new E.View('broadcast', 'Broadcast', 0, 40, 1, 1);   // as kits/pinball.js registers its view\n448\tconst session = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);   // session.js ran first (§3.3), so this is known from the first line\n449\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'broadcast', bg: '#06070c', id: 'europhoria-football',\n450\t  input: EF.KEYS,\n451\t  corner: !session,                         // the hub has its own corner bar\n452\t  menu: {\n453\t    settings: EF.SETTINGS,                  // §6.31: defined in sessions too (gameplay reads game.settings)\n454\t    controls: { pass: 'Pass / Tackle', shoot: 'Shoot / Slide', lob: 'Lob / Barge', through: 'Through ball / Switch',\n455\t                sprint: 'Sprint', skill: 'Skill move', switch: 'Switch / One-two', dive: 'Theatrics', euphoria: 'Europhoria' },\n456\t    items: session ? [] : [['Restart match', () => EF.restartMatch()], ['Dev mode', () => EF.Dev.open()]],\n457\t    quit: session ? false : 'title', saves: false } });\n458\t```\n459\t\n460\tSaves go through `game.saves` from our own menus, not through the pause menu. Theme the engine's standard HTML screens\n461\t(pause, settings, controls) to match the game with `new E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#fff6e0', paper: '#0d1430',\n462\taccent: '#ffc83a', muted: '#9aa6c8', danger: '#ff5a4a', line: '#2a3a6a' } })`, created once in `00-core.js`.\n463\t\n464\t---\n465\t\n466\t## 5. Engine changes\n467\t\n468\tThe engine is ours to change. Keep every change small and marked `// EF:`, and record each one in\n469\t`engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md` (what, where, why). Planned changes:\n470\t\n471\t1. **Dialog voices that babble (`E.Dialog`).** In `Dialog.update` the box calls `this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)` on\n472\t   every second newly shown letter (search for `this._blip++`). Change it so that `voice` may be a function: call\n473\t   `voice(ch, index, line)` once for each newly revealed character (including spaces and punctuation, which the\n474\t   function uses for pauses). Allow `say(text, { voice })` to set the voice for that call only, and restore it after.\n475\t   `EF.babble.voiceFor(speakerId)` returns such a function (§6.22.4).\n476\t2. **Shirt patterns and numbers (`E.Humanoid`).** In the shirt branch of the draw code (search for\n477\t   `const t = tones(C.cloth), plate = [shL, shR`), after the base fill, draw the kit pattern clipped to the torso plate,\n478\t   when `o.kit` is set: `{ pattern: 'hoops' | 'stripes' | 'halves' | 'sash' | 'plain', color2, number, numberColor }`.\n479\t   Build hoops as 3 bands: quads from lerps between the shoulder line (shL to shR) and the hip line (hL to hR) at\n480\t   fractions .2–.33, .5–.63, .8–.93. Build stripes as 3 vertical bands from lerps across the plate, halves as the\n481\t   left half of the plate, and a sash as a diagonal band from shL to hR. Use `px.poly` in `tones(color2).base`, and\n482\t   `.sh` on the side away from the light. Draw the number (1 or 2 digits, `E.font` `'tiny'`, `numberColor`) at the\n483\t   torso centre when the rig faces away from the camera (`!facingCam`). Sleeves take the shirt colour (they already do\n484\t   with `sleeves: 'short'`). Fallback if this proves hard: plain shirts in the main colour with `trim` in `color2`, and\n485\t   no numbers.\n486\t3. **Whole-body tilt (`E.Humanoid`).** A generalisation of the built-in roll (`_roll(u)`, applied when state `flip` is\n487\t   set). Add a state `tilt: { axis: 'forward' | 'right', angle, pivot: 'feet' | 'hips', lift }`. After `solvePose()`,\n488\t   rotate every joint in `J` (except `bladeDir`, which only turns) about the pivot by `angle` around the axis in the\n489\t   rig's frame `[forward, right, up]`:\n490\t   - axis `forward` (a sideways fall: keeper dives, sideways tumbles): `r' = r·cos a + u·sin a`, `u' = −r·sin a + u·cos a`;\n491\t   - axis `right` (pitching forward or back: diving headers, bicycle kicks): `f' = f·cos a − u·sin a`, `u' = f·sin a + u·cos a`;\n492\t\n493\t   then raise the whole body by `lift`, and by however much is needed to keep every joint above the floor (as `_roll`\n494\t   does). Set `this.mocapTilt = { body: M, head: M }` (the 3×3 rotation, rows forward/right/up) for that step so the\n495\t   face, hair and belt details tilt with the body (`_offsets` reads it). Move the cape and hair points for this step\n496\t   only and put them back before they simulate, exactly as `_roll` does with `this._unroll`. Keep the built-in `flip`\n497\t   untouched.\n498\t4. **Named audio buses (`Audio`).** Add `audio.bus(name)`: it returns a `GainNode` (created on first use, connected to\n499\t   the master gain) whose volume follows `game.settings[name]` when that setting exists. It returns null when there is\n500\t   no audio context (headless, or sound blocked). We use buses `voices` and `crowd`. Also add `audio.now()` (the\n501\t   context's `currentTime`, or 0) and expose `audio.noiseBuffer()` (the engine's existing noise buffer), so the crowd\n502\t   engine and the babble voice synthesise with the engine's own context, master volume and mute.\n503\t5. **Accented capitals in the 5×7 font.** Add glyphs for `É È Á Ó Ü Ö Ä Ñ Ç` and lower-case `é è á ó ü ö ä ñ ç`, drawn\n504\t   in the font's style (copy the base letter's bitmap and add the mark in the rows above, for capitals in the\n505\t   ascender space). Names and chants use them (\"OLÉ!\", \"ESTADIO PASAPASA\"). Until this lands, write them in ASCII; the\n506\t   content validator warns about any character the font cannot draw.\n507\t6. **Only if needed:** if the standard `glyphs` setting cannot be redefined from the game (§2.3), set\n508\t   `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs.value` to `'playstation'` and its options to PlayStation and Xbox.\n509\t\n510\tDo not change anything else without adding it to `CHANGES-ENGINE.md`.\n511\t\n512\t---\n513\t\n514\t## 6. Systems and mechanics\n515\t\n516\tUnits are world units (1 tile = 16), seconds and radians. `EF.T.<key>` marks a value tuned live in dev mode\n517\t(Appendix A).\n518\t\n519\t### 6.1 Pitch and stadium geometry\n520\t\n521\t- **Field** (inside the lines): length `L = 832` (52 tiles) along x; width `W = 512` (32 tiles) along y. Home side\n522\t  (side 0) attacks +x in the first half; the sides swap at half time.\n523\t- **Goals:** mouth 96 wide (`GH = 48` either side of `CY`), crossbar `BAR = 36` high, net 30 deep. Posts and bar are\n524\t  drawn as white 2-px bars (as the SPORTS kit does with `r.queue`) and collide as cylinders of radius 2.\n525\t- **Markings:** halfway line; centre circle radius 64; penalty area 112 deep and 320 wide; goal area 40 deep and 176\n526\t  wide; penalty spot 80 from the goal line; penalty arc radius 72 around the spot (outside the box only); corner arcs\n527\t  radius 8. Paint them in the floor texture, worn a little (the kit's `line(x, y)` approach, extended).\n528\t- **The TileMap** is generated from rows, as the SPORTS kit does. From north to south: the north stand (5 tiers, wall\n529\t  heights 34/44/54/64/74; each stadium can change this), the north apron (1 tile), the north boards (`h: 26`), the field,\n530\t  the south boards (`h: 26`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`, so they drop low when they would hide play), the south apron\n531\t  (2 tiles: dugouts, photographers, the fourth official), the outside. From west to east: the west end stand (4 tiers),\n532\t  low end boards (`h: 18`), the goal-end apron (3 tiles: the ball goes out here), the goal and its net floor, the field,\n533\t  then the same mirrored. Legend tags: `grass`, `net`, `apron`, `out`, `mud`, `puddle`.\n534\t- **The ball and the boards:** the touchline boards bounce the ball (Body vs walls). A ball higher than a board flies\n535\t  over it into the stands. The goal-line ends have no boards on the line: a ball that crosses the goal line outside the\n536\t  goal is out (§6.11).\n537\t- **Out-of-play tests:** `P.crossedGoalLine(ball)`, `P.inGoal(ball)`, `P.overTouchline(ball)`, `P.inBox(side, x, y)`,\n538\t  `P.inGoalArea(side, x, y)`. All are unit-tested.\n539\t\n540\t### 6.2 The ball\n541\t\n542\t- `new E.Body({ r: 3, friction: 0, bounce: EF.T.ballBounce /* .55 */, gravity: EF.T.ballGravity /* 600 */ })`, plus our\n543\t  fields `spin`, `roll` (for the sprite's turn), `lastTouch`, `trail`.\n544\t- **Rolling:** on the ground, `v *= exp(−dt · EF.T.ballFriction · surface)`. Surfaces: grass 1.0, wet 0.7 (it skids),\n545\t  hard and dry 0.8, snow 1.7, mud 3.0, puddle 4.0 (stops dead and splashes). In the air: `v *= exp(−dt · .12)`.\n546\t  Bounce by surface: grass .55, wet .45, snow .35, mud .2.\n547\t- **Curl:** while `|spin| > 0` and the speed is over 20, turn the velocity across its path by `spin · dt` (the kit's\n548\t  formula); `spin *= exp(−1.4·dt)`. Aftertouch sets spin (§6.5).\n549\t- **Woodwork:** if the ball's centre comes within `3 + 2` of a post's axis (z under `BAR`) or of the bar's axis,\n550\t  reflect the normal component with restitution .7. Emit `woodwork` (a \"DOINK\", and the crowd's \"OOOH\").\n551\t- **Goal:** the ball's centre is past the goal line by more than its radius, `|y − CY| < GH − 3`, and `z < BAR − 3`.\n552\t  Then emit `goal` (or `ownGoal` if the last touch was the defending side's), and hand over to Rules.\n553\t- **Net:** inside the goal box the ball bounces off the net's sides, back and top with restitution .2 and heavy damping.\n554\t  The net mesh (a 7×4 grid of points a side) gets an impulse at the hit point and springs back (k 60, damping 8). Draw\n555\t  the mesh as dithered white lines (`px.polyDither`, or lines at 50% blend).\n556\t- **Possession:** a loose ball becomes a footballer's when it is within 9 of his feet, `z < 9`, its speed is under\n557\t  `EF.T.trapSpeed` (210), and he has no `cool` (0.3 s after he kicked) and no `stun`. A faster ball is trapped only\n558\t  within 4.5, and the first touch knocks it 4–10 units away, depending on the player's skill stat. The sprite's\n559\t  `roll` advances with speed, and it uses 4 frames, not 2.\n560\t- **Dribble touches:** the owned ball sits ahead of the feet: offset `7 + 2·sin(stridePhase)` when running, `10–14`\n561\t  when sprinting (a knock-on gap a poke can reach), `5` when standing. A turn of more than 100° within 0.2 s slows the\n562\t  owner to ×0.7 for 0.2 s.\n563\t- **Super-strike paths** (registry `super`, §6.9): a ball with `superPath` set ignores friction and spin and follows\n564\t  its path function for its flight. Paths: `wobble` (a sine across the path), `zigzag` (3 sharp turns), `hammer` (hits\n565\t  the ground 3 times, shaking the screen, and keeps its speed), `meteor` (straight up off-screen, then down onto the\n566\t  goal), `around` (steers round every body in front of it), `split` (3 balls; only one is real; the decoys burst into\n567\t  confetti at the goal line), `rocket` (straight, with flames: the team super for non-captains).\n568\t\n569\t### 6.3 Footballers: movement, stamina, dribbling\n570\t\n571\t- Body: `new E.Body({ r: 5, friction: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Rig: an HD `E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, size, build, hair,\n572\t  hat, colors, kit })` (§8.1).\n573\t- **Speed:** `run = EF.T.runSpeed (88) × (0.85 + 0.3 × pace/100)`. Sprint ×`EF.T.sprintMul` (1.45); ×1.35 with the\n574\t  ball. Acceleration `EF.T.accel` (900). Turn rate: 14 rad/s without the ball, 9 with it (`E.approachAng`, as the kit\n575\t  does).\n576\t- **Stamina** (0–100): sprinting drains `EF.T.staminaDrain` (20/s). It regains `EF.T.staminaRegen` (14/s) after 0.5 s\n577\t  without sprinting. Below 25 the sprint multiplier is only 1.15 and the player's tag shows a sweat drop. At stoppages a\n578\t  tired player puts his hands on his knees (§8.3).\n579\t- **Stats** (0–100): `pace, shoot, pass, tackle, skill, keep, weight, temper`. `temper` drives the AI's foul and dive\n580\t  tendency.\n581\t- **Sent off:** state `off`. He walks to the tunnel and leaves the match. The team plays on with 3 outfield players,\n582\t  and its formation drops the role marked `drop` in the formation spec.\n583\t\n584\t### 6.4 Passing\n585\t\n586\t- **Choosing the receiver:** candidates are the teammates except the passer (the keeper only when the stick points\n587\t  back toward his own goal). The direction is `intent.aim || intent.move || facing`. Score each candidate by\n588\t  `cos(angle between direction and candidate)` (it must be under the pass-assist cone: Off 20°, Low 35°, High 70°;\n589\t  `EF.T.passAssistDeg` sets High), minus `distance/1200`, plus `0.15 × openness`. Openness is\n590\t  `min(1, nearest opponent's distance / 40)`. With no candidate in the cone, the pass goes along the direction into\n591\t  space. A mouse click on a teammate (`intent.target`) overrides all of this.\n592\t- **Ground pass:** speed `clamp(d · 1.5 + 90, EF.T.passSpeedMin /*150*/, EF.T.passSpeedMax /*300*/)`. It leads the\n593\t  receiver: aim at `receiver + receiver.v · (d / speed) · 0.8`. The pass stat adds an angle error with σ = `(100 −\n594\t  pass)/100 · 0.06` rad, doubled if an opponent is within 12 of the passer.\n595\t- **Through ball (`through` with the ball):** aim 50–90 units ahead of the receiver along his run (forwards make the\n596\t  run as the pass is played), at a speed that arrives as he does. It lands well in space or is intercepted.\n597\t- **Lob / cross (`lob`):** `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })` lands at the receiver's led position. Apex 30 when\n598\t  short, 55 when longer than 250. From a wide position in the final third (more than 150 from the centre line, within\n599\t  250 of the goal line) it is a cross to the penalty spot area, or to the teammate nearest it. The receiver then\n600\t  attacks the ball in the air (§6.5).\n601\t- **One-two (`switch` held + `pass`):** control stays with the passer. He runs on toward goal while the receiver plays\n602\t  the ball first time into his path 0.35 s after he receives it. The passer must be within 220 of the receiver.\n603\t- **Interceptions:** an opponent within 6 of a moving ball (z < 9) takes it if his tackle stat allows, else deflects\n604\t  it (with a speed loss, at a random angle up to 45°). Keepers in their box catch passes too.\n605\t- **Events:** `pass` (with `to`), `passDone` when a teammate receives it, `intercept`.\n606\t\n607\t### 6.5 Shooting, air moves\n608\t\n609\t- **Charge:** hold `shoot`; the meter fills over `EF.T.shotChargeTime` (0.8 s); release to shoot. Power `p` is 0..1.\n610\t  Speed `= 180 + p · (EF.T.shotSpeedMax /*420*/ − 180)`. Lift `vz = 25 + p · 90`. If `p > 0.95`, add a 50% chance of\n611\t  `vz + 40` (blazed over the bar).\n612\t- **Sweet spot:** releasing at `p` in 0.78–0.90 gives a **Screamer**: speed ×1.15, a white streak trail, a hit-stop of\n613\t  0.05 s, and the keeper's save rating ×0.75. The meter shows the zone in gold.\n614\t- **Aim:** the stick's component across the goal (screen up and down) picks the target y: `CY + aimY · (GH − 6)`. With\n615\t  no stick and shot assist on, the target is the corner farther from the keeper. Mouse aim: the target y is the\n616\t  reticle's y, clamped to the mouth. Accuracy error: σ = `(100 − shoot)/100 · 0.08`, plus 0.04 under pressure, plus\n617\t  0.05 when shooting across the body (more than 100° from facing). The error is drawn from `match.rng`.\n618\t- **Aftertouch curl:** for 0.4 s after the kick, stick input across the ball's path adds spin, up to ±1.6\n619\t  (`EF.T.curlStrength` 3.2 per second, the kit's formula). Emit `curl` once per shot (for training and stats).\n620\t- **Chip:** `lob` with the ball within 160 of goal while the keeper is more than 24 off his line: `E.arc` lands just\n621\t  under the bar behind the keeper (apex 45).\n622\t- **Air moves:** each step, predict the ball's path for the next 0.6 s. If a controlled player can reach a point on it\n623\t  where the ball is between z 6 and 40 (the **air-ball window**), the HUD shows the move's prompt. Pressing `shoot`\n624\t  (finish at goal) or `pass` (cushion it to a teammate) does:\n625\t\n626\t  | Ball height at contact | Condition | Move | Ball speed out |\n627\t  |---|---|---|---|\n628\t  | 22–40 | facing goal (within 110°) | **header** (a jump if z > 28) | 220–300 |\n629\t  | 22–40 | facing away from goal (more than 110°) | **bicycle kick** (slow motion 0.35× for 0.4 s) | 380–460 |\n630\t  | 8–22 | any | **volley** (a side volley if the ball comes from the side) | 300–420 |\n631\t  | 4–14 | sprinting, the ball crossing in front | **diving header** | 260–320 |\n632\t\n633\t  Contact happens at the move's active phase. The player's body is steered to meet the predicted point (a short dash\n634\t  of up to 40 units). Quality: the closer the contact point to the ideal, the less aim error. Events: `air`, `header`,\n635\t  `volley`, `bicycle`. CPU players use the same rules.\n636\t- **Events:** `shot` (power, sweet, target), `onTarget` (when the predicted crossing point is inside the frame).\n637\t\n638\t### 6.6 Skill moves (`skill`)\n639\t\n640\t| Input | Move | Effect | Euphoria |\n641\t|---|---|---|---|\n642\t| R1 + stick sideways | **step-over** (0.35 s) | a defender within 20 in front is wrong-footed with chance `0.35 + 0.5·(skill − his tackle)/100` (at least .15, at most .9): he stumbles (stunned 0.4 s) and you burst 12 sideways | +8 |\n643\t| R1 with a defender straight ahead within 16 | **nutmeg** | the ball goes through his legs and you run round him; chance `0.45 + 0.4·skill/100`; on failure he takes the ball | +12, an \"OLÉ!\" from the crowd |\n644\t| R1 + stick back | **spin turn** (0.45 s, `rig.spin` 2π) | you keep the ball and cannot be tackled for 0.2 s in the middle of it | +6 |\n645\t| R1 twice within 0.3 s | **rainbow flick** | the ball goes over your head forward (vz 110, 60 forward); a defender within 24 in front is beaten (stunned 0.6 s) | +12 |\n646\t| R1 + stick forward, nobody close | **knock-on** | the ball is pushed 40 ahead and you sprint onto it | +2 |\n647\t\n648\tSkill moves cost 8 stamina and have a 0.6 s cooldown. Events: `skill` (with its kind), `nutmeg`, `rainbow`.\n649\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"4ed49664-8dd2-4cc0-a7aa-99fe182e3c80","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:17:55.295Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":" └──────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                ▼ typed events on EF.bus (goal, shot, pass, tackle, foul, card, whistle, bounce…)\n   Presentation: Camera · Crowd · Commentary · Audio (sfx, music, crowd engine, babble) · HUD ·\n                 Replay recorder · Rumble · Stats/Stickers · Network host (forwards events)\n                ▼ draw(r)\n   MatchView: pitch floor/walls, stands & crowd, goals & nets, actors (rigs), ball, effects, HUD overlay\n```\n\n- **The Match is pure simulation.** It reads Intents, moves bodies, applies rules, and emits events. It never reads\n  input devices, never plays sounds, never draws. Everything else reacts to its events and reads its state. This one\n  rule makes the bots, the attract mode, replays, tests and the network host all work the same way.\n- **Animation runs on the presentation side.** Rigs are updated from each footballer's state (`velocity`, `facing`,\n  `action`, `actionU`, `pose`), not from input. A client on the network does the same from snapshot state.\n- **The fixed step.** The engine runs `update(dt)` at 1/120 s. The sim uses `dt` everywhere and never `Math.random`:\n  it uses `match.rng = E.rng(seed)`. Cosmetic randomness (crowd, particles, voices) uses `EF.fxRng`, a separate stream,\n  so the same seed and inputs give the same match whatever the presentation does.\n\n### 4.2 Modules (src fragments, in load order)\n\n| File | Holds | Key names it exports (on `EF`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `00-core.js` | the namespace `EF`, registries `EF.def/EF.get/EF.all`, the event bus `EF.bus.on/off/emit`, the tuning table `EF.T` and `EF.tune(key)`, RNG streams, small math helpers, deep-link parsing; then, in this order, the `broadcast` View, the `EF.KEYS` preset (§2.2), the `EF.SETTINGS` list (§6.31), and `new E.Game({...})` (§4.7), because the Game reads all three when it is created | `game`, `EF.def`, `EF.bus`, `EF.T`, `EF.tune`, `EF.fxRng`, `EF.KEYS`, `EF.SETTINGS` |\n| `01-input.js` | `HumanController`, mouse aim, the euphoria chord, the intent recorder (for tests and attract), touch-only detection | `EF.Intent`, `EF.HumanController`, `EF.touchOnly()` |\n| `02-glyphs.js` | glyph icons and `EF.prompt` (§2.3) | `EF.Glyphs`, `EF.prompt` |\n| `03-audio.js` | SFX voices, songs, `EF.Crowd` audio (the crowd engine), `EF.Babble` (gibberish voices), `EF.Chant` (sung chants), rumble helpers; all no-ops headless | `EF.sfx`, `EF.music`, `EF.crowdAudio`, `EF.babble` |\n| `04-art.js` | palettes, kits as rig colours, ball sprites, card/whistle/flag/glove sprites, crest painter, custom `E.SHAPES` (goal frame, corner flag, dugout, floodlight pylon, team bus, trophy, ad board, camera tower, podium) | `EF.kitColors`, `EF.drawCrest`, `EF.BALLS` |\n| `05-anim.js` | the clip library (`Mocap.load(MOCAP.EF)`), `EF.Anim.play(rig, clip, o)`, procedural moves (body tilt recipes, keeper dives, header, bicycle, dive, celebrations), football kick specs | `EF.Anim`, `EF.KICKS` |\n| `10-pitch.js` | pitch geometry constants, the TileMap (stands, boards, aprons, nets), floor textures by stadium (stripes, wear, mud, snow, wet sheen, puddles), lines, out-of-play tests | `EF.Pitch`, `P.X0 P.X1 P.Y0 P.Y1 P.CX P.CY P.GH P.BAR` |\n| `11-ball.js` | ball physics (Body, surfaces, spin/curl, drag, posts and bar, net, boards), possession and dribble touches, ball trails, super-strike flight paths | `EF.Ball` |\n| `12-footballer.js` | the Footballer entity: body, stats, stamina, state machine, action execution (pass, shoot, lob, through, skill, tackle, slide, barge, dive, air moves), contact and knockdowns | `EF.Footballer` |\n| `13-keeper.js` | keeper positioning, shot reading, save decisions, dives, catches, parries, punches, distribution, rushing out | `EF.Keeper` |\n| `14-team-ai.js` | `TeamBrain` (phase, formation spots, pressing, marking, runs), the ball-carrier decision model, set-piece routines, difficulty | `EF.TeamBrain`, `EF.BotController` |\n| `15-rules.js` | the match state machine, the clock (game minutes, stoppage time), restarts, half time, full time, golden goal, shootout bookkeeping | `EF.Rules` |\n| `16-referee.js` | the referee character, foul judgement, advantage, cards, theatrics judgement, VAR sequence, referee personalities | `EF.Referee` |\n| `17-euphoria.js` | per-team Euphoria, gains and decay, Europhoria, Super Strikes (registry `super`), the Save Duel | `EF.Euphoria`, `EF.SaveDuel` |\n| `18-setpieces.js` | kickoff, goal kick, corner, free kick, penalty, shootout controllers and their UIs' state | `EF.SetPiece` |\n| `19-crowd.js` | stand layout, fans (sprites, and classic-style rigs in the front rows), crowd mood, crowd animation states, tifo, flares, Mexican wave, the crowd throw-back | `EF.CrowdView`, `EF.mood` |\n| `20-events.js` | matchday events (registry `event`): seagull, beach ball, pitch invader, floodlight flicker, flare smoke, drone, fireworks | `EF.MatchEvents` |\n| `21-camera.js` | the broadcast camera director (follow, lead, zoom by context, set-piece framing, cinematic moments, replay cameras) | `EF.Camera` |\n| `22-replay.js` | the ring-buffer recorder and the replay player | `EF.Replay` |\n| `23-commentary.js` | the commentary director (event to line pools, priority, cooldowns, pairs, variables), the radio box, the PA announcer | `EF.Commentary` |\n| `24-hud.js` | score bug, clock, Euphoria gauges, name tags, stamina, power meter, reticles, radar, notices, prompts, the Save Duel ring, the fourth official's board | `EF.HUD` |\n| `30-ui.js` | the 10-foot UI kit: a screen stack and widgets (Tile, Button, List, Slider, Toggle, Tabs, Card, Pager) with d-pad, stick, keyboard, mouse hover and click | `EF.UI` |\n| `31-front.js` | scenes: `title`, `setup` (Kick-About), `penaltysetup`, `album`, `about`; the touch-only notice | scenes |\n| `32-cup.js` | scenes: `cup` (bracket and story beat player: tabloid, travel map, talk, team talk, results), `tunnel` (walkout; also the AI Hub card), `ending` (ceremony, parade, credits) | scenes |\n| `33-match.js` | scene `match`: builds a Match from options, runs it, MatchView drawing, half time, results overlay; deep-link parts | scene |\n| `34-training.js` | scene `training`: drill select, the drill runner (registry `drill`) | scene |\n| `40-attract.js` | the idle watcher (10 s on title and menu scenes) and scene `attract` (a scripted showcase, §6.29) | scene |\n| `41-devmode.js` | the dev panel (tabs Tune, Cheats, Warp, Info), the pause-menu entry, F1, tuning persistence and reset | `EF.Dev` |\n| `42-hub.js` | AI Hub sessions: scene `hubwait` (connecting), connect, card, ready, start, host role (sim, snapshots, events), client role (input, interpolation), server mode, leave, time-up, end, finish, the SESSION SETTINGS overlay | `EF.Hub` |\n| `43-saves.js` | the save schema (cup progress, stickers, unlocks, records), `game.saves` hook-up, migrations | `EF.Save` |\n| `50-teams.js` | team, formation, tactic and referee data (§7.1) | data |\n| `51-stadiums.js` | stadium data (§7.2) | data |\n| `52-story.js` | the cup's story beats, tabloids, team talk lines, challenges, stickers (§7.3, §7.5) | data |\n| `53-commentary-lines.js` | the commentary line pools (§7.4) | data |\n| `54-drills.js` | training drills (§7.6) | data |\n| `55-audio-data.js` | songs and chants (§7.8, Appendix D) | data |\n| `90-start.js` | `game.debug`, `EF.test` hooks, boot steps, the content validation run, `game.start({...})` | — |\n\n### 4.3 Core contracts\n\n**Intent** (what a controller asks of one footballer for this step):\n\n```js\n{ move: [x, y],            // ground direction, length 0..1 (screen direction already turned to ground: view.screenDirToGround)\n  aim: [x, y] | null,      // explicit aim (mouse reticle direction) or null (aim with move)\n  aimPoint: {x, y} | null, // the reticle's ground point (mouse), for passes to a spot\n  sprint: false,\n  pass: B, shoot: B, lob: B, through: B, skill: B, sw: B, dive: B,   // B = { down, pressed, released, held (seconds) }\n  euphoria: false,         // pressed this step (the key, or the chord)\n  target: null }           // a teammate picked by a mouse click, or null\n```\n\nEvery controller (human, bot, remote, script) returns one. `Footballer.act(intent, dt)` is the only way a footballer\ndoes anything. Tests drive footballers by feeding Intents through `ScriptController`, or by pressing actions on\n`game.input` (`input.tap('pass')`, `input.hold('shoot')`) through a `HumanController`.\n\n**Footballer state** (what the presentation, replays and the network read):\n\n```js\n{ id, side, role, team, data /* roster entry */, body /* E.Body */, facing, stamina, ctl /* controller */,\n  state: 'run' | 'kick' | 'slide' | 'poke' | 'barge' | 'skill' | 'air' | 'down' | 'stunned' | 'celebrate' | 'dive'\n       | 'keeper-set' | 'keeper-dive' | 'keeper-hold' | 'off' /* sent off */ | 'setpiece',\n  action: null | 'pass' | 'shot' | 'chip' | 'volley' | 'header' | 'bicycle' | 'divingHeader' | 'stepover' | ...,\n  actionT, actionU /* 0..1 */, pose, expr, downT, cards: 0..2, sentOff: false, human: playerIndex | null }\n```\n\n**Match state** (sim): `{ mode, half, clock /* real s */, minute /* game min */, stoppage, score: [a, b], possession,\nlastTouch, euphoria: [a, b], europhoria: { side, t }, setpiece, shootout, cards, stats, rngSeed }`. Modes:\n`'kickoff' | 'play' | 'stoppage' | 'setpiece' | 'goal' | 'celebrate' | 'replay' | 'var' | 'halftime' | 'fulltime' |\n'extratime' | 'shootout' | 'over'`.\n\n**Events on `EF.bus`.** Each is `{ type, t /* match time */, side, who /* footballer id */, x, y, z, ...data }`. Types:\n`kickoff whistle touch pass passDone intercept shot onTarget woodwork save catch parry tip goal ownGoal out corner\ngoalKick crowdThrow tackleWon tackleFailed slide barge knockdown foul advantage card sendOff dive diveWon diveBooked var\nvarDecision penaltyAwarded penaltyTaken shootoutKick skill nutmeg rainbow air header volley bicycle euphoriaGain\neuphoriaFull europhoria superStrike saveDuel saveDuelResult celebrate replayStart replayEnd half fulltime extraTime\ngoldenGoal shootoutStart shootoutEnd event stamina`. Listeners: audio, commentary, crowd, camera, HUD, stats, stickers\nand challenges, replay markers, hub host, rumble.\n\n### 4.4 Scenes and flow\n\n```\nboot ──► (AIHub.active?) ──yes──► hub: connect ─► tunnel (as the hub card) ─► match (session) ─► end screen\n   └──no──► title ◄──────────────────────────────── any input ◄── attract (after 10 s idle on title/menus)\n             ├─ CUP RUN ──► cup (bracket ▸ beats: tabloid ▸ travel ▸ talk ▸ team talk) ─► tunnel ─► match ─►\n             │               cup (result ▸ tabloid ▸ stickers) ─► … ─► final ─► ending (ceremony ▸ parade ▸ credits) ─► title\n             ├─ KICK-ABOUT ─► setup ─► tunnel (short) ─► match ─► results ─► setup | title\n             ├─ PENALTIES ──► penaltysetup ─► match { shootoutOnly } ─► results\n             ├─ TRAINING ───► training (drill list ▸ drill ▸ result)\n             ├─ STICKER ALBUM ► album\n             ├─ OPTIONS ────► game.menu('settings')\n             └─ ABOUT & CREDITS ► about\n```\n\n- Gameplay scenes (`match`, `training`) set `pausable: true` (when not in a hub session). Title, menus, cup screens,\n  results and the attract mode do not.\n- **Deep links** (for tests, `tools/check.mjs` and the dev Warp tab): `#title`, `#attract`, `#setup`, `#match`,\n  `#match/<stadiumId>`, `#match/corner`, `#match/freekick`, `#match/penalty`, `#match/shootout`, `#match/super`,\n  `#match/duel`, `#cup`, `#cup/r1`…`#cup/r5` (r1 the Qualifying Round … r5 the final; `#cup/final` works too),\n  `#ending`, `#training/<drillId>`, `#album`, `#about`, `#dev/anim/<move>` (the animation gallery, §11.7). Queries:\n  `?seed=N` (fixes the match RNG), `?touchonly=1` (forces touch-only mode), `?dev=1` (opens the dev panel at start).\n\n### 4.5 Simulation, presentation and network roles\n\n| Role | Runs the Match sim | Reads local input | Draws | Sends |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Single machine (normal) | yes | yes (1–4 players) | yes | — |\n| Hub host with a player | yes | its own player | yes | snapshots and events |\n| Hub host as server (`AIHub.server`) | yes | no | no (draws nothing) | snapshots and events |\n| Hub client | no: it applies snapshots to a mirror Match used for drawing | its own player | yes | its Intent |\n\nThe MatchView and the rig animation code are the same in all four. Only where the state comes from differs.\n\n### 4.6 Registries: the designers' language\n\n`EF.def(kind, id, spec)` registers content; `EF.get(kind, id)` and `EF.all(kind)` read it. Kinds: `team`, `formation`,\n`tactic`, `referee`, `stadium`, `super`, `celebration`, `event`, `drill`, `beat`, `lines` (commentary pools), `chant`,\n`song`, `sticker`, `challenge`, `ball`, `teamtalk`. Content refers to other content by id only. At boot,\n`EF.validate()` checks every reference (a team's stadium, a player's super, a beat's team and photo, a line pool's\nspeaker) and reports problems through `game.fail` (red box). The test suite runs the same check (§11.3). Adding a team,\na stadium or a cup round means adding entries, not code. Appendix C shows each shape.\n\n### 4.7 The Game object\n\n```js\n// first: the Game resolves its view, preset and settings when it is created\nE.VIEWS.broadcast = E.VIEWS.broadcast || new E.View('broadcast', 'Broadcast', 0, 40, 1, 1);   // as kits/pinball.js registers its view\nconst session = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);   // session.js ran first (§3.3), so this is known from the first line\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'broadcast', bg: '#06070c', id: 'europhoria-football',\n  input: EF.KEYS,\n  corner: !session,                         // the hub has its own corner bar\n  menu: {\n    settings: EF.SETTINGS,                  // §6.31: defined in sessions too (gameplay reads game.settings)\n    controls: { pass: 'Pass / Tackle', shoot: 'Shoot / Slide', lob: 'Lob / Barge', through: 'Through ball / Switch',\n                sprint: 'Sprint', skill: 'Skill move', switch: 'Switch / One-two', dive: 'Theatrics', euphoria: 'Europhoria' },\n    items: session ? [] : [['Restart match', () => EF.restartMatch()], ['Dev mode', () => EF.Dev.open()]],\n    quit: session ? false : 'title', saves: false } });\n```\n\nSaves go through `game.saves` from our own menus, not through the pause menu. Theme the engine's standard HTML screens\n(pause, settings, controls) to match the game with `new E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink: '#fff6e0', paper: '#0d1430',\naccent: '#ffc83a', muted: '#9aa6c8', danger: '#ff5a4a', line: '#2a3a6a' } })`, created once in `00-core.js`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Engine changes\n\nThe engine is ours to change. Keep every change small and marked `// EF:`, and record each one in\n`engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md` (what, where, why). Planned changes:\n\n1. **Dialog voices that babble (`E.Dialog`).** In `Dialog.update` the box calls `this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)` on\n   every second newly shown letter (search for `this._blip++`). Change it so that `voice` may be a function: call\n   `voice(ch, index, line)` once for each newly revealed character (including spaces and punctuation, which the\n   function uses for pauses). Allow `say(text, { voice })` to set the voice for that call only, and restore it after.\n   `EF.babble.voiceFor(speakerId)` returns such a function (§6.22.4).\n2. **Shirt patterns and numbers (`E.Humanoid`).** In the shirt branch of the draw code (search for\n   `const t = tones(C.cloth), plate = [shL, shR`), after the base fill, draw the kit pattern clipped to the torso plate,\n   when `o.kit` is set: `{ pattern: 'hoops' | 'stripes' | 'halves' | 'sash' | 'plain', color2, number, numberColor }`.\n   Build hoops as 3 bands: quads from lerps between the shoulder line (shL to shR) and the hip line (hL to hR) at\n   fractions .2–.33, .5–.63, .8–.93. Build stripes as 3 vertical bands from lerps across the plate, halves as the\n   left half of the plate, and a sash as a diagonal band from shL to hR. Use `px.poly` in `tones(color2).base`, and\n   `.sh` on the side away from the light. Draw the number (1 or 2 digits, `E.font` `'tiny'`, `numberColor`) at the\n   torso centre when the rig faces away from the camera (`!facingCam`). Sleeves take the shirt colour (they already do\n   with `sleeves: 'short'`). Fallback if this proves hard: plain shirts in the main colour with `trim` in `color2`, and\n   no numbers.\n3. **Whole-body tilt (`E.Humanoid`).** A generalisation of the built-in roll (`_roll(u)`, applied when state `flip` is\n   set). Add a state `tilt: { axis: 'forward' | 'right', angle, pivot: 'feet' | 'hips', lift }`. After `solvePose()`,\n   rotate every joint in `J` (except `bladeDir`, which only turns) about the pivot by `angle` around the axis in the\n   rig's frame `[forward, right, up]`:\n   - axis `forward` (a sideways fall: keeper dives, sideways tumbles): `r' = r·cos a + u·sin a`, `u' = −r·sin a + u·cos a`;\n   - axis `right` (pitching forward or back: diving headers, bicycle kicks): `f' = f·cos a − u·sin a`, `u' = f·sin a + u·cos a`;\n\n   then raise the whole body by `lift`, and by however much is needed to keep every joint above the floor (as `_roll`\n   does). Set `this.mocapTilt = { body: M, head: M }` (the 3×3 rotation, rows forward/right/up) for that step so the\n   face, hair and belt details tilt with the body (`_offsets` reads it). Move the cape and hair points for this step\n   only and put them back before they simulate, exactly as `_roll` does with `this._unroll`. Keep the built-in `flip`\n   untouched.\n4. **Named audio buses (`Audio`).** Add `audio.bus(name)`: it returns a `GainNode` (created on first use, connected to\n   the master gain) whose volume follows `game.settings[name]` when that setting exists. It returns null when there is\n   no audio context (headless, or sound blocked). We use buses `voices` and `crowd`. Also add `audio.now()` (the\n   context's `currentTime`, or 0) and expose `audio.noiseBuffer()` (the engine's existing noise buffer), so the crowd\n   engine and the babble voice synthesise with the engine's own context, master volume and mute.\n5. **Accented capitals in the 5×7 font.** Add glyphs for `É È Á Ó Ü Ö Ä Ñ Ç` and lower-case `é è á ó ü ö ä ñ ç`, drawn\n   in the font's style (copy the base letter's bitmap and add the mark in the rows above, for capitals in the\n   ascender space). Names and chants use them (\"OLÉ!\", \"ESTADIO PASAPASA\"). Until this lands, write them in ASCII; the\n   content validator warns about any character the font cannot draw.\n6. **Only if needed:** if the standard `glyphs` setting cannot be redefined from the game (§2.3), set\n   `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs.value` to `'playstation'` and its options to PlayStation and Xbox.\n\nDo not change anything else without adding it to `CHANGES-ENGINE.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Systems and mechanics\n\nUnits are world units (1 tile = 16), seconds and radians. `EF.T.<key>` marks a value tuned live in dev mode\n(Appendix A).\n\n### 6.1 Pitch and stadium geometry\n\n- **Field** (inside the lines): length `L = 832` (52 tiles) along x; width `W = 512` (32 tiles) along y. Home side\n  (side 0) attacks +x in the first half; the sides swap at half time.\n- **Goals:** mouth 96 wide (`GH = 48` either side of `CY`), crossbar `BAR = 36` high, net 30 deep. Posts and bar are\n  drawn as white 2-px bars (as the SPORTS kit does with `r.queue`) and collide as cylinders of radius 2.\n- **Markings:** halfway line; centre circle radius 64; penalty area 112 deep and 320 wide; goal area 40 deep and 176\n  wide; penalty spot 80 from the goal line; penalty arc radius 72 around the spot (outside the box only); corner arcs\n  radius 8. Paint them in the floor texture, worn a little (the kit's `line(x, y)` approach, extended).\n- **The TileMap** is generated from rows, as the SPORTS kit does. From north to south: the north stand (5 tiers, wall\n  heights 34/44/54/64/74; each stadium can change this), the north apron (1 tile), the north boards (`h: 26`), the field,\n  the south boards (`h: 26`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`, so they drop low when they would hide play), the south apron\n  (2 tiles: dugouts, photographers, the fourth official), the outside. From west to east: the west end stand (4 tiers),\n  low end boards (`h: 18`), the goal-end apron (3 tiles: the ball goes out here), the goal and its net floor, the field,\n  then the same mirrored. Legend tags: `grass`, `net`, `apron`, `out`, `mud`, `puddle`.\n- **The ball and the boards:** the touchline boards bounce the ball (Body vs walls). A ball higher than a board flies\n  over it into the stands. The goal-line ends have no boards on the line: a ball that crosses the goal line outside the\n  goal is out (§6.11).\n- **Out-of-play tests:** `P.crossedGoalLine(ball)`, `P.inGoal(ball)`, `P.overTouchline(ball)`, `P.inBox(side, x, y)`,\n  `P.inGoalArea(side, x, y)`. All are unit-tested.\n\n### 6.2 The ball\n\n- `new E.Body({ r: 3, friction: 0, bounce: EF.T.ballBounce /* .55 */, gravity: EF.T.ballGravity /* 600 */ })`, plus our\n  fields `spin`, `roll` (for the sprite's turn), `lastTouch`, `trail`.\n- **Rolling:** on the ground, `v *= exp(−dt · EF.T.ballFriction · surface)`. Surfaces: grass 1.0, wet 0.7 (it skids),\n  hard and dry 0.8, snow 1.7, mud 3.0, puddle 4.0 (stops dead and splashes). In the air: `v *= exp(−dt · .12)`.\n  Bounce by surface: grass .55, wet .45, snow .35, mud .2.\n- **Curl:** while `|spin| > 0` and the speed is over 20, turn the velocity across its path by `spin · dt` (the kit's\n  formula); `spin *= exp(−1.4·dt)`. Aftertouch sets spin (§6.5).\n- **Woodwork:** if the ball's centre comes within `3 + 2` of a post's axis (z under `BAR`) or of the bar's axis,\n  reflect the normal component with restitution .7. Emit `woodwork` (a \"DOINK\", and the crowd's \"OOOH\").\n- **Goal:** the ball's centre is past the goal line by more than its radius, `|y − CY| < GH − 3`, and `z < BAR − 3`.\n  Then emit `goal` (or `ownGoal` if the last touch was the defending side's), and hand over to Rules.\n- **Net:** inside the goal box the ball bounces off the net's sides, back and top with restitution .2 and heavy damping.\n  The net mesh (a 7×4 grid of points a side) gets an impulse at the hit point and springs back (k 60, damping 8). Draw\n  the mesh as dithered white lines (`px.polyDither`, or lines at 50% blend).\n- **Possession:** a loose ball becomes a footballer's when it is within 9 of his feet, `z < 9`, its speed is under\n  `EF.T.trapSpeed` (210), and he has no `cool` (0.3 s after he kicked) and no `stun`. A faster ball is trapped only\n  within 4.5, and the first touch knocks it 4–10 units away, depending on the player's skill stat. The sprite's\n  `roll` advances with speed, and it uses 4 frames, not 2.\n- **Dribble touches:** the owned ball sits ahead of the feet: offset `7 + 2·sin(stridePhase)` when running, `10–14`\n  when sprinting (a knock-on gap a poke can reach), `5` when standing. A turn of more than 100° within 0.2 s slows the\n  owner to ×0.7 for 0.2 s.\n- **Super-strike paths** (registry `super`, §6.9): a ball with `superPath` set ignores friction and spin and follows\n  its path function for its flight. Paths: `wobble` (a sine across the path), `zigzag` (3 sharp turns), `hammer` (hits\n  the ground 3 times, shaking the screen, and keeps its speed), `meteor` (straight up off-screen, then down onto the\n  goal), `around` (steers round every body in front of it), `split` (3 balls; only one is real; the decoys burst into\n  confetti at the goal line), `rocket` (straight, with flames: the team super for non-captains).\n\n### 6.3 Footballers: movement, stamina, dribbling\n\n- Body: `new E.Body({ r: 5, friction: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Rig: an HD `E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, size, build, hair,\n  hat, colors, kit })` (§8.1).\n- **Speed:** `run = EF.T.runSpeed (88) × (0.85 + 0.3 × pace/100)`. Sprint ×`EF.T.sprintMul` (1.45); ×1.35 with the\n  ball. Acceleration `EF.T.accel` (900). Turn rate: 14 rad/s without the ball, 9 with it (`E.approachAng`, as the kit\n  does).\n- **Stamina** (0–100): sprinting drains `EF.T.staminaDrain` (20/s). It regains `EF.T.staminaRegen` (14/s) after 0.5 s\n  without sprinting. Below 25 the sprint multiplier is only 1.15 and the player's tag shows a sweat drop. At stoppages a\n  tired player puts his hands on his knees (§8.3).\n- **Stats** (0–100): `pace, shoot, pass, tackle, skill, keep, weight, temper`. `temper` drives the AI's foul and dive\n  tendency.\n- **Sent off:** state `off`. He walks to the tunnel and leaves the match. The team plays on with 3 outfield players,\n  and its formation drops the role marked `drop` in the formation spec.\n\n### 6.4 Passing\n\n- **Choosing the receiver:** candidates are the teammates except the passer (the keeper only when the stick points\n  back toward his own goal). The direction is `intent.aim || intent.move || facing`. Score each candidate by\n  `cos(angle between direction and candidate)` (it must be under the pass-assist cone: Off 20°, Low 35°, High 70°;\n  `EF.T.passAssistDeg` sets High), minus `distance/1200`, plus `0.15 × openness`. Openness is\n  `min(1, nearest opponent's distance / 40)`. With no candidate in the cone, the pass goes along the direction into\n  space. A mouse click on a teammate (`intent.target`) overrides all of this.\n- **Ground pass:** speed `clamp(d · 1.5 + 90, EF.T.passSpeedMin /*150*/, EF.T.passSpeedMax /*300*/)`. It leads the\n  receiver: aim at `receiver + receiver.v · (d / speed) · 0.8`. The pass stat adds an angle error with σ = `(100 −\n  pass)/100 · 0.06` rad, doubled if an opponent is within 12 of the passer.\n- **Through ball (`through` with the ball):** aim 50–90 units ahead of the receiver along his run (forwards make the\n  run as the pass is played), at a speed that arrives as he does. It lands well in space or is intercepted.\n- **Lob / cross (`lob`):** `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })` lands at the receiver's led position. Apex 30 when\n  short, 55 when longer than 250. From a wide position in the final third (more than 150 from the centre line, within\n  250 of the goal line) it is a cross to the penalty spot area, or to the teammate nearest it. The receiver then\n  attacks the ball in the air (§6.5).\n- **One-two (`switch` held + `pass`):** control stays with the passer. He runs on toward goal while the receiver plays\n  the ball first time into his path 0.35 s after he receives it. The passer must be within 220 of the receiver.\n- **Interceptions:** an opponent within 6 of a moving ball (z < 9) takes it if his tackle stat allows, else deflects\n  it (with a speed loss, at a random angle up to 45°). Keepers in their box catch passes too.\n- **Events:** `pass` (with `to`), `passDone` when a teammate receives it, `intercept`.\n\n### 6.5 Shooting, air moves\n\n- **Charge:** hold `shoot`; the meter fills over `EF.T.shotChargeTime` (0.8 s); release to shoot. Power `p` is 0..1.\n  Speed `= 180 + p · (EF.T.shotSpeedMax /*420*/ − 180)`. Lift `vz = 25 + p · 90`. If `p > 0.95`, add a 50% chance of\n  `vz + 40` (blazed over the bar).\n- **Sweet spot:** releasing at `p` in 0.78–0.90 gives a **Screamer**: speed ×1.15, a white streak trail, a hit-stop of\n  0.05 s, and the keeper's save rating ×0.75. The meter shows the zone in gold.\n- **Aim:** the stick's component across the goal (screen up and down) picks the target y: `CY + aimY · (GH − 6)`. With\n  no stick and shot assist on, the target is the corner farther from the keeper. Mouse aim: the target y is the\n  reticle's y, clamped to the mouth. Accuracy error: σ = `(100 − shoot)/100 · 0.08`, plus 0.04 under pressure, plus\n  0.05 when shooting across the body (more than 100° from facing). The error is drawn from `match.rng`.\n- **Aftertouch curl:** for 0.4 s after the kick, stick input across the ball's path adds spin, up to ±1.6\n  (`EF.T.curlStrength` 3.2 per second, the kit's formula). Emit `curl` once per shot (for training and stats).\n- **Chip:** `lob` with the ball within 160 of goal while the keeper is more than 24 off his line: `E.arc` lands just\n  under the bar behind the keeper (apex 45).\n- **Air moves:** each step, predict the ball's path for the next 0.6 s. If a controlled player can reach a point on it\n  where the ball is between z 6 and 40 (the **air-ball window**), the HUD shows the move's prompt. Pressing `shoot`\n  (finish at goal) or `pass` (cushion it to a teammate) does:\n\n  | Ball height at contact | Condition | Move | Ball speed out |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 22–40 | facing goal (within 110°) | **header** (a jump if z > 28) | 220–300 |\n  | 22–40 | facing away from goal (more than 110°) | **bicycle kick** (slow motion 0.35× for 0.4 s) | 380–460 |\n  | 8–22 | any | **volley** (a side volley if the ball comes from the side) | 300–420 |\n  | 4–14 | sprinting, the ball crossing in front | **diving header** | 260–320 |\n\n  Contact happens at the move's active phase. The player's body is steered to meet the predicted point (a short dash\n  of up to 40 units). Quality: the closer the contact point to the ideal, the less aim error. Events: `air`, `header`,\n  `volley`, `bicycle`. CPU players use the same rules.\n- **Events:** `shot` (power, sweet, target), `onTarget` (when the predicted crossing point is inside the frame).\n\n### 6.6 Skill moves (`skill`)\n\n| Input | Move | Effect | Euphoria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 + stick sideways | **step-over** (0.35 s) | a defender within 20 in front is wrong-footed with chance `0.35 + 0.5·(skill − his tackle)/100` (at least .15, at most .9): he stumbles (stunned 0.4 s) and you burst 12 sideways | +8 |\n| R1 with a defender straight ahead within 16 | **nutmeg** | the ball goes through his legs and you run round him; chance `0.45 + 0.4·skill/100`; on failure he takes the ball | +12, an \"OLÉ!\" from the crowd |\n| R1 + stick back | **spin turn** (0.45 s, `rig.spin` 2π) | you keep the ball and cannot be tackled for 0.2 s in the middle of it | +6 |\n| R1 twice within 0.3 s | **rainbow flick** | the ball goes over your head forward (vz 110, 60 forward); a defender within 24 in front is beaten (stunned 0.6 s) | +12 |\n| R1 + stick forward, nobody close | **knock-on** | the ball is pushed 40 ahead and you sprint onto it | +2 |\n\nSkill moves cost 8 stamina and have a 0.6 s cooldown. Events: `skill` (with its kind), `nutmeg`, `rainbow`.\n","numLines":350,"startLine":300,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M8JLNnh6CT5g3rcMfkHCvW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2ojXWXWKpuzatyfbaw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KKmKkGHvTC2XHURWNdvnxd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":650,"limit":350},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14260,"cache_read_input_tokens":32443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14260},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"040df6eb-bd20-414b-88be-83f16de7d358","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:17:58.765Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2ojG8xD8kPJBywbx5U","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KKmKkGHvTC2XHURWNdvnxd":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":650,"limit":350}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KKmKkGHvTC2XHURWNdvnxd","type":"tool_result","content":"650\t### 6.7 Defending\n651\t\n652\t- **Standing tackle / poke** (`pass` without the ball): 0.25 s; the toe reaches 9 (`EF.T.tackleReach`). It wins the\n653\t  ball if the ball is within reach and on the near side of the carrier. A miss costs 0.3 s of recovery. If it touches\n654\t  the carrier's body and not the ball, it is a light foul candidate.\n655\t- **Slide tackle** (`shoot` without the ball): a slide at `EF.T.slideSpeed` (190), decaying with `exp(−3·dt)`, over\n656\t  0.45 s. The hitbox is a capsule along the feet (length 12, radius 4). Ball first: the ball shoots off in the slide's\n657\t  direction at 150, and the tackle is fair. Man first: a foul candidate (§6.10), and the victim is **launched**: an OTT\n658\t  cartwheel (0.6 s in the air, `vz` 120, spinning with a tilt about the forward axis, stars) before he hits the ground\n659\t  (state `down`, 0.9–1.4 s). The slider gets up after 0.6 s.\n660\t- **Shoulder barge** (`lob` without the ball): a 0.3 s lunge; its hitbox is a circle of radius 7 at the shoulder. Hit\n661\t  the carrier side-on: if `weight + rng·30 > his weight + rng·30` he stumbles and loses the ball; else you bounce off.\n662\t  From behind it is a foul candidate.\n663\t- **Switching:** `switch` or `through` (without the ball) switches to the teammate nearest the ball; pressing again\n664\t  takes the next nearest. Settings → Game → Switching: **Auto** (switches by itself on a loss of possession and when a\n665\t  pass reaches a teammate), **Assisted** (the default: Auto, but never while you hold sprint), **Manual**. A mouse click\n666\t  on a teammate while defending switches to him.\n667\t- **Knockdowns:** a foul, a heavy barge, a super strike through a body, or a collision at a closing speed over 220\n668\t  knocks the victim down: state `down` for `downT` (0.8–1.4 s), then he gets up (§8.3). Emit `knockdown`. Use\n669\t  `game.hitFx` at the contact point with `power` by severity (it gives hit-stop, shake, a star, sparks and rumble).\n670\t\n671\t### 6.8 Goalkeepers\n672\t\n673\t- **Positioning:** on the bisector of the angle from the ball to the two posts, at distance\n674\t  `clamp(8 + (400 − ballDist) · 0.06, 6, 36)` from the goal line. He shuffles sideways (facing the ball), crouched in\n675\t  the set pose when the ball is within 200. He comes out to **rush** a carrier who is through on goal (within 120, no\n676\t  defender between) and **smothers** at his feet (a low forward dive).\n677\t- **Reading a shot:** on `shot`, predict where the ball crosses the goal line (y, z) and when (`tCross`). After his\n678\t  reaction time (`EF.T.keeperReaction`, 0.18 s, ±40% by the keep stat and difficulty, ×1.3 against Screamers), he\n679\t  moves or dives toward the point. Reach: the dive covers `EF.T.keeperReach` (48) laterally in 0.35 s, plus 12 of arm\n680\t  reach (in z: 0–40 on a high dive).\n681\t- **Outcome** when he gets there: `q` = how well he reached it (0..1), times the shot speed factor (`1 − (speed − 200)/400`,\n682\t  at least .2), times keep/100. If `q > .7` and the speed is under 260, a **catch** (he holds it: state `keeper-hold`).\n683\t  Else if `q > .35`, a **parry** (the ball rebounds at 40–60% speed, away from the goal centre, so rebounds happen) or\n684\t  a **tip** round the post or over the bar (a high ball near the frame becomes a corner). Else a goal.\n685\t- **Distribution:** hold up to 2 s (the human side waits for ✕ throw / □ long kick, then the AI decides). Throw:\n686\t  E.arc to the open teammate nearest the keeper (an underarm roll if he is within 120). Long kick: E.arc 300–450 toward\n687\t  the most advanced teammate (route-one teams always kick long). Opponents must stay 60 away while he holds it.\n688\t- **Animation:** the set stance; side shuffles; the dive (tilt about the forward axis ±70–95°, lifted 2 on a low dive\n689\t  and 14 on a high dive, arms over the head with IK to the ball); the catch (hands to the chest); the parry (`jab`);\n690\t  the tip (one arm up); the get-up; the throw (`OverhandThrow`), §8.3.\n691\t\n692\t### 6.9 Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes, the Save Duel\n693\t\n694\t**Euphoria** is each side's crowd, 0–100, drawn as the \"EUPHORIA\" gauge under the team's name in the score bug, in 3\n695\tsegments.\n696\t\n697\t| Event | Euphoria (× `EF.T.euphoriaGain` and the team's crowd factor) |\n698\t|---|---|\n699\t| a completed pass | +2, +1 more for each pass in an unbroken chain (at most +8 a pass) |\n700\t| a successful skill move | +6 to +12 (§6.6) |\n701\t| a tackle that wins the ball | +6; a slide that wins it cleanly +8 |\n702\t| a shot on target | +5; the woodwork +7; a Screamer +4 more |\n703\t| a save (the keeper's side) | +6; a catch from a Screamer +10 |\n704\t| a goal | +35 to the scorer's side; −10 to the other |\n705\t| a celebration picked in time (§6.21) | +5 to +15 by the celebration |\n706\t| a dive that wins a foul | +5; a dive that gets booked −20 (the crowd boos) |\n707\t| decay | −`EF.T.euphoriaDecay` (1.5) per second when above 0 and not in Europhoria |\n708\t\n709\t- **Thresholds:** 34 (stamina regenerates 25% faster), 67 (shots charge 20% faster; the fans wave their scarves and\n710\t  sing), 100 (**EUROPHORIA READY**: the gauge flashes, the prompt \"L1+R1 EUROPHORIA!\" shows, the tifo is held ready).\n711\t- **Europhoria** (press `euphoria` when full): `EF.T.europhoriaTime` (8 s of game time; it keeps counting through\n712\t  stoppages and slows with slow motion). The\n713\t  side gets speed +12%, free sprinting, a tackle reach of +25%, and the keeper +30% reach. The music's Europhoria layer\n714\t  comes in, the side's fans light flares and unfurl the tifo, the LED boards turn to the team's colours, and the\n715\t  side's players glow faintly (emissive outline). One **Super Strike** is unlocked for the side during Europhoria. The\n716\t  gauge drains to 0 over the duration. Emit `europhoria`.\n717\t- **Super Strike:** during Europhoria, any shot charged to `p ≥ 0.9` becomes a super strike. The captain's is his own\n718\t  (registry `super`, §7.1); any other player's is the team super `rocket`. The sequence: 0.6 s of charge-up (the\n719\t  shooter rises 6, the camera zooms to 1.4, time slows to 0.3×, a radial burst, the super's name in big letters), then\n720\t  the strike at `EF.T.superSpeed` (520) along its path. The keeper cannot save it normally:\n721\t  - **Save Duel** (the defending side has a human): a timing ring shrinks around the keeper (1.0 s, at real speed even\n722\t    though the game is in slow motion: count it in unscaled time, `dt / game.timeScale`, so tests stay exact) toward a\n723\t    target circle, with the glyph of `pass` (✕). Press within ±60 ms of\n724\t    the target for **PERFECT** (a catch: Euphoria +15 for the defenders, the crowd erupts). Within ±140 ms gives\n725\t    **GOOD** (a parry: the ball spins away). Otherwise **MISS** (a goal: the keeper and the ball go into the net\n726\t    together, OTT). Several human defenders: the one controlling the player nearest the keeper takes the duel.\n727\t  - CPU keeper against a human's super: save chance Easy 15%, Normal 30%, Hard 45%, Europhoric 55%. The outcome is\n728\t    shown with the same animations.\n729\t- Events: `euphoriaGain`, `euphoriaFull`, `europhoria`, `superStrike`, `saveDuel`, `saveDuelResult`.\n730\t\n731\t### 6.10 The referee, fouls, advantage, cards, theatrics, VAR\n732\t\n733\t- **The referee** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, a whistle sprite). He follows play 60–90 from the ball,\n734\t  stays out of passing lanes, and is a Body the ball can hit (he falls over comically: `down` and an \"OOOH\"). He has a\n735\t  personality (registry `referee`): `strictness` (0.6–1.4), `gullibility` (how often he buys dives, 0.2–0.7),\n736\t  `varHappy` (0–1), `voice`.\n737\t- **Foul judgement:** on a tackle, slide or barge contact with a body before the ball (or with no ball near), compute\n738\t  `severity = closingSpeed/150 × (fromBehind ? 1.5 : 1) × (late ? 1.4 : 1) × (slide ? 1.2 : 1)`. `fromBehind`: the\n739\t  tackler is more than 120° from the victim's facing. `late`: the victim had passed more than 0.4 s earlier. It is a\n740\t  foul if `k = severity × strictness × EF.T.foulStrictness` is over 0.5. Cards on the same `k`: a yellow above 1.3, a\n741\t  straight red above 2.4, and a second yellow is a red. Settings → Game → Cards: Off (fouls, no cards) / Normal /\n742\t  Strict (`k` ×1.3).\n743\t- **Advantage:** if the fouled side still has the ball 0.8 s after the foul, show \"ADVANTAGE!\" (the referee's arms\n744\t  forward) and play on. Any card waits for the next stoppage (\"the referee will come back to that\").\n745\t- **Restart:** a direct free kick where the foul happened; a penalty if a defender fouls inside his own box. The\n746\t  referee's whistle, the jog over, the card (he raises it high: §8.3), the player's protest (`Angry` or `Shrug` clip).\n747\t  The crowd boos the card.\n748\t- **Theatrics (`dive`):** the player flops theatrically (§8.3). The referee judges:\n749\t  - if an opponent touched him (any contact within the last 0.5 s), or an opponent is within 8 and closing: it is a\n750\t    foul with chance `gullibility × (1.2 − d/14)` (at least .1), else play on;\n751\t  - if no opponent is within 14 and there was no contact in 0.5 s: **SIMULATION!**, a yellow card for the diver, the\n752\t    crowd boos, Euphoria −20.\n753\t\n754\t  The diver is down for 1.2 s either way. AC Lucchetto's AI dives in the box on purpose.\n755\t- **VAR:** checks every penalty award, and goals scored within 3 s of an unpunished foul in the build-up (with\n756\t  `varHappy` chance). The sequence (2.5 s): \"VAR CHECK\" in a TV-style lower third, the referee holds a hand to his ear,\n757\t  the crowd hums, beeps play. Then the decision: on a penalty with a \"soft\" foul (severity under 0.8), it is\n758\t  overturned with 50% chance (the referee draws a TV rectangle with both hands: \"NO PENALTY\"). Otherwise\n759\t  \"PENALTY STANDS\" or \"GOAL STANDS\". The clock stops during VAR. Events: `var`, `varDecision`.\n760\t\n761\t### 6.11 Set pieces and restarts\n762\t\n763\tEach restart is a `SetPiece` controller with the steps setup (place the players, 0.6–1.2 s) → aim (a human taker\n764\tgets up to 6 s, then auto) → take → play. The match mode is `setpiece` while it runs.\n765\t\n766\t- **Kickoff:** the kicking side's two forwards stand in the centre circle, everyone else in their own half; the\n767\t  opponents stay out of the circle until the ball is played (the kit's `kickHold`, 2.5 s). The whistle, then ✕ passes.\n768\t- **Goal kick** (the ball over the goal line, last touched by the attackers): the keeper places it at the edge of the\n769\t  goal area; opponents leave the box. A human side: ✕ short pass (stick picks the target) or ○ long (E.arc toward the\n770\t  stick's direction, 300–420).\n771\t- **Corner** (over the goal line, last touched by the defenders, including keeper tips): the nearest attacker jogs to\n772\t  the corner flag. A human taker moves a ground ring (the target) inside the box with the stick for up to 4 s, then\n773\t  presses ○ or ✕ to cross it there (E.arc with apex 55, curling in- or out-swinging by the stick's side at release), or\n774\t  □ for a short corner pass to the nearest teammate. Attackers run to the near post, the far post, the penalty spot and\n775\t  the edge of the box (for a volley). Defenders mark goal-side. When the ball is in the air the human gets the\n776\t  attacker nearest the ring (auto-switch), and the air-ball prompt shows (§6.5).\n777\t- **Free kick** (a foul outside the box): within 320 of goal it can be shot. A wall of 2 defenders stands 40 from the\n778\t  ball and jumps (`z` +10 for 0.35 s) when the shot is taken. The human aims a reticle across the goal frame (the stick\n779\t  moves it in y and z), holds □ for power and releases, then curls with the stick (aftertouch). ✕ passes and ○ lobs\n780\t  instead. Farther out: pass, lob or shoot as in open play.\n781\t- **Penalty:** the taker stands at the spot and the keeper on his line. The taker aims a cursor over 6 zones (top or\n782\t  bottom × left, centre or right) and holds □ for power: below 0.2 aimed centre is a **Panenka** (a slow chip down the\n783\t  middle); 0.2–0.9 places it; above 0.9 is a blast with a 25% chance of going over. A human keeper picks a dive\n784\t  direction with the stick and presses ✕ at or just before the kick: diving early (more than 0.25 s before) shows it,\n785\t  and the CPU taker may change sides. A CPU keeper guesses with weights from difficulty and the taker's habit. Shots\n786\t  are saved, hit the post, go over or score by the keeper rules (§6.8) with the dive committed.\n787\t- **Crowd throw-back** (instead of throw-ins): a ball that flies over the touchline boards into the stands is thrown\n788\t  back by a fan (an arc from the front row) to the nearest player of the side that did not kick it out. The banner:\n789\t  \"INTO THE CROWD!\" Emit `crowdThrow`.\n790\t\n791\t### 6.12 Match flow, clock, extra time, shootouts\n792\t\n793\t- **The clock:** `EF.T.halfLength` (Settings: 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00 real time per half; 2:00 by default) maps to\n794\t  45 game minutes. The score bug shows game minutes (`37'`). The clock runs in `play` and `setpiece`, and stops for\n795\t  goals, celebrations, replays, VAR, cards and half time.\n796\t- **Stoppage time:** add 1 game minute for every 12 real-time seconds the clock was stopped in the half (goals,\n797\t  celebrations, replays, VAR, cards, knockdowns over 1.5 s), at least 1 and at most 5. At 44' the\n798\t  fourth official holds up his LED board (\"+3\") on the south apron, with a HUD notice. The half ends at 45 + stoppage,\n799\t  at the first moment the ball is not in a dangerous attack (not in either final third), or 15 s of game time later at\n800\t  most.\n801\t- **Half time:** a 4 s overlay: the score, two big stats (shots, possession), a commentary pair. The sides swap\n802\t  ends. The second half's kickoff goes to the side that did not kick off the first.\n803\t- **Full time:** the three-blast whistle and the results (§6.23). In a **cup tie** a draw goes to **golden-goal extra\n804\t  time** (60 real seconds, shown as 91'–105'), then to a **penalty shootout**. In Kick-About: Settings → Draws: Allowed\n805\t  (the default) / Golden goal / Penalties.\n806\t- **Shootout:** 5 kicks each, alternating, then sudden death. It ends early when one side cannot be caught. The HUD\n807\t  shows a row of ✓/✗ dots per side. Takers go through the roster in order (keepers last). The camera sits behind the\n808\t  taker. The crowd's tension music: a heartbeat under a held chord (§6.22).\n809\t\n810\t### 6.13 Team AI, tactics and difficulty\n811\t\n812\t**TeamBrain** (one per side), each step:\n813\t\n814\t1. **Phase:** `attack` when the side has the ball, `defend` when the other side has it, `transition` for 1 s after a\n815\t   change, `loose` when nobody has it (the 2 nearest chase it).\n816\t2. **Formation spots** (registry `formation`). Each role has `base [u, v]`, `att [du, dv]`, `def [du, dv]`,\n817\t   `pull [ku, kv]` and `uRange`. `u` runs from the side's own goal line (0) to the opponent's (1); `v` runs across the\n818\t   pitch from the north touchline (0) to the south (1). Spot = `base + (phase is attack ? att : def) + pull ⊙ (ballUV\n819\t   − [.5, .5])`, with `u` clamped to `uRange`. Tactics then shift it: defenders' `u += (line − .5) · .2`;\n820\t   `v = .5 + (v − .5) · width`. Convert to world x, y by the side's direction.\n821\t3. **Pressing:** the nearest `pressers` (1, or 2 for high-press teams) go at the carrier when he is within the press\n822\t   zone (`u_ball > 1 − press`, in the defending side's frame). They tackle when within reach with probability\n823\t   `aggression × 3` per second (a poke), or slide when he is going past within 30 (`aggression × .8` per second;\n824\t   `temper` adds from-behind attempts). The others mark the opponent nearest their spot, standing 35% of the way from\n825\t   him toward the ball (covering the lane).\n826\t4. **The ball carrier** decides every `EF.T.aiReaction` seconds (0.25, scaled by difficulty) by utility:\n827\t   - `shoot = clamp(1 − d/shootRange, 0, 1) × openAngle × (1 − .3·blockers) × (europhoria ? 1.5 : 1) × shootBias`;\n828\t   - `pass(t) = laneClear(t) × openness(t) × (.4 + .6·progress(t)) × (short ? shortBias : 1) × (1 − risk(t)·(1 − passRisk))`,\n829\t     where `laneClear` comes from the distance of opponents to the pass segment (the kit's `segDist`);\n830\t   - `through`, `lob`/cross (wide in the final third with teammates in the box, `× longBall`), `dribble`\n831\t     (`space ahead / 80 × dribble`), `skill` (a defender in front: `skill × stat`), `dive` (in the box with a defender\n832\t     close: `dive × temper`);\n833\t   - pick the best, plus noise with σ = `(1 − EF.T.aiAccuracy) × .3`. A CPU **shot** holds `shoot` until its chosen\n834\t     power, as the kit's `brain()` does.\n835\t5. **Runs:** when a teammate has the ball in midfield, the forward farthest from the ball runs in behind if the space\n836\t   is there; after a one-two pass the passer runs on; attackers attack crosses (§6.11).\n837\t6. **Keeper:** §6.8.\n838\t7. **Euphoria use:** the CPU triggers Europhoria when full and in the attacking half, or as the team's gimmick says.\n839\t\n840\t**Difficulty** (Settings → Game → Difficulty):\n841\t\n842\t| | Easy | Normal | Hard | Europhoric |\n843\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n844\t| `aiReaction` (s) | .38 | .25 | .16 | .10 |\n845\t| `aiAccuracy` | .60 | .80 | .90 | .97 |\n846\t| `aiAggression` | .30 | .50 | .70 | .85 |\n847\t| CPU keeper reaction (s) | .26 | .19 | .15 | .12 |\n848\t| CPU Euphoria gain | ×.8 | ×1 | ×1.15 | ×1.3 |\n849\t\n850\t**Tactic profiles** (registry `tactic`): numbers `press, pressers, line, width, tempo, passRisk, shortBias, longBall,\n851\tdribble, skill, shootRange, shootBias, foul, dive, euphoriaUse` and a `gimmick` id. The gimmicks:\n852\t\n853\t- `routeone` (Hoofington): the keeper always kicks long; 60% of their passes are lobs toward the striker; their\n854\t  defenders head every high ball away.\n855\t- `keepball` (Pasapasa): short passes, ×2 preference for a pass back when pressed; they keep the ball rather than\n856\t  shoot until the pass chain reaches 4.\n857\t- `gegenpress` (Stahlpresse): for 3 s after losing the ball, 3 players swarm the carrier; high line; tempo 1.\n858\t- `catenaccio` (Lucchetto): line .15, 3 defenders; counterattacks with long passes; fouls (`foul .6`); dives\n859\t  (`dive .5`); **the bus**: when leading after 60', a team bus (a solid 18 deep and 60 wide (y), 30 high, a `map.solid`\n860\t  of the `team-bus` shape) drives on in front of their goal, covering the middle 60% of the mouth. Shots must go round\n861\t  it, be chipped over it (under the 36 bar), or be a super strike, which smashes it (the windows break, the bus drives\n862\t  off, Euphoria +10). The commentary goes wild: \"They've LITERALLY parked the bus!\"\n863\t- `galacticos` (Opulence): dribble .7 and skill .8; Euphoria gain ×1.3 (\"they hand out clappers\"). Their captain's\n864\t  **Golden Moment**: at 80', if they are behind or level, Europhoria triggers by itself.\n865\t\n866\t### 6.14 Camera\n867\t\n868\t- **Broadcast view** (`'broadcast'`, pitch 40°). The scene sets `camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.8], start: 1.25 }`. At 1.25\n869\t  on a 16:9 screen (427×240 game pixels) it shows about 340 units of the pitch's length and 300 of its width. The\n870\t  player can zoom with the wheel, `-` and `=`, and Settings.\n871\t- **The director** (`game.focus` every update; not `follow`): focus = the ball + 0.3 s of its velocity, pulled 25%\n872\t  toward the human's controlled player. It is smoothed by `cam.smooth` (.15) and kept in `cam.bounds`. Its height is\n873\t  `ball.z × .4`, so lofted balls stay framed.\n874\t- **Context zoom** (eased with `game.setZoom` through a tween): set pieces 1.4 on the taker, then 1.25; corners frame\n875\t  the box (`cam.frame`, zoom .9–1.25); a super strike 1.4 on the shooter, then follow; goals 1.5 on the scorer for the\n876\t  celebration; the shootout 1.5 behind the taker.\n877\t- **Cinematics:** `game.timeScale` slow motion (0.3) for super strikes, bicycle kicks and Save Duels; hit-stop\n878\t  (`game.freeze`) for big tackles and Screamers; shake (`game.shake`) for woodwork, the hammer super and fireworks;\n879\t  flashes (`game.flash`) for goals and Europhoria. All of them already respect the comfort settings.\n880\t- **Alternative cameras** (Settings → Game → Camera): Broadcast (default), Classic (`'threequarter'`), Aerial\n881\t  (`'topdown'`). The scene's `views` lists all three; `V` cycles them in dev builds. Every view must look right\n882\t  (§11.7).\n883\t- **Replay cameras:** `game.rotateView(±45)` around the action, and a low \"pitchside\" custom view (pitch 20°).\n884\t\n885\t### 6.15 Action replay\n886\t\n887\t- **Recorder:** a ring buffer of the last 8 s at 60 Hz (every other step) of the ball (x, y, z, roll, super path\n888\t  state), each footballer, the referee and any event actor: x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, state, action, actionU, pose,\n889\t  expr, tilt, downW, mocap clip id and time, glow. It also records sound cues: each `touch`, `shot`, `woodwork` and\n890\t  `goal` event with its time.\n891\t- **Player:** on `goal` (when Settings → Replays is On), after the celebration it plays from 4.5 s before the goal to\n892\t  0.8 s after, at 0.5× speed, from a turned camera (rotate ±45°, zoom 1.4, tracking the ball). The rigs are driven\n893\t  from the recorded states through `rig.update` (gait comes from velocity). A \"REPLAY\" tag, scanlines (an overlay),\n894\t  and the recorded sounds replayed at 0.5× pitch. A commentary line (\"Let's see that again…\"). ✕, Enter or a click\n895\t  skips it. The jumbotron in the Euphorium shows \"REPLAY\" too.\n896\t- Replays are skipped in hub sessions (§6.28). The attract mode uses them (§6.29).\n897\t\n898\t### 6.16 HUD (10-foot)\n899\t\n900\tDrawn in `r.overlay` in game pixels, anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`. It keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a\n901\t5% safe margin (TVs overscan).\n902\t\n903\t- **Score bug** (top left): the two crests (12 px), the 3-letter codes, the score in large type, the clock\n904\t  (`37'`, `45+2'`; \"ET\", \"PENS\"), each team's Euphoria gauge (3 segments), and a red card icon per player sent off.\n905\t- **Name tags:** a triangle in the player's colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) over each human-controlled footballer, with the\n906\t  name (font scale 1) and a stamina bar that shows only below 60. CPU-only matches (attract) show the ball carrier's\n907\t  name.\n908\t- **Power meter** over the shooter: the fill, the gold sweet spot, a pulse at full.\n909\t- **Reticles:** the corner ring, the free-kick reticle across the goal, the penalty cursor, the mouse aim reticle.\n910\t- **Radar** (top right, under the corner area; Settings → Radar): the pitch at 1/9 scale, team dots in kit colours\n911\t  plus a shape per side (circle home, square away, so colour is not the only cue), the ball in white, humans with a\n912\t  ring.\n913\t- **Notices** in the centre (`E.font.title`, a scale-4 gradient): KICK OFF, GOAL!, HALF TIME, FULL TIME, ADVANTAGE!,\n914\t  YELLOW CARD (with the player's name), RED CARD, VAR CHECK, SIMULATION!, INTO THE CROWD!, EUROPHORIA!, the super's\n915\t  name, PERFECT / GOOD / MISS.\n916\t- **Commentary box** (bottom centre): an `E.Dialog` radio box (`modal: false, auto`), 2 lines, with Barry's or Trev's\n917\t  live portrait.\n918\t- **Prompts:** §2.3.\n919\t- **Save Duel ring:** around the keeper in world space (an `r.queue` emissive ring), with the glyph.\n920\t- **Off-screen arrows** at the screen's edges for the ball and for human-controlled players.\n921\t\n922\t### 6.17 Commentary\n923\t\n924\t- **Commentators:** BARRY BELLOW (play-by-play: excitable, shouty, puns) and TREV BRICKLEY (co-commentator, an\n925\t  ex-centre-half: deadpan, dry, practical). Each is a portrait rig (a Humanoid with a headset) and a babble voice.\n926\t- **Director:** it listens to events. Each event type maps to a line pool (registry `lines`). A pool entry is\n927\t  `{ who, text, reply?, when? }`: `when` is a condition on the match (score state, minute, side, streaks, weather,\n928\t  stadium); `reply` is the partner's answer, said straight after. Rules:\n929\t  - priorities: goal 100, super 95, saveDuel 90, red card 85, penalty 80, woodwork 70, card 65, VAR 60, dive 55,\n930\t    save 50, near miss 45, bicycle and header goals 45, skill 30, tackle 25, generic 10;\n931\t  - each event type has an 8 s cooldown; at least 3.5 s between lines; a higher priority interrupts a lower one;\n932\t  - no line repeats within a match (keep the used ids);\n933\t  - variables `{$player}`, `{$team}`, `{$opp}`, `{$score}`, `{$minute}`, `{$stadium}`, `{$keeper}`, `{$ref}` through\n934\t    `Dialog`'s `vars`;\n935\t  - idle chatter (weather, the stadium, the cup, banter pairs) when nothing has been said for 12 s.\n936\t- **Display:** the radio box. **Voice:** the babble voice reads the line as gibberish (§6.22.4); Settings → Commentary\n937\t  On/Off (subtitles stay with voices off: Settings → Voices volume).\n938\t- **PA announcer** (the stadium's voice: \"ding-dong\" chime, echoing babble, text at the top of the screen):\n939\t  attendance, goal scorers, substitution-style jokes (\"Would the owner of a minibus with three wheels…\").\n940\t\n941\t### 6.18 Crowd\n942\t\n943\t- **Layout:** the stands from the TileMap tiers. Fans are spaced 6–8 units apart along each tier; each stadium sets a\n944\t  density, so a stadium has 400–1,600 fans. Each end (and part of the long stand) belongs to a side: the home end,\n945\t  the away end (smaller), and a mixed main stand.\n946\t- **Fans:** pixel sprites drawn by code (`r.queue`): 3 frames (idle, arms up, jump) × 4 kinds (plain, scarf, flag,\n947\t  drummer), palette-swapped per side (shirt in the kit colours, skin, hair). The front row of each stand is\n948\t  `E.Humanoid({ style: 'classic', size: .9 })` rigs drawn with `every: 3`, so they cheer, wave and boo with real poses.\n949\t- **Mood** (per side, 0..1, smoothed): it rises with danger (the ball in the final third, shots), spikes on goals,\n950\t  dips on conceding. **States** set the animation: idle bob; tense (they lean in when a shot is coming); **jump**\n951\t  (goal, save, super); despair (hands on heads after a miss); **boo** (thumbs down after dives and cards); **scarf\n952\t  wall** (Euphoria ≥ 67: scarves held up, swaying to the chant); **Mexican wave** (Euphoria ≥ 67 and 2 goals up: a\n953\t  phase sweeping round the stands); **Europhoria** (flares in the front rows: fire, smoke and red light; the tifo,\n954\t  §8.2, unrolls over the side's end: scrolled in over 1 s, held, rolled away at the end).\n955\t- **The crowd throw-back:** §6.11.\n956\t\n957\t### 6.19 Weather, pitch condition, lighting\n958\t\n959\t- **Rain** (`game.weather = { kind: 'rain', amount, wind }`): the floor texture gets a wet sheen and puddles (tag\n960\t  `puddle`: the ball stops and splashes); the surface is \"wet\" (§6.2); slides go 25% farther; players kick up spray.\n961\t- **Snow:** `kind: 'snow'`; snowy floor (the lines cleared and brushed); surface \"snow\"; the **orange ball** is\n962\t  automatic; footprints as fading decals.\n963\t- **Sun:** the hard dry surface; a heat shimmer over the far stand (dithered offset bands); bright light, high ambient.\n964\t- **Fog** (Lucchetto, second half): a custom overlay of dithered layers that thickens with distance from the camera's\n965\t  focus. The radar matters more in fog.\n966\t- **Night and dusk:** `game.lights.enabled = true`, ambient .45 (night) or .6 (dusk). Four floodlight pylons (§8.2) at\n967\t  the corners, each `game.lights.add(x, y, 220, 520, .9, { color: '#fff0d0' })`. Lamp glow on the pylons\n968\t  (emissive). Where WebGPU is available, `game.enableGPU({ map })` adds shadows; it falls back to canvas lighting by\n969\t  itself. Set both ambients so they match (`gpu.ambient`, `lights.ambient`), as the ADVENTURE kit does.\n970\t- **Wind** (the Smokehouse): lofted balls drift `wind × 20` units/s across.\n971\t\n972\t### 6.20 Matchday events\n973\t\n974\tRegistry `event`: `{ stadiums, chance, when: { minute: [a, b], ballLoose, notSetPiece }, start(match), update(match, dt),\n975\tdone(match), line }`. At most one per half; none during set pieces or the last 5 game minutes. Everything they do goes\n976\tthrough `match.rng`, so a seed replays them.\n977\t\n978\t1. **Seagull** (the Smokehouse): a white `E.Blob({ wings: true })` lands on a loose, slow ball. The ball is pinned\n979\t   until a player runs within 10 (the gull flaps away with a squawk). The commentary has fun with it.\n980\t2. **Beach ball** (Pasapasa): a fan throws a big beach ball onto the pitch (a Body of radius 7 with a light, bouncy\n981\t   physics: bounce .9, gravity 200). It deflects the real ball and bodies for 20 s, then the referee pops it.\n982\t3. **Pitch invader** (the Smokehouse: KIPPER KEITH, the club mascot in a giant smoked-fish costume; Stahlpresse: the\n983\t   STEEL STAG). He runs a zig-zag across the pitch with 2 stewards in hi-vis chasing. The ball bounces off him; a\n984\t   human who tackles him gets +10 Euphoria and a sticker (§7.5).\n985\t4. **Floodlight flicker** (night matches): the floodlights stutter and fail for 4 s (ambient .12); the ball and the\n986\t   players' tags glow (emissive). The PA apologises (\"The fish-oil generator…\").\n987\t5. **Flare smoke** (Lucchetto): red smoke from the curva drifts across a band of the pitch for 15 s (an overlay plus\n988\t   particles; cosmetic).\n989\t6. **Drone and fireworks** (the Euphorium): a camera drone flies over (cosmetic); fireworks above the stands at goals\n990\t   and at Europhoria (`particles.explosion` high in the sky, coloured light, a small shake).\n991\t\n992\t### 6.21 Celebrations\n993\t\n994\t- After a goal, the scorer runs toward the nearest corner flag or the side's fans, and 4 celebrations show as glyph\n995\t  prompts (✕ □ ○ △) for 1.2 s. The picked one plays for 2–3 s, and teammates run in to pile on. A CPU scorer, or no\n996\t  pick, plays the player's signature celebration.\n997\t- Registry `celebration` (§8.3): knee slide, backflip, cartwheel, aeroplane, robot dance, shirt over the head (a\n998\t  **yellow card**, as in real football: the referee books him at the restart), corner-flag dance, badge kiss, helicopter\n999\t  (breakdance), the Kipperton **fish slap** (two players mime slapping each other with a kipper: a fish sprite in one"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"d0bafa10-2152-4dc7-a67b-3bbd5bee07a0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:17:58.906Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.7 Defending\n\n- **Standing tackle / poke** (`pass` without the ball): 0.25 s; the toe reaches 9 (`EF.T.tackleReach`). It wins the\n  ball if the ball is within reach and on the near side of the carrier. A miss costs 0.3 s of recovery. If it touches\n  the carrier's body and not the ball, it is a light foul candidate.\n- **Slide tackle** (`shoot` without the ball): a slide at `EF.T.slideSpeed` (190), decaying with `exp(−3·dt)`, over\n  0.45 s. The hitbox is a capsule along the feet (length 12, radius 4). Ball first: the ball shoots off in the slide's\n  direction at 150, and the tackle is fair. Man first: a foul candidate (§6.10), and the victim is **launched**: an OTT\n  cartwheel (0.6 s in the air, `vz` 120, spinning with a tilt about the forward axis, stars) before he hits the ground\n  (state `down`, 0.9–1.4 s). The slider gets up after 0.6 s.\n- **Shoulder barge** (`lob` without the ball): a 0.3 s lunge; its hitbox is a circle of radius 7 at the shoulder. Hit\n  the carrier side-on: if `weight + rng·30 > his weight + rng·30` he stumbles and loses the ball; else you bounce off.\n  From behind it is a foul candidate.\n- **Switching:** `switch` or `through` (without the ball) switches to the teammate nearest the ball; pressing again\n  takes the next nearest. Settings → Game → Switching: **Auto** (switches by itself on a loss of possession and when a\n  pass reaches a teammate), **Assisted** (the default: Auto, but never while you hold sprint), **Manual**. A mouse click\n  on a teammate while defending switches to him.\n- **Knockdowns:** a foul, a heavy barge, a super strike through a body, or a collision at a closing speed over 220\n  knocks the victim down: state `down` for `downT` (0.8–1.4 s), then he gets up (§8.3). Emit `knockdown`. Use\n  `game.hitFx` at the contact point with `power` by severity (it gives hit-stop, shake, a star, sparks and rumble).\n\n### 6.8 Goalkeepers\n\n- **Positioning:** on the bisector of the angle from the ball to the two posts, at distance\n  `clamp(8 + (400 − ballDist) · 0.06, 6, 36)` from the goal line. He shuffles sideways (facing the ball), crouched in\n  the set pose when the ball is within 200. He comes out to **rush** a carrier who is through on goal (within 120, no\n  defender between) and **smothers** at his feet (a low forward dive).\n- **Reading a shot:** on `shot`, predict where the ball crosses the goal line (y, z) and when (`tCross`). After his\n  reaction time (`EF.T.keeperReaction`, 0.18 s, ±40% by the keep stat and difficulty, ×1.3 against Screamers), he\n  moves or dives toward the point. Reach: the dive covers `EF.T.keeperReach` (48) laterally in 0.35 s, plus 12 of arm\n  reach (in z: 0–40 on a high dive).\n- **Outcome** when he gets there: `q` = how well he reached it (0..1), times the shot speed factor (`1 − (speed − 200)/400`,\n  at least .2), times keep/100. If `q > .7` and the speed is under 260, a **catch** (he holds it: state `keeper-hold`).\n  Else if `q > .35`, a **parry** (the ball rebounds at 40–60% speed, away from the goal centre, so rebounds happen) or\n  a **tip** round the post or over the bar (a high ball near the frame becomes a corner). Else a goal.\n- **Distribution:** hold up to 2 s (the human side waits for ✕ throw / □ long kick, then the AI decides). Throw:\n  E.arc to the open teammate nearest the keeper (an underarm roll if he is within 120). Long kick: E.arc 300–450 toward\n  the most advanced teammate (route-one teams always kick long). Opponents must stay 60 away while he holds it.\n- **Animation:** the set stance; side shuffles; the dive (tilt about the forward axis ±70–95°, lifted 2 on a low dive\n  and 14 on a high dive, arms over the head with IK to the ball); the catch (hands to the chest); the parry (`jab`);\n  the tip (one arm up); the get-up; the throw (`OverhandThrow`), §8.3.\n\n### 6.9 Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes, the Save Duel\n\n**Euphoria** is each side's crowd, 0–100, drawn as the \"EUPHORIA\" gauge under the team's name in the score bug, in 3\nsegments.\n\n| Event | Euphoria (× `EF.T.euphoriaGain` and the team's crowd factor) |\n|---|---|\n| a completed pass | +2, +1 more for each pass in an unbroken chain (at most +8 a pass) |\n| a successful skill move | +6 to +12 (§6.6) |\n| a tackle that wins the ball | +6; a slide that wins it cleanly +8 |\n| a shot on target | +5; the woodwork +7; a Screamer +4 more |\n| a save (the keeper's side) | +6; a catch from a Screamer +10 |\n| a goal | +35 to the scorer's side; −10 to the other |\n| a celebration picked in time (§6.21) | +5 to +15 by the celebration |\n| a dive that wins a foul | +5; a dive that gets booked −20 (the crowd boos) |\n| decay | −`EF.T.euphoriaDecay` (1.5) per second when above 0 and not in Europhoria |\n\n- **Thresholds:** 34 (stamina regenerates 25% faster), 67 (shots charge 20% faster; the fans wave their scarves and\n  sing), 100 (**EUROPHORIA READY**: the gauge flashes, the prompt \"L1+R1 EUROPHORIA!\" shows, the tifo is held ready).\n- **Europhoria** (press `euphoria` when full): `EF.T.europhoriaTime` (8 s of game time; it keeps counting through\n  stoppages and slows with slow motion). The\n  side gets speed +12%, free sprinting, a tackle reach of +25%, and the keeper +30% reach. The music's Europhoria layer\n  comes in, the side's fans light flares and unfurl the tifo, the LED boards turn to the team's colours, and the\n  side's players glow faintly (emissive outline). One **Super Strike** is unlocked for the side during Europhoria. The\n  gauge drains to 0 over the duration. Emit `europhoria`.\n- **Super Strike:** during Europhoria, any shot charged to `p ≥ 0.9` becomes a super strike. The captain's is his own\n  (registry `super`, §7.1); any other player's is the team super `rocket`. The sequence: 0.6 s of charge-up (the\n  shooter rises 6, the camera zooms to 1.4, time slows to 0.3×, a radial burst, the super's name in big letters), then\n  the strike at `EF.T.superSpeed` (520) along its path. The keeper cannot save it normally:\n  - **Save Duel** (the defending side has a human): a timing ring shrinks around the keeper (1.0 s, at real speed even\n    though the game is in slow motion: count it in unscaled time, `dt / game.timeScale`, so tests stay exact) toward a\n    target circle, with the glyph of `pass` (✕). Press within ±60 ms of\n    the target for **PERFECT** (a catch: Euphoria +15 for the defenders, the crowd erupts). Within ±140 ms gives\n    **GOOD** (a parry: the ball spins away). Otherwise **MISS** (a goal: the keeper and the ball go into the net\n    together, OTT). Several human defenders: the one controlling the player nearest the keeper takes the duel.\n  - CPU keeper against a human's super: save chance Easy 15%, Normal 30%, Hard 45%, Europhoric 55%. The outcome is\n    shown with the same animations.\n- Events: `euphoriaGain`, `euphoriaFull`, `europhoria`, `superStrike`, `saveDuel`, `saveDuelResult`.\n\n### 6.10 The referee, fouls, advantage, cards, theatrics, VAR\n\n- **The referee** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, a whistle sprite). He follows play 60–90 from the ball,\n  stays out of passing lanes, and is a Body the ball can hit (he falls over comically: `down` and an \"OOOH\"). He has a\n  personality (registry `referee`): `strictness` (0.6–1.4), `gullibility` (how often he buys dives, 0.2–0.7),\n  `varHappy` (0–1), `voice`.\n- **Foul judgement:** on a tackle, slide or barge contact with a body before the ball (or with no ball near), compute\n  `severity = closingSpeed/150 × (fromBehind ? 1.5 : 1) × (late ? 1.4 : 1) × (slide ? 1.2 : 1)`. `fromBehind`: the\n  tackler is more than 120° from the victim's facing. `late`: the victim had passed more than 0.4 s earlier. It is a\n  foul if `k = severity × strictness × EF.T.foulStrictness` is over 0.5. Cards on the same `k`: a yellow above 1.3, a\n  straight red above 2.4, and a second yellow is a red. Settings → Game → Cards: Off (fouls, no cards) / Normal /\n  Strict (`k` ×1.3).\n- **Advantage:** if the fouled side still has the ball 0.8 s after the foul, show \"ADVANTAGE!\" (the referee's arms\n  forward) and play on. Any card waits for the next stoppage (\"the referee will come back to that\").\n- **Restart:** a direct free kick where the foul happened; a penalty if a defender fouls inside his own box. The\n  referee's whistle, the jog over, the card (he raises it high: §8.3), the player's protest (`Angry` or `Shrug` clip).\n  The crowd boos the card.\n- **Theatrics (`dive`):** the player flops theatrically (§8.3). The referee judges:\n  - if an opponent touched him (any contact within the last 0.5 s), or an opponent is within 8 and closing: it is a\n    foul with chance `gullibility × (1.2 − d/14)` (at least .1), else play on;\n  - if no opponent is within 14 and there was no contact in 0.5 s: **SIMULATION!**, a yellow card for the diver, the\n    crowd boos, Euphoria −20.\n\n  The diver is down for 1.2 s either way. AC Lucchetto's AI dives in the box on purpose.\n- **VAR:** checks every penalty award, and goals scored within 3 s of an unpunished foul in the build-up (with\n  `varHappy` chance). The sequence (2.5 s): \"VAR CHECK\" in a TV-style lower third, the referee holds a hand to his ear,\n  the crowd hums, beeps play. Then the decision: on a penalty with a \"soft\" foul (severity under 0.8), it is\n  overturned with 50% chance (the referee draws a TV rectangle with both hands: \"NO PENALTY\"). Otherwise\n  \"PENALTY STANDS\" or \"GOAL STANDS\". The clock stops during VAR. Events: `var`, `varDecision`.\n\n### 6.11 Set pieces and restarts\n\nEach restart is a `SetPiece` controller with the steps setup (place the players, 0.6–1.2 s) → aim (a human taker\ngets up to 6 s, then auto) → take → play. The match mode is `setpiece` while it runs.\n\n- **Kickoff:** the kicking side's two forwards stand in the centre circle, everyone else in their own half; the\n  opponents stay out of the circle until the ball is played (the kit's `kickHold`, 2.5 s). The whistle, then ✕ passes.\n- **Goal kick** (the ball over the goal line, last touched by the attackers): the keeper places it at the edge of the\n  goal area; opponents leave the box. A human side: ✕ short pass (stick picks the target) or ○ long (E.arc toward the\n  stick's direction, 300–420).\n- **Corner** (over the goal line, last touched by the defenders, including keeper tips): the nearest attacker jogs to\n  the corner flag. A human taker moves a ground ring (the target) inside the box with the stick for up to 4 s, then\n  presses ○ or ✕ to cross it there (E.arc with apex 55, curling in- or out-swinging by the stick's side at release), or\n  □ for a short corner pass to the nearest teammate. Attackers run to the near post, the far post, the penalty spot and\n  the edge of the box (for a volley). Defenders mark goal-side. When the ball is in the air the human gets the\n  attacker nearest the ring (auto-switch), and the air-ball prompt shows (§6.5).\n- **Free kick** (a foul outside the box): within 320 of goal it can be shot. A wall of 2 defenders stands 40 from the\n  ball and jumps (`z` +10 for 0.35 s) when the shot is taken. The human aims a reticle across the goal frame (the stick\n  moves it in y and z), holds □ for power and releases, then curls with the stick (aftertouch). ✕ passes and ○ lobs\n  instead. Farther out: pass, lob or shoot as in open play.\n- **Penalty:** the taker stands at the spot and the keeper on his line. The taker aims a cursor over 6 zones (top or\n  bottom × left, centre or right) and holds □ for power: below 0.2 aimed centre is a **Panenka** (a slow chip down the\n  middle); 0.2–0.9 places it; above 0.9 is a blast with a 25% chance of going over. A human keeper picks a dive\n  direction with the stick and presses ✕ at or just before the kick: diving early (more than 0.25 s before) shows it,\n  and the CPU taker may change sides. A CPU keeper guesses with weights from difficulty and the taker's habit. Shots\n  are saved, hit the post, go over or score by the keeper rules (§6.8) with the dive committed.\n- **Crowd throw-back** (instead of throw-ins): a ball that flies over the touchline boards into the stands is thrown\n  back by a fan (an arc from the front row) to the nearest player of the side that did not kick it out. The banner:\n  \"INTO THE CROWD!\" Emit `crowdThrow`.\n\n### 6.12 Match flow, clock, extra time, shootouts\n\n- **The clock:** `EF.T.halfLength` (Settings: 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00 real time per half; 2:00 by default) maps to\n  45 game minutes. The score bug shows game minutes (`37'`). The clock runs in `play` and `setpiece`, and stops for\n  goals, celebrations, replays, VAR, cards and half time.\n- **Stoppage time:** add 1 game minute for every 12 real-time seconds the clock was stopped in the half (goals,\n  celebrations, replays, VAR, cards, knockdowns over 1.5 s), at least 1 and at most 5. At 44' the\n  fourth official holds up his LED board (\"+3\") on the south apron, with a HUD notice. The half ends at 45 + stoppage,\n  at the first moment the ball is not in a dangerous attack (not in either final third), or 15 s of game time later at\n  most.\n- **Half time:** a 4 s overlay: the score, two big stats (shots, possession), a commentary pair. The sides swap\n  ends. The second half's kickoff goes to the side that did not kick off the first.\n- **Full time:** the three-blast whistle and the results (§6.23). In a **cup tie** a draw goes to **golden-goal extra\n  time** (60 real seconds, shown as 91'–105'), then to a **penalty shootout**. In Kick-About: Settings → Draws: Allowed\n  (the default) / Golden goal / Penalties.\n- **Shootout:** 5 kicks each, alternating, then sudden death. It ends early when one side cannot be caught. The HUD\n  shows a row of ✓/✗ dots per side. Takers go through the roster in order (keepers last). The camera sits behind the\n  taker. The crowd's tension music: a heartbeat under a held chord (§6.22).\n\n### 6.13 Team AI, tactics and difficulty\n\n**TeamBrain** (one per side), each step:\n\n1. **Phase:** `attack` when the side has the ball, `defend` when the other side has it, `transition` for 1 s after a\n   change, `loose` when nobody has it (the 2 nearest chase it).\n2. **Formation spots** (registry `formation`). Each role has `base [u, v]`, `att [du, dv]`, `def [du, dv]`,\n   `pull [ku, kv]` and `uRange`. `u` runs from the side's own goal line (0) to the opponent's (1); `v` runs across the\n   pitch from the north touchline (0) to the south (1). Spot = `base + (phase is attack ? att : def) + pull ⊙ (ballUV\n   − [.5, .5])`, with `u` clamped to `uRange`. Tactics then shift it: defenders' `u += (line − .5) · .2`;\n   `v = .5 + (v − .5) · width`. Convert to world x, y by the side's direction.\n3. **Pressing:** the nearest `pressers` (1, or 2 for high-press teams) go at the carrier when he is within the press\n   zone (`u_ball > 1 − press`, in the defending side's frame). They tackle when within reach with probability\n   `aggression × 3` per second (a poke), or slide when he is going past within 30 (`aggression × .8` per second;\n   `temper` adds from-behind attempts). The others mark the opponent nearest their spot, standing 35% of the way from\n   him toward the ball (covering the lane).\n4. **The ball carrier** decides every `EF.T.aiReaction` seconds (0.25, scaled by difficulty) by utility:\n   - `shoot = clamp(1 − d/shootRange, 0, 1) × openAngle × (1 − .3·blockers) × (europhoria ? 1.5 : 1) × shootBias`;\n   - `pass(t) = laneClear(t) × openness(t) × (.4 + .6·progress(t)) × (short ? shortBias : 1) × (1 − risk(t)·(1 − passRisk))`,\n     where `laneClear` comes from the distance of opponents to the pass segment (the kit's `segDist`);\n   - `through`, `lob`/cross (wide in the final third with teammates in the box, `× longBall`), `dribble`\n     (`space ahead / 80 × dribble`), `skill` (a defender in front: `skill × stat`), `dive` (in the box with a defender\n     close: `dive × temper`);\n   - pick the best, plus noise with σ = `(1 − EF.T.aiAccuracy) × .3`. A CPU **shot** holds `shoot` until its chosen\n     power, as the kit's `brain()` does.\n5. **Runs:** when a teammate has the ball in midfield, the forward farthest from the ball runs in behind if the space\n   is there; after a one-two pass the passer runs on; attackers attack crosses (§6.11).\n6. **Keeper:** §6.8.\n7. **Euphoria use:** the CPU triggers Europhoria when full and in the attacking half, or as the team's gimmick says.\n\n**Difficulty** (Settings → Game → Difficulty):\n\n| | Easy | Normal | Hard | Europhoric |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `aiReaction` (s) | .38 | .25 | .16 | .10 |\n| `aiAccuracy` | .60 | .80 | .90 | .97 |\n| `aiAggression` | .30 | .50 | .70 | .85 |\n| CPU keeper reaction (s) | .26 | .19 | .15 | .12 |\n| CPU Euphoria gain | ×.8 | ×1 | ×1.15 | ×1.3 |\n\n**Tactic profiles** (registry `tactic`): numbers `press, pressers, line, width, tempo, passRisk, shortBias, longBall,\ndribble, skill, shootRange, shootBias, foul, dive, euphoriaUse` and a `gimmick` id. The gimmicks:\n\n- `routeone` (Hoofington): the keeper always kicks long; 60% of their passes are lobs toward the striker; their\n  defenders head every high ball away.\n- `keepball` (Pasapasa): short passes, ×2 preference for a pass back when pressed; they keep the ball rather than\n  shoot until the pass chain reaches 4.\n- `gegenpress` (Stahlpresse): for 3 s after losing the ball, 3 players swarm the carrier; high line; tempo 1.\n- `catenaccio` (Lucchetto): line .15, 3 defenders; counterattacks with long passes; fouls (`foul .6`); dives\n  (`dive .5`); **the bus**: when leading after 60', a team bus (a solid 18 deep and 60 wide (y), 30 high, a `map.solid`\n  of the `team-bus` shape) drives on in front of their goal, covering the middle 60% of the mouth. Shots must go round\n  it, be chipped over it (under the 36 bar), or be a super strike, which smashes it (the windows break, the bus drives\n  off, Euphoria +10). The commentary goes wild: \"They've LITERALLY parked the bus!\"\n- `galacticos` (Opulence): dribble .7 and skill .8; Euphoria gain ×1.3 (\"they hand out clappers\"). Their captain's\n  **Golden Moment**: at 80', if they are behind or level, Europhoria triggers by itself.\n\n### 6.14 Camera\n\n- **Broadcast view** (`'broadcast'`, pitch 40°). The scene sets `camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.8], start: 1.25 }`. At 1.25\n  on a 16:9 screen (427×240 game pixels) it shows about 340 units of the pitch's length and 300 of its width. The\n  player can zoom with the wheel, `-` and `=`, and Settings.\n- **The director** (`game.focus` every update; not `follow`): focus = the ball + 0.3 s of its velocity, pulled 25%\n  toward the human's controlled player. It is smoothed by `cam.smooth` (.15) and kept in `cam.bounds`. Its height is\n  `ball.z × .4`, so lofted balls stay framed.\n- **Context zoom** (eased with `game.setZoom` through a tween): set pieces 1.4 on the taker, then 1.25; corners frame\n  the box (`cam.frame`, zoom .9–1.25); a super strike 1.4 on the shooter, then follow; goals 1.5 on the scorer for the\n  celebration; the shootout 1.5 behind the taker.\n- **Cinematics:** `game.timeScale` slow motion (0.3) for super strikes, bicycle kicks and Save Duels; hit-stop\n  (`game.freeze`) for big tackles and Screamers; shake (`game.shake`) for woodwork, the hammer super and fireworks;\n  flashes (`game.flash`) for goals and Europhoria. All of them already respect the comfort settings.\n- **Alternative cameras** (Settings → Game → Camera): Broadcast (default), Classic (`'threequarter'`), Aerial\n  (`'topdown'`). The scene's `views` lists all three; `V` cycles them in dev builds. Every view must look right\n  (§11.7).\n- **Replay cameras:** `game.rotateView(±45)` around the action, and a low \"pitchside\" custom view (pitch 20°).\n\n### 6.15 Action replay\n\n- **Recorder:** a ring buffer of the last 8 s at 60 Hz (every other step) of the ball (x, y, z, roll, super path\n  state), each footballer, the referee and any event actor: x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, state, action, actionU, pose,\n  expr, tilt, downW, mocap clip id and time, glow. It also records sound cues: each `touch`, `shot`, `woodwork` and\n  `goal` event with its time.\n- **Player:** on `goal` (when Settings → Replays is On), after the celebration it plays from 4.5 s before the goal to\n  0.8 s after, at 0.5× speed, from a turned camera (rotate ±45°, zoom 1.4, tracking the ball). The rigs are driven\n  from the recorded states through `rig.update` (gait comes from velocity). A \"REPLAY\" tag, scanlines (an overlay),\n  and the recorded sounds replayed at 0.5× pitch. A commentary line (\"Let's see that again…\"). ✕, Enter or a click\n  skips it. The jumbotron in the Euphorium shows \"REPLAY\" too.\n- Replays are skipped in hub sessions (§6.28). The attract mode uses them (§6.29).\n\n### 6.16 HUD (10-foot)\n\nDrawn in `r.overlay` in game pixels, anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`. It keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a\n5% safe margin (TVs overscan).\n\n- **Score bug** (top left): the two crests (12 px), the 3-letter codes, the score in large type, the clock\n  (`37'`, `45+2'`; \"ET\", \"PENS\"), each team's Euphoria gauge (3 segments), and a red card icon per player sent off.\n- **Name tags:** a triangle in the player's colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) over each human-controlled footballer, with the\n  name (font scale 1) and a stamina bar that shows only below 60. CPU-only matches (attract) show the ball carrier's\n  name.\n- **Power meter** over the shooter: the fill, the gold sweet spot, a pulse at full.\n- **Reticles:** the corner ring, the free-kick reticle across the goal, the penalty cursor, the mouse aim reticle.\n- **Radar** (top right, under the corner area; Settings → Radar): the pitch at 1/9 scale, team dots in kit colours\n  plus a shape per side (circle home, square away, so colour is not the only cue), the ball in white, humans with a\n  ring.\n- **Notices** in the centre (`E.font.title`, a scale-4 gradient): KICK OFF, GOAL!, HALF TIME, FULL TIME, ADVANTAGE!,\n  YELLOW CARD (with the player's name), RED CARD, VAR CHECK, SIMULATION!, INTO THE CROWD!, EUROPHORIA!, the super's\n  name, PERFECT / GOOD / MISS.\n- **Commentary box** (bottom centre): an `E.Dialog` radio box (`modal: false, auto`), 2 lines, with Barry's or Trev's\n  live portrait.\n- **Prompts:** §2.3.\n- **Save Duel ring:** around the keeper in world space (an `r.queue` emissive ring), with the glyph.\n- **Off-screen arrows** at the screen's edges for the ball and for human-controlled players.\n\n### 6.17 Commentary\n\n- **Commentators:** BARRY BELLOW (play-by-play: excitable, shouty, puns) and TREV BRICKLEY (co-commentator, an\n  ex-centre-half: deadpan, dry, practical). Each is a portrait rig (a Humanoid with a headset) and a babble voice.\n- **Director:** it listens to events. Each event type maps to a line pool (registry `lines`). A pool entry is\n  `{ who, text, reply?, when? }`: `when` is a condition on the match (score state, minute, side, streaks, weather,\n  stadium); `reply` is the partner's answer, said straight after. Rules:\n  - priorities: goal 100, super 95, saveDuel 90, red card 85, penalty 80, woodwork 70, card 65, VAR 60, dive 55,\n    save 50, near miss 45, bicycle and header goals 45, skill 30, tackle 25, generic 10;\n  - each event type has an 8 s cooldown; at least 3.5 s between lines; a higher priority interrupts a lower one;\n  - no line repeats within a match (keep the used ids);\n  - variables `{$player}`, `{$team}`, `{$opp}`, `{$score}`, `{$minute}`, `{$stadium}`, `{$keeper}`, `{$ref}` through\n    `Dialog`'s `vars`;\n  - idle chatter (weather, the stadium, the cup, banter pairs) when nothing has been said for 12 s.\n- **Display:** the radio box. **Voice:** the babble voice reads the line as gibberish (§6.22.4); Settings → Commentary\n  On/Off (subtitles stay with voices off: Settings → Voices volume).\n- **PA announcer** (the stadium's voice: \"ding-dong\" chime, echoing babble, text at the top of the screen):\n  attendance, goal scorers, substitution-style jokes (\"Would the owner of a minibus with three wheels…\").\n\n### 6.18 Crowd\n\n- **Layout:** the stands from the TileMap tiers. Fans are spaced 6–8 units apart along each tier; each stadium sets a\n  density, so a stadium has 400–1,600 fans. Each end (and part of the long stand) belongs to a side: the home end,\n  the away end (smaller), and a mixed main stand.\n- **Fans:** pixel sprites drawn by code (`r.queue`): 3 frames (idle, arms up, jump) × 4 kinds (plain, scarf, flag,\n  drummer), palette-swapped per side (shirt in the kit colours, skin, hair). The front row of each stand is\n  `E.Humanoid({ style: 'classic', size: .9 })` rigs drawn with `every: 3`, so they cheer, wave and boo with real poses.\n- **Mood** (per side, 0..1, smoothed): it rises with danger (the ball in the final third, shots), spikes on goals,\n  dips on conceding. **States** set the animation: idle bob; tense (they lean in when a shot is coming); **jump**\n  (goal, save, super); despair (hands on heads after a miss); **boo** (thumbs down after dives and cards); **scarf\n  wall** (Euphoria ≥ 67: scarves held up, swaying to the chant); **Mexican wave** (Euphoria ≥ 67 and 2 goals up: a\n  phase sweeping round the stands); **Europhoria** (flares in the front rows: fire, smoke and red light; the tifo,\n  §8.2, unrolls over the side's end: scrolled in over 1 s, held, rolled away at the end).\n- **The crowd throw-back:** §6.11.\n\n### 6.19 Weather, pitch condition, lighting\n\n- **Rain** (`game.weather = { kind: 'rain', amount, wind }`): the floor texture gets a wet sheen and puddles (tag\n  `puddle`: the ball stops and splashes); the surface is \"wet\" (§6.2); slides go 25% farther; players kick up spray.\n- **Snow:** `kind: 'snow'`; snowy floor (the lines cleared and brushed); surface \"snow\"; the **orange ball** is\n  automatic; footprints as fading decals.\n- **Sun:** the hard dry surface; a heat shimmer over the far stand (dithered offset bands); bright light, high ambient.\n- **Fog** (Lucchetto, second half): a custom overlay of dithered layers that thickens with distance from the camera's\n  focus. The radar matters more in fog.\n- **Night and dusk:** `game.lights.enabled = true`, ambient .45 (night) or .6 (dusk). Four floodlight pylons (§8.2) at\n  the corners, each `game.lights.add(x, y, 220, 520, .9, { color: '#fff0d0' })`. Lamp glow on the pylons\n  (emissive). Where WebGPU is available, `game.enableGPU({ map })` adds shadows; it falls back to canvas lighting by\n  itself. Set both ambients so they match (`gpu.ambient`, `lights.ambient`), as the ADVENTURE kit does.\n- **Wind** (the Smokehouse): lofted balls drift `wind × 20` units/s across.\n\n### 6.20 Matchday events\n\nRegistry `event`: `{ stadiums, chance, when: { minute: [a, b], ballLoose, notSetPiece }, start(match), update(match, dt),\ndone(match), line }`. At most one per half; none during set pieces or the last 5 game minutes. Everything they do goes\nthrough `match.rng`, so a seed replays them.\n\n1. **Seagull** (the Smokehouse): a white `E.Blob({ wings: true })` lands on a loose, slow ball. The ball is pinned\n   until a player runs within 10 (the gull flaps away with a squawk). The commentary has fun with it.\n2. **Beach ball** (Pasapasa): a fan throws a big beach ball onto the pitch (a Body of radius 7 with a light, bouncy\n   physics: bounce .9, gravity 200). It deflects the real ball and bodies for 20 s, then the referee pops it.\n3. **Pitch invader** (the Smokehouse: KIPPER KEITH, the club mascot in a giant smoked-fish costume; Stahlpresse: the\n   STEEL STAG). He runs a zig-zag across the pitch with 2 stewards in hi-vis chasing. The ball bounces off him; a\n   human who tackles him gets +10 Euphoria and a sticker (§7.5).\n4. **Floodlight flicker** (night matches): the floodlights stutter and fail for 4 s (ambient .12); the ball and the\n   players' tags glow (emissive). The PA apologises (\"The fish-oil generator…\").\n5. **Flare smoke** (Lucchetto): red smoke from the curva drifts across a band of the pitch for 15 s (an overlay plus\n   particles; cosmetic).\n6. **Drone and fireworks** (the Euphorium): a camera drone flies over (cosmetic); fireworks above the stands at goals\n   and at Europhoria (`particles.explosion` high in the sky, coloured light, a small shake).\n\n### 6.21 Celebrations\n\n- After a goal, the scorer runs toward the nearest corner flag or the side's fans, and 4 celebrations show as glyph\n  prompts (✕ □ ○ △) for 1.2 s. The picked one plays for 2–3 s, and teammates run in to pile on. A CPU scorer, or no\n  pick, plays the player's signature celebration.\n- Registry `celebration` (§8.3): knee slide, backflip, cartwheel, aeroplane, robot dance, shirt over the head (a\n  **yellow card**, as in real football: the referee books him at the restart), corner-flag dance, badge kiss, helicopter\n  (breakdance), the Kipperton **fish slap** (two players mime slapping each other with a kipper: a fish sprite in one","numLines":350,"startLine":650,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KKmKkGHvTC2XHURWNdvnxd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2ozzSBpvAd4DRXZMBX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q8vxRoWcNqYPVGBmngpKqj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1000,"limit":350},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12940,"cache_read_input_tokens":46703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12940},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"beac4021-2d5f-4545-bc14-d26cc82d2844","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:02.581Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2ozhpkGZ3eJ5LQsVnD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Q8vxRoWcNqYPVGBmngpKqj":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1000,"limit":350}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8vxRoWcNqYPVGBmngpKqj","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\t  hand). Euphoria +5 to +15 each; the shirt-over-head gives +15 and a yellow.\n1001\t\n1002\t### 6.22 Audio (all in code)\n1003\t\n1004\t#### 6.22.1 Music (the engine's song format, original compositions)\n1005\t\n1006\t| Song id | Where | Character |\n1007\t|---|---|---|\n1008\t| `anthem` | title, tunnel walkout, trophy ceremony | the EUROPHORIA ANTHEM: a grand cup-competition anthem in its own melody (Appendix D) |\n1009\t| `menu` | menus, setup, album | an upbeat 128 bpm loop on the anthem's chords |\n1010\t| `travel` | the travel map | a jaunty road-trip tune (whistled lead: sine with vibrato) |\n1011\t| `tabloid` | tabloid screens | a press-room stinger and a short loop (typewriter ticks in the drums) |\n1012\t| `dressing` | team talks | a warm low loop |\n1013\t| `europhoria` | in the match, as a layer | drums, brass stabs and bass, faded in by `audio.layer` during Europhoria; otherwise matches have no music, only the crowd |\n1014\t| `halftime` | the half-time overlay | a light jazzy jingle |\n1015\t| `goal` | `audio.sting('goal', { at: 'bar' })` | a 2-bar fanfare |\n1016\t| `tension` | shootouts, the Save Duel | a held chord and a heartbeat (the kick drum at 60 bpm) |\n1017\t| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare; a sad trombone (saw with vibrato, falling) |\n1018\t| `villain` | Baron von Bullion's scenes | a minor, oily waltz |\n1019\t| `ceremony` | the trophy lift | the anthem, full and fast |\n1020\t| `credits` | credits, the album | the anthem as a music box (triangle and sine) |\n1021\t| `training` | training | a laid-back loop |\n1022\t| `attract` | attract mode | the anthem's high-energy remix |\n1023\t\n1024\t#### 6.22.2 Sound effects\n1025\t\n1026\tDefine them with `audio.define(name, voice)` (the engine's voices: wave, freq, to, dur, vol, filter, arp, vib). The\n1027\tlist: touch, pass, shot, screamer (a thump and a rising noise whoosh), super charge (rising arp) and release (boom\n1028\tplus sizzle), bounce by surface (a grass thump, a wet splash, a snow crunch), woodwork \"DOINK\" (triangle 1400 → 1100\n1029\twith a ring), net swish (highpass noise, 0.3 s), catch (a slap), parry (punch), whistle (short, long, two blasts at\n1030\thalf time, three at full time), card (a snap), slide (a grass rip), knockdown thud, skill swish, nutmeg ding,\n1031\tEuphoria segment chime, Europhoria chord stab, Save Duel ticks and the result (perfect ding / miss buzz), VAR beeps,\n1032\tthe PA chime, a seagull squawk (sine with bends), the beach ball boing, floodlight power-down (a falling saw buzz),\n1033\tthe bus horn, fireworks (`explode`), menu move, select and back (the engine's `select`, `confirm`, `cancel`), the\n1034\tsticker shimmer, heartbeat. Rumble (`game.input.rumble`) on shots (by power), tackles, the woodwork, goals and the Save\n1035\tDuel.\n1036\t\n1037\t#### 6.22.3 The crowd engine (`EF.crowdAudio`, WebAudio through the `crowd` bus, §5.4)\n1038\t\n1039\t- **Bed:** 3 looping noise sources through bandpass filters (300 Hz Q .7, 900 Hz Q 1, 2500 Hz Q 1.2) into gains. The\n1040\t  level = `size × (.25 + .75 × excitement)`. Excitement follows the crowd mood (§6.18), smoothed over 0.3 s up and\n1041\t  1.5 s down.\n1042\t- **Reactions:** an \"OOOH\" (noise through 2 formant bandpasses sweeping from F1 400 / F2 800 to F1 600 / F2 1000 over\n1043\t  0.8 s) on near misses and the woodwork; a **roar** (the bed to full, plus a brighter band, 3 s) on goals; **boos**\n1044\t  (a low \"oo\" formant, the pitch falling) on dives and cards; whistles from fans (high sine chirps) at fouls; **claps**\n1045\t  (noise bursts) in rhythm with chants.\n1046\t- **Chants** (`EF.Chant`, registry `chant`): a choir of 8 voices per side. Each voice is a sawtooth plus a pulse,\n1047\t  detuned ±12 cents, through 2 bandpass formants per syllable vowel (a: 800/1200, e: 500/1800, i: 300/2300, o:\n1048\t  500/900, u: 350/700). Syllables follow a melody in the engine's note syntax, with claps and drums. Each team has a\n1049\t  chant (§7.8). Triggers: the scarf wall (Euphoria ≥ 67), after goals, at kickoffs. The **OLÉ** chant rises on each\n1050\t  pass of a chain from 5 passes on (one \"OLÉ!\" per pass).\n1051\t- Headless: every call is a no-op (no audio context). The crowd bus volume follows Settings → Crowd.\n1052\t\n1053\t#### 6.22.4 Babble voices (`EF.babble`, Animalese/Simlish-style)\n1054\t\n1055\t- Each character of a line, as `Dialog` reveals it (§5.1), makes a 50–70 ms syllable:\n1056\t  - **source:** a sawtooth (bright voices) or pulse (nasal voices) at `f0 × letterPitch × contour`. `letterPitch` is a\n1057\t    fixed table per letter (±15%). The contour rises toward a `?`, falls toward a `.`, and is louder and higher on\n1058\t    `!` and on capitals;\n1059\t  - **formants:** 2 bandpass filters at the vowel's formants. A consonant uses the next vowel's formants plus a 10–15\n1060\t    ms noise burst: highpass 3–5 kHz for s, z, f, sh; a click (bandpass 2 kHz, 5 ms) for t, k, p, b, d;\n1061\t  - **envelope:** attack 5 ms, hold, release 30 ms;\n1062\t  - **pauses:** a space is 30 ms of silence, `,` 120 ms, `.` `!` `?` 220 ms.\n1063\t- **Speaker profiles** (registry on the speaker's data): `{ f0, wave, formantShift, rate, breath (a noise mix), vibrato, echo }`.\n1064\t  Barry: f0 160, saw, rate 1.1, bright. Trev: f0 95, pulse, rate .85, dull (formants ×.9). Mags: f0 215, saw, breath\n1065\t  .25 (raspy). The referee: f0 135, short. The PA: f0 120 with an echo (a 180 ms delay, feedback .35). Players: f0\n1066\t  110–260 by character. Baron von Bullion: f0 80, vibrato (6 Hz, 3%). Each voice routes through the `voices` bus.\n1067\t- Only one voice speaks at once (the commentary queue makes sure); celebrations get short shouts (\"Yeesh!\", \"Wahey!\")\n1068\t  as babble.\n1069\t\n1070\t### 6.23 The 10-foot UI kit and the screens\n1071\t\n1072\t**UI kit (`30-ui.js`):** a screen stack (`UI.push(screen)`, `UI.pop()`), widgets with focus:\n1073\t\n1074\t- **Tile** (a big card with an icon or portrait, a title at scale 2, a line of text), **Button**, **List** (at most 6\n1075\t  rows visible), **Slider** (left/right change it, held repeat with acceleration; mouse drag), **Toggle**, **Choice**\n1076\t  (left/right cycles), **Tabs** (L1/R1, Q/E, or click), **Pager** (the album and About pages).\n1077\t- **Navigation:** d-pad, left stick (past half way, repeated with `input.repeat`), arrows and WASD. ✕ / Enter / Space /\n1078\t  a click picks. ○ / Esc / Backspace / a right click goes back. Hovering the mouse moves the focus; the focus ring\n1079\t  follows the pointer only while it moves. Spatial navigation: the nearest widget in the pressed direction.\n1080\t- **Style:** `E.ui.box` gradient panels (paper `#0d1430` to `#16224a`, a gold `#ffc83a` focus border with a 2-px glow\n1081\t  and a gentle pulse), `E.font.title` for headings, `E.font.text` with a drop shadow for body text. **Type sizes:**\n1082\t  menu items at scale 2 at least; body text at scale 1 of the 5×7 font at least (never the `'tiny'` font for anything a\n1083\t  player must read); titles at scale 3–4. Each screen has one main action, at most 6 choices in view, and a prompt\n1084\t  footer with glyphs.\n1085\t- **Sounds:** move, select and back blips; focus changes give a light rumble (.1, 30 ms) on pads.\n1086\t\n1087\t**Screens:**\n1088\t\n1089\t- **Title** (`title`): the logo \"EUROPHORIA FOOTBALL\" (`E.font.title` scale 4, a gold gradient, depth 3), the subtitle\n1090\t  \"OVER-THE-TOP ARCADE FOOTBALL\", the Euphorium at night behind it (stands, crowd, floodlights, a slow pan), Daz\n1091\t  Pilchard doing keepy-uppies in front, fireworks every 8 s. \"PRESS START\" blinks with the right glyph. Then the main\n1092\t  menu, as 7 tiles: CUP RUN (with \"CONTINUE: QUARTER-FINAL\" when a save exists), KICK-ABOUT, PENALTIES, TRAINING,\n1093\t  STICKER ALBUM, OPTIONS, ABOUT & CREDITS. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game's version) sits in a\n1094\t  bottom corner. On touch-only devices, the notice panel (§2.5).\n1095\t- **Kick-About setup** (`setup`): 4 steps, one per screen: TEAMS (home and away carousels of big crest tiles; a kit\n1096\t  toggle), STADIUM (5 tiles with a painted thumbnail), CONDITIONS (weather: As the stadium / Sun / Rain / Snow / Fog;\n1097\t  time: Day / Dusk / Night; ball style; half length; difficulty), PLAYERS (the controller side picker, §6.27). Then\n1098\t  START MATCH.\n1099\t- **Penalties setup** (`penaltysetup`): two teams, then the side picker.\n1100\t- **Results** (`results`): the scoreline huge, up to 4 scorer lines with minutes, Player of the Match (portrait and\n1101\t  name), 3 big stats (shots, possession %, tackles), stickers earned, then CONTINUE.\n1102\t- **Sticker Album** (`album`): a page per team (2 × 3 big stickers: a live portrait, the name, the position); special\n1103\t  pages (stadiums, characters, shinies). Unearned stickers are silhouettes with \"?\". L1/R1 turns pages with a flip\n1104\t  tween.\n1105\t- **About & Credits** (`about`): paged (L1/R1): Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback\n1106\t  (all from `EF.ABOUT`, §3.3), then Credits (engine, mocap libraries and their licences, the AI Hub client, the model).\n1107\t  Large type, one block per page.\n1108\t- **Pause:** the engine's standard pause menu (themed), with our items Restart match and Dev mode.\n1109\t\n1110\t### 6.24 The Cup Run (campaign) flow\n1111\t\n1112\t- **The bracket screen** (`cup`): the Kippers' path as 5 big stacked cards (QUALIFYING ROUND, ROUND OF 16,\n1113\t  QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, FINAL), each with the opponent's crest, the stadium, and the result once played. The\n1114\t  current card is focused, and a bus icon moves along the path. NEW CUP RUN / CONTINUE.\n1115\t- **The beat player** runs a beat's steps (registry `beat`, §7.3) in order:\n1116\t  - `tabloid`: a newspaper page (THE DAILY ROAR masthead, the headline at `E.font.title` scale 3, black on newsprint,\n1117\t    a \"photo\" (a live rig posed in a box, desaturated), a subhead and 2 lines of body). The paper drops in spinning\n1118\t    (an old-film spin tween), with a typewriter tick.\n1119\t  - `travel`: a stylised map of a fictional Europe (pixel coastlines drawn from a polygon list), with the minibus \"The\n1120\t    Old Trout\" driving a dotted route to the next city.\n1121\t  - `talk`: dialogue with portraits (`E.Dialog`, modal, babble voices), possibly with choices (`choices`, `onChoice`)\n1122\t    that set flags.\n1123\t  - `teamtalk`: 3 big cards (§7.3): HAIRDRYER, ARM ROUND THE SHOULDER, TACTICS BOARD (which then asks for a formation:\n1124\t    2-2 / 1-2-1 / 2-1-1). Extra local players can join here.\n1125\t  - `challenge`: the Gaffer's Challenge card for this match (an optional objective).\n1126\t  - `tunnel`: the walkout (below).\n1127\t  - `match`: plays the match with the round's options.\n1128\t  - `result`: the bracket advances; the tabloid for a win or a loss; stickers; the autosave.\n1129\t- **Losing** a round: the \"KNOCKED OUT!\" tabloid, then CONTINUE? with a 10 s countdown (arcade style; ✕ retries the\n1130\t  round from its team talk, ○ returns to the title).\n1131\t- **Tunnel walkout** (`tunnel`): both teams line up in the tunnel, then walk out onto the pitch in two lines with the\n1132\t  referee. The anthem plays. The handshake line: each player passes the other line, arm out. Captains and the referee\n1133\t  at the centre circle, then the coin toss (a sprite flip). This scene also works as the AI Hub card (§6.28).\n1134\t- **Ending** (`ending`): the trophy ceremony (a podium on the pitch, the Europhoria Cup (§8.2) lifted by Daz with all\n1135\t  the Kippers jumping, confetti and fireworks, the anthem), then the parade (Kipperton harbour by day: the team on top\n1136\t  of a fishing trawler on wheels driving along the harbour road, the crowd on both sides throwing scarves, gulls), then\n1137\t  the closing tabloid, then the credits roll (names scrolling over the parade, the About credits).\n1138\t\n1139\t### 6.25 Training\n1140\t\n1141\tScene `training`: a list of 9 drills (§7.6), each with a completion tick. The coach (Mags, then Sandra for\n1142\tdefending) explains each step in a short modal dialog, then the drill runs on the training ground with a goal and\n1143\tcounters on the HUD (\"PASSES 3/5\"). Success: a fanfare and the next step. A drill's last step completes it (saved).\n1144\tDummies are footballers driven by `ScriptController`s (static, slow-walking, or attacking).\n1145\t\n1146\t### 6.26 Penalties mode\n1147\t\n1148\tA shootout from the start (`match { shootoutOnly: true }`) between two picked teams in a picked stadium. 1 player\n1149\t(against the CPU) or 2 (versus): each human takes his side's kicks and keeps goal for his side. Best of 5, then sudden\n1150\tdeath. Results as §6.23.\n1151\t\n1152\t### 6.27 Local multiplayer\n1153\t\n1154\t- 1–4 players: each joined input (`game.players`) picks a side on the PLAYERS screen: a big row of controller icons,\n1155\t  each in its player's colour, moved left (HOME), centre (CPU, which means sitting out) or right (AWAY), then ✕ for\n1156\t  ready. At least one human must be on a side. Co-op (humans on the same side) and versus both work.\n1157\t- Each human controls one footballer at a time and switches on his own. Two humans on a side never hold the same\n1158\t  footballer: switching skips held ones. Each human has his own prompts (their device) and colour tag.\n1159\t- One shared screen: the broadcast camera follows the ball. When humans are far apart, it widens toward them\n1160\t  (`cam.frame` with a zoom range of .9–1.25).\n1161\t- The pause shows who paused (the engine does: \"P2 PAUSED\").\n1162\t\n1163\t### 6.28 Online: AI Hub sessions (shared-world)\n1164\t\n1165\tRead the protocol (github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub `lib/hub/README.md`) whole before building this. The flow:\n1166\t\n1167\t1. `session.js` is the first script (§3.3). `AIHub.active` is true from the first line in a session. Then the game\n1168\t   creates `E.Game` with `corner: false` and `menu: { quit: false }`, skips the title and the attract mode, and every\n1169\t   scene has `pausable: false`.\n1170\t2. Boot goes to scene `hubwait` (\"CONNECTING…\" over the stadium backdrop) and runs\n1171\t   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`. With `null`, go to the title\n1172\t   and run as a normal game.\n1173\t3. **Set up from the shared seed** (the same on every copy): `const R = AIHub.rng('setup')`: the two teams (from the 6),\n1174\t   the stadium (from the 5), its weather. Sides: players in seat order alternate HOME (ids at even positions in\n1175\t   `info.players`) and AWAY. With 3 players, the side with 1 human gets the **underdog boost**: Euphoria gain ×1.5.\n1176\t   Each human controls one footballer of his side. The half length fits the round:\n1177\t   `min(90, (info.limitMs/1000 − 50)/2)` seconds, and at least 45.\n1178\t4. **The card:** scene `tunnel` in card mode: the two teams in the tunnel, the hub players' names in their seat\n1179\t   colours (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) with ✓ for those in `card.ready`; \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the\n1180\t   other side before the final whistle\"; this device's controls (glyph prompts); the time left from `card.left`\n1181\t   (\"PAUSED\" when `card.paused`); \"READY ✕/Enter\" and \"MORE TIME △/T\" buttons (also tapped or clicked). Enter, ✕ or a\n1182\t   click on Ready calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △, T or a click on More time calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (again to\n1183\t   take it back). Nothing on the card changes the round; it has no menus. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the match is built,\n1184\t   with no key press.\n1185\t5. **Start:** on `start`, go to `match` in session mode. A 3-2-1 countdown follows `AIHub.time()` (negative); play\n1186\t   begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n1187\t6. **Host** (`AIHub.isHost`): runs the sim. Remote humans' footballers use `RemoteController`s fed by their input\n1188\t   messages (Appendix B: stick, held bits, cumulative press counters so a lost packet never loses a press; neutral\n1189\t   after 500 ms without input). It sends a snapshot 14 times a second (unreliable, under 1,100 bytes) and coalesced\n1190\t   events at most 5 times a second (reliable). That keeps it at 19 messages a second or fewer, under the limit of 20.\n1191\t7. **Client:** sends its Intent 15 times a second (unreliable) and rare reliable messages (the Save Duel press with its\n1192\t   `AIHub.time()`, the celebration pick). It renders 100 ms behind the newest snapshot, interpolating positions (and\n1193\t   extrapolating up to 150 ms when snapshots are late). It runs rig animation, crowd, audio and commentary locally from\n1194\t   the snapshot state and the host's events. The client's own player is drawn where the host says (no prediction).\n1195\t   Instead, every button press gives instant local feedback: the glyph flashes, a kick sound, rumble.\n1196\t8. **Save Duel online:** the host sends `duel` with its start time. The defending client shows the ring on the same\n1197\t   timeline and sends its press time. The host resolves when the press arrives, or 300 ms after the window closes\n1198\t   (a miss).\n1199\t9. **Server mode** (`AIHub.server`, the host has no player of its own): run the host code with no local player, no\n1200\t   camera and no input; draw nothing.\n1201\t10. **Leaving:** on `leave`, that player's footballer goes back to the CPU. The round goes on (the hub voids it only if\n1202\t    the host leaves).\n1203\t11. **Time-up:** on `time-up`, the host calls `finish` at once with the current score.\n1204\t12. **Finish** (the host, once; at full time or on time-up):\n1205\t    `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`. `standings`: the winning side's players (still in the round)\n1206\t    tied first, the other side's second; a draw is one group with everyone. `scores`: each player's side's goals.\n1207\t    `stats`: per player `{ Goals, Shots, Tackles }`. `awards`: `[{ id, title: 'Player of the Match', detail }]` for the\n1208\t    human with the best match rating. Before it, send a last reliable snapshot with `over: 1`, so every copy shows the\n1209\t    same final score.\n1210\t13. **End:** on `end` (any reason), stop taking input, stop sending, stop all sound (music, the crowd engine, voices),\n1211\t    and show \"FULL TIME\" with the score, or \"ROUND VOID\" for `void` or `host-left`, \"YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT\" for\n1212\t    `sat-out`. The hub draws its results over it.\n1213\t14. **Rules:** no other network access; no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`/`window.open`; no names typed by players (names\n1214\t    come from `info.players` and are drawn with `E.font`, never inserted as HTML); Options while Create (button 8) is\n1215\t    held is the hub's, so ignore it. In a session, Options (or Esc) alone opens **our own** canvas overlay, SESSION\n1216\t    SETTINGS (volume, music, effects, voices, crowd, button symbols; built with `EF.UI`), not the engine's menu, so\n1217\t    nothing pauses: the match goes on, on the host above all, and the player's footballer goes to the CPU while the\n1218\t    overlay is open. Dev mode, the attract mode, saves and the cup do not exist in sessions. A draw at full time\n1219\t    stands in a session (no extra time or shootout), so a round fits its minutes.\n1220\t\n1221\t### 6.29 Attract mode\n1222\t\n1223\t- **The idle watcher** runs on `title` and every front-end and cup menu screen (not in matches, training or story\n1224\t  dialogs). Any input resets it: a key, a mouse move of more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, a touch, a pad button, or a\n1225\t  stick past the dead zone. After **10.0 s** without input it goes to `attract`. In tests: `game.advance(9.9)` leaves\n1226\t  the title showing; `game.advance(0.2)` more starts the attract mode.\n1227\t- **The attract scene** is a director script (`game.script`) over a real AI-versus-AI match that **cheats freely**: it\n1228\t  places players and the ball, sets the Euphoria, forces outcomes (the save fails, the volley goes in), and turns on\n1229\t  everyone's infinite stamina. Segments, about 90 s per loop:\n1230\t  1. **MATCHDAY LIVE** (30 s): a random stadium (it cycles through all 5 over loops). The captain is given the ball 230\n1231\t     from goal with the gauge full: Europhoria, the super strike, the Save Duel (it fails), the goal, a celebration,\n1232\t     the replay.\n1233\t  2. **SET-PIECE SPECIAL** (15 s): a corner, then a bicycle kick goal (forced).\n1234\t  3. **THE DARK ARTS** (15 s): Lucchetto: a dive in the box, the penalty, VAR CHECK, \"PENALTY STANDS\", the goal; then a\n1235\t     Simulation booking.\n1236\t  4. **SHOOTOUT** (15 s): 3 kicks a side, including a Panenka.\n1237\t  5. **WEATHER REPORT** (10 s): 2.5 s cuts: rain at the Smokehouse, the snow and the orange ball, fog and flares,\n1238\t     fireworks in the Euphorium.\n1239\t  6. **TITLE CARD** (5 s): the logo, \"PRESS START\", the cup records (fastest cup win, biggest win).\n1240\t- A banner \"DEMO · PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (with the right glyph) stays at the bottom. Commentary and the crowd play as in a\n1241\t  match.\n1242\t- **Any input** (the watcher's list) goes straight back to `title`, with the focus on the first tile. The press that\n1243\t  exits is swallowed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it does not also pick a menu item.\n1244\t- On touch-only devices it runs the same way; a tap goes back to the title.\n1245\t\n1246\t### 6.30 Dev mode\n1247\t\n1248\t- **Reach it:** the pause menu's \"Dev mode\" item, the backquote key (`` ` ``) or F1 in any scene (call\n1249\t  `preventDefault()` on F1's keydown, or Chrome opens its help page), or `?dev=1`. It is never available in AI Hub\n1250\t  sessions. Opening it from the pause menu resumes the game (`game.resume()`) and opens the panel over the running\n1251\t  scene. The panel takes the input while it is open; the match keeps running behind it, with every human's footballer\n1252\t  handed to the CPU, so slider changes can be watched live. A **Freeze** toggle stops the sim instead.\n1253\t- **The panel:** a canvas drawer on the right 40% of the screen, translucent (`E.ui.box` with alpha .9), 4 tabs (L1/R1,\n1254\t  Q/E, or click): TUNE, CHEATS, WARP, INFO. Rows are navigated with the d-pad or stick; left/right changes a value\n1255\t  (holding speeds it up); ✕ toggles or runs; ○, Esc or F1 closes. The mouse hovers, clicks and drags sliders.\n1256\t  - **TUNE:** every `EF.T` slider (Appendix A), grouped (Movement, Ball, Passing & Shooting, Keepers, Defending &\n1257\t    Rules, Euphoria, AI, Match). Each shows its value, its default and a ↺ when changed. At the top: **RESET ALL TO\n1258\t    DEFAULTS**; on each row, □ resets that one. Changes apply at once and are kept in `E.store('ef:tuning')`, so they\n1259\t    survive a reload until reset. A dev-panel badge shows on the HUD while any value differs from its default.\n1260\t  - **CHEATS:** infinite stamina (per side), Euphoria always full (per side), invincible keeper (per side), the CPU\n1261\t    controls everyone (watch mode), \"pure football\" (no Euphoria, supers or events), freeze the clock, a goal for home\n1262\t    / away, set the clock to 44' / 89', slow motion (0.25×) and step one frame (while frozen), show hitboxes and\n1263\t    contact capsules, show the AI (formation spots, roles, the pass lanes it scores, its decision text over the\n1264\t    carrier), show the ball's predicted path and the air-ball window, show `rig.debug` skeletons, mute the crowd.\n1265\t  - **WARP:** go to any scene and part: every deep link (§4.4), each cup round's pre-match beat, half time, extra time,\n1266\t    a shootout, the results, the ending, the album, about; trigger now: a corner, a free kick, a penalty, a matchday\n1267\t    event (pick one), a super strike, a Save Duel, a foul with a yellow or a red, a dive, VAR, a celebration (pick\n1268\t    one), a replay; unlock everything (the cup's rounds, stickers, balls); reset the save. Two galleries: ANIMATION\n1269\t    (every move of §8.3 on a loop, on a chosen rig, in every view, at 1×, 0.25× or frame by frame; deep link\n1270\t    `#dev/anim/<move>`) and SOUND TEST (every SFX, song, chant and voice, with sliders for the speaker profiles).\n1271\t  - **INFO:** the version and build, the seed, the scene and mode, `game.debug.snapshot()` pretty-printed, counts\n1272\t    (bodies, particles, fans, lights, rigs drawn), the frame time (`game.stats`), the hub role when relevant.\n1273\t- Dev mode never changes a save unless WARP's unlock or reset is used (it asks first, with its own confirm row).\n1274\t\n1275\t### 6.31 Saves, settings, unlocks, stickers\n1276\t\n1277\t- **Saves:** `game.saves` with `write = () => ({ data: EF.Save.data(), place: roundName, level: roundIndex })` and `read`.\n1278\t  It autosaves after each cup match and at the start of each round. CUP RUN → CONTINUE loads `saves.latest()`. Data\n1279\t  (versioned, with `migrate`): `{ v: 1, cup: { round, results: [{ opp, score, pens }], flags: { loyal } , teamTalks },\n1280\t  stickers: { id: true | 'shiny' }, unlocks: { balls: [] }, records: { fastestCup, biggestWin }, drills: { id: true } }`.\n1281\t- **Our settings** (`EF.SETTINGS` in `new E.Game({ menu: { settings } })`; group Game unless noted): difficulty (Easy /\n1282\t  Normal / Hard / Europhoric), half length (1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), pass assist (Off / Low / High), shot assist\n1283\t  (On / Off), switching (Auto / Assisted / Manual), cards (Off / Normal / Strict), draws in Kick-About (Allowed / Golden\n1284\t  goal / Penalties), prompts (Always / While learning / Off), commentary (On / Off), replays (On / Off), camera\n1285\t  (Broadcast / Classic / Aerial), radar (On / Off); group Sound: Voices (slider .8), Crowd (slider .8); group\n1286\t  Controller: Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox, §2.3). The engine supplies the rest (volume, music, effects, reduce\n1287\t  motion, shake, flashes, screen filter, zoom, rebinding).\n1288\t- **Unlocks** (\"items\"): balls for Kick-About: Classic (white panels), Winter Orange (automatic in snow), The Golden\n1289\t  Ball (win the cup), Old Leather (finish all 5 Gaffer's Challenges). Matches have no pickups: football stays\n1290\t  football.\n1291\t- **Stickers:** §7.5. Earning one shows a toast with the sticker sliding in (sound: shimmer).\n1292\t\n1293\t### 6.32 About and credits\n1294\t\n1295\tThe About pages render `EF.ABOUT` (§3.3) in this order: Source Information (every field TASK.md lists: Date, Source,\n1296\tPlan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model,\n1297\tUsage), Testing Feedback (4 answers), Engine Feedback (6 answers), Prompt Feedback (4 answers), then the credits.\n1298\t\"unknown\" stays \"unknown\". The test suite checks that every field is present and non-empty (§11.3).\n1299\t\n1300\t### 6.33 Touch-only detection\n1301\t\n1302\t`EF.touchOnly()` is true when `?touchonly=1` is set, or when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches` and not\n1303\t`matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad is connected (`navigator.getGamepads()`). It becomes false\n1304\tfor the rest of the visit on the first `keydown` or `gamepadconnected`. While it is true: the title shows the notice\n1305\tand the SETTINGS button; menus still answer taps (to reach settings and about); play cannot start (the tiles show\n1306\t\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" when tapped); the attract mode runs.\n1307\t\n1308\t---\n1309\t\n1310\t## 7. Content\n1311\t\n1312\tIn a football game the usual content words map like this. **Levels** are the 5 cup rounds, each in its own stadium\n1313\twith its own weather and events (§7.2), plus the training ground. **Enemies** are the 5 opposing clubs, each with its\n1314\town tactics and gimmick; the final's Olympique Opulence is the boss team, with a boss keeper and a boss captain\n1315\t(§7.1). The referees are the neutral hazard. **Items** are the unlockable balls, the stickers and the team-talk buffs;\n1316\tthere are no pickups in matches (§6.31). **Story beats** are in §7.3.\n1317\t\n1318\tTone everywhere: British football broadcasting and tabloid back pages, turned up. That means puns (fish puns for the\n1319\tKippers), commentary clichés, deadpan replies, affectionate and never mean. National stereotypes are off-limits: the\n1320\topponents' jokes come from their **football philosophies**, their food, weather and stadiums. All names are original;\n1321\tnone is a real club, player or person. Text is ASCII except the accented letters §5.5 adds.\n1322\t\n1323\t### 7.1 Teams\n1324\t\n1325\tEach team: name, short code, nickname, city, stadium, kits (home, away, keeper), crest, formation, tactic, chant,\n1326\tsignature celebration, 5 players (number, name, position, build, size, hair, skin, hair colour, stats, captain's super).\n1327\tKit colours give rig colours: `cloth` (shirt), `pants` (shorts), `boot`, `belt` (= shorts), `trim` (socks and collar),\n1328\t`glove` (keepers), plus `kit: { pattern, color2, number, numberColor }` (§5.2).\n1329\t\n1330\t**KIPPERTON ATHLETIC** — \"The Kippers\", KIP. A fishing town on the cold north coast. Home: the Smokehouse. Kit: tangerine\n1331\t`#f08a24` and navy `#1c2a5a` hoops, navy shorts, tangerine socks; away: white with a tangerine sash. Crest: a navy shield\n1332\twith a smoked kipper crossed over an anchor. Formation 2-1-1 (the team talk can change it). Tactic `plucky` (balanced:\n1333\tpress .55, line .45, tempo .7, passRisk .5). Chant \"KIP-PER-TON!\". Celebration: the fish slap. Manager: MAGS MULLIGAN\n1334\t(a fishmonger turned manager: flat cap, scarf, a voice like a foghorn).\n1335\t\n1336\t| # | Name | Pos | Build / size / hair | Key stats | Notes |\n1337\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1338\t| 1 | WALLY CRABB | GK | bulky 1.2, bald | keep 76, weight 80 | 41, a part-time lighthouse keeper; huge gloves |\n1339\t| 4 | SANDRA \"THE HARBOUR WALL\" OKAFOR | DEF | bulky 1.2, short | tackle 88, weight 95, temper 40 | barges like a trawler |\n1340\t| 6 | AGGIE NOWAK | MID | heroic 1.12, ponytail | pass 90, skill 70 | the brains; Polish grandmother in the stands |\n1341\t| 7 | TOMMY \"TWINKLETOES\" TRAN | FWD | heroic 1.08, spiky | pace 95, skill 92 | step-overs for breakfast |\n1342\t| 9 | DAZ PILCHARD (captain) | FWD | heroic 1.15, short | shoot 90, pace 80 | super **THE SMOKED KIPPER** (path `wobble`, smoke trail, the ball briefly shaped like a fish) |\n1343\t\n1344\t**AFC HOOFINGTON** — \"The Hoofers\", HOO (Qualifying Round). Brown `#6a4a2a` and amber `#e8a830` stripes. Crest: a\n1345\tmuddy boot. Formation 2-2. Tactic `routeone` (longBall .6, press .4, line .4, tempo .5, foul .25). Chant: a\n1346\tfoghorn-low \"HOOOOF!\" on every clearance. Celebration: Cheering_Two_Hands.\n1347\t\n1348\t| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n1349\t|---|---|---|---|"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"1d59e4a1-630d-4405-9afa-a8006fca16e0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:02.726Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":"  hand). Euphoria +5 to +15 each; the shirt-over-head gives +15 and a yellow.\n\n### 6.22 Audio (all in code)\n\n#### 6.22.1 Music (the engine's song format, original compositions)\n\n| Song id | Where | Character |\n|---|---|---|\n| `anthem` | title, tunnel walkout, trophy ceremony | the EUROPHORIA ANTHEM: a grand cup-competition anthem in its own melody (Appendix D) |\n| `menu` | menus, setup, album | an upbeat 128 bpm loop on the anthem's chords |\n| `travel` | the travel map | a jaunty road-trip tune (whistled lead: sine with vibrato) |\n| `tabloid` | tabloid screens | a press-room stinger and a short loop (typewriter ticks in the drums) |\n| `dressing` | team talks | a warm low loop |\n| `europhoria` | in the match, as a layer | drums, brass stabs and bass, faded in by `audio.layer` during Europhoria; otherwise matches have no music, only the crowd |\n| `halftime` | the half-time overlay | a light jazzy jingle |\n| `goal` | `audio.sting('goal', { at: 'bar' })` | a 2-bar fanfare |\n| `tension` | shootouts, the Save Duel | a held chord and a heartbeat (the kick drum at 60 bpm) |\n| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare; a sad trombone (saw with vibrato, falling) |\n| `villain` | Baron von Bullion's scenes | a minor, oily waltz |\n| `ceremony` | the trophy lift | the anthem, full and fast |\n| `credits` | credits, the album | the anthem as a music box (triangle and sine) |\n| `training` | training | a laid-back loop |\n| `attract` | attract mode | the anthem's high-energy remix |\n\n#### 6.22.2 Sound effects\n\nDefine them with `audio.define(name, voice)` (the engine's voices: wave, freq, to, dur, vol, filter, arp, vib). The\nlist: touch, pass, shot, screamer (a thump and a rising noise whoosh), super charge (rising arp) and release (boom\nplus sizzle), bounce by surface (a grass thump, a wet splash, a snow crunch), woodwork \"DOINK\" (triangle 1400 → 1100\nwith a ring), net swish (highpass noise, 0.3 s), catch (a slap), parry (punch), whistle (short, long, two blasts at\nhalf time, three at full time), card (a snap), slide (a grass rip), knockdown thud, skill swish, nutmeg ding,\nEuphoria segment chime, Europhoria chord stab, Save Duel ticks and the result (perfect ding / miss buzz), VAR beeps,\nthe PA chime, a seagull squawk (sine with bends), the beach ball boing, floodlight power-down (a falling saw buzz),\nthe bus horn, fireworks (`explode`), menu move, select and back (the engine's `select`, `confirm`, `cancel`), the\nsticker shimmer, heartbeat. Rumble (`game.input.rumble`) on shots (by power), tackles, the woodwork, goals and the Save\nDuel.\n\n#### 6.22.3 The crowd engine (`EF.crowdAudio`, WebAudio through the `crowd` bus, §5.4)\n\n- **Bed:** 3 looping noise sources through bandpass filters (300 Hz Q .7, 900 Hz Q 1, 2500 Hz Q 1.2) into gains. The\n  level = `size × (.25 + .75 × excitement)`. Excitement follows the crowd mood (§6.18), smoothed over 0.3 s up and\n  1.5 s down.\n- **Reactions:** an \"OOOH\" (noise through 2 formant bandpasses sweeping from F1 400 / F2 800 to F1 600 / F2 1000 over\n  0.8 s) on near misses and the woodwork; a **roar** (the bed to full, plus a brighter band, 3 s) on goals; **boos**\n  (a low \"oo\" formant, the pitch falling) on dives and cards; whistles from fans (high sine chirps) at fouls; **claps**\n  (noise bursts) in rhythm with chants.\n- **Chants** (`EF.Chant`, registry `chant`): a choir of 8 voices per side. Each voice is a sawtooth plus a pulse,\n  detuned ±12 cents, through 2 bandpass formants per syllable vowel (a: 800/1200, e: 500/1800, i: 300/2300, o:\n  500/900, u: 350/700). Syllables follow a melody in the engine's note syntax, with claps and drums. Each team has a\n  chant (§7.8). Triggers: the scarf wall (Euphoria ≥ 67), after goals, at kickoffs. The **OLÉ** chant rises on each\n  pass of a chain from 5 passes on (one \"OLÉ!\" per pass).\n- Headless: every call is a no-op (no audio context). The crowd bus volume follows Settings → Crowd.\n\n#### 6.22.4 Babble voices (`EF.babble`, Animalese/Simlish-style)\n\n- Each character of a line, as `Dialog` reveals it (§5.1), makes a 50–70 ms syllable:\n  - **source:** a sawtooth (bright voices) or pulse (nasal voices) at `f0 × letterPitch × contour`. `letterPitch` is a\n    fixed table per letter (±15%). The contour rises toward a `?`, falls toward a `.`, and is louder and higher on\n    `!` and on capitals;\n  - **formants:** 2 bandpass filters at the vowel's formants. A consonant uses the next vowel's formants plus a 10–15\n    ms noise burst: highpass 3–5 kHz for s, z, f, sh; a click (bandpass 2 kHz, 5 ms) for t, k, p, b, d;\n  - **envelope:** attack 5 ms, hold, release 30 ms;\n  - **pauses:** a space is 30 ms of silence, `,` 120 ms, `.` `!` `?` 220 ms.\n- **Speaker profiles** (registry on the speaker's data): `{ f0, wave, formantShift, rate, breath (a noise mix), vibrato, echo }`.\n  Barry: f0 160, saw, rate 1.1, bright. Trev: f0 95, pulse, rate .85, dull (formants ×.9). Mags: f0 215, saw, breath\n  .25 (raspy). The referee: f0 135, short. The PA: f0 120 with an echo (a 180 ms delay, feedback .35). Players: f0\n  110–260 by character. Baron von Bullion: f0 80, vibrato (6 Hz, 3%). Each voice routes through the `voices` bus.\n- Only one voice speaks at once (the commentary queue makes sure); celebrations get short shouts (\"Yeesh!\", \"Wahey!\")\n  as babble.\n\n### 6.23 The 10-foot UI kit and the screens\n\n**UI kit (`30-ui.js`):** a screen stack (`UI.push(screen)`, `UI.pop()`), widgets with focus:\n\n- **Tile** (a big card with an icon or portrait, a title at scale 2, a line of text), **Button**, **List** (at most 6\n  rows visible), **Slider** (left/right change it, held repeat with acceleration; mouse drag), **Toggle**, **Choice**\n  (left/right cycles), **Tabs** (L1/R1, Q/E, or click), **Pager** (the album and About pages).\n- **Navigation:** d-pad, left stick (past half way, repeated with `input.repeat`), arrows and WASD. ✕ / Enter / Space /\n  a click picks. ○ / Esc / Backspace / a right click goes back. Hovering the mouse moves the focus; the focus ring\n  follows the pointer only while it moves. Spatial navigation: the nearest widget in the pressed direction.\n- **Style:** `E.ui.box` gradient panels (paper `#0d1430` to `#16224a`, a gold `#ffc83a` focus border with a 2-px glow\n  and a gentle pulse), `E.font.title` for headings, `E.font.text` with a drop shadow for body text. **Type sizes:**\n  menu items at scale 2 at least; body text at scale 1 of the 5×7 font at least (never the `'tiny'` font for anything a\n  player must read); titles at scale 3–4. Each screen has one main action, at most 6 choices in view, and a prompt\n  footer with glyphs.\n- **Sounds:** move, select and back blips; focus changes give a light rumble (.1, 30 ms) on pads.\n\n**Screens:**\n\n- **Title** (`title`): the logo \"EUROPHORIA FOOTBALL\" (`E.font.title` scale 4, a gold gradient, depth 3), the subtitle\n  \"OVER-THE-TOP ARCADE FOOTBALL\", the Euphorium at night behind it (stands, crowd, floodlights, a slow pan), Daz\n  Pilchard doing keepy-uppies in front, fireworks every 8 s. \"PRESS START\" blinks with the right glyph. Then the main\n  menu, as 7 tiles: CUP RUN (with \"CONTINUE: QUARTER-FINAL\" when a save exists), KICK-ABOUT, PENALTIES, TRAINING,\n  STICKER ALBUM, OPTIONS, ABOUT & CREDITS. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` plus the game's version) sits in a\n  bottom corner. On touch-only devices, the notice panel (§2.5).\n- **Kick-About setup** (`setup`): 4 steps, one per screen: TEAMS (home and away carousels of big crest tiles; a kit\n  toggle), STADIUM (5 tiles with a painted thumbnail), CONDITIONS (weather: As the stadium / Sun / Rain / Snow / Fog;\n  time: Day / Dusk / Night; ball style; half length; difficulty), PLAYERS (the controller side picker, §6.27). Then\n  START MATCH.\n- **Penalties setup** (`penaltysetup`): two teams, then the side picker.\n- **Results** (`results`): the scoreline huge, up to 4 scorer lines with minutes, Player of the Match (portrait and\n  name), 3 big stats (shots, possession %, tackles), stickers earned, then CONTINUE.\n- **Sticker Album** (`album`): a page per team (2 × 3 big stickers: a live portrait, the name, the position); special\n  pages (stadiums, characters, shinies). Unearned stickers are silhouettes with \"?\". L1/R1 turns pages with a flip\n  tween.\n- **About & Credits** (`about`): paged (L1/R1): Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback\n  (all from `EF.ABOUT`, §3.3), then Credits (engine, mocap libraries and their licences, the AI Hub client, the model).\n  Large type, one block per page.\n- **Pause:** the engine's standard pause menu (themed), with our items Restart match and Dev mode.\n\n### 6.24 The Cup Run (campaign) flow\n\n- **The bracket screen** (`cup`): the Kippers' path as 5 big stacked cards (QUALIFYING ROUND, ROUND OF 16,\n  QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, FINAL), each with the opponent's crest, the stadium, and the result once played. The\n  current card is focused, and a bus icon moves along the path. NEW CUP RUN / CONTINUE.\n- **The beat player** runs a beat's steps (registry `beat`, §7.3) in order:\n  - `tabloid`: a newspaper page (THE DAILY ROAR masthead, the headline at `E.font.title` scale 3, black on newsprint,\n    a \"photo\" (a live rig posed in a box, desaturated), a subhead and 2 lines of body). The paper drops in spinning\n    (an old-film spin tween), with a typewriter tick.\n  - `travel`: a stylised map of a fictional Europe (pixel coastlines drawn from a polygon list), with the minibus \"The\n    Old Trout\" driving a dotted route to the next city.\n  - `talk`: dialogue with portraits (`E.Dialog`, modal, babble voices), possibly with choices (`choices`, `onChoice`)\n    that set flags.\n  - `teamtalk`: 3 big cards (§7.3): HAIRDRYER, ARM ROUND THE SHOULDER, TACTICS BOARD (which then asks for a formation:\n    2-2 / 1-2-1 / 2-1-1). Extra local players can join here.\n  - `challenge`: the Gaffer's Challenge card for this match (an optional objective).\n  - `tunnel`: the walkout (below).\n  - `match`: plays the match with the round's options.\n  - `result`: the bracket advances; the tabloid for a win or a loss; stickers; the autosave.\n- **Losing** a round: the \"KNOCKED OUT!\" tabloid, then CONTINUE? with a 10 s countdown (arcade style; ✕ retries the\n  round from its team talk, ○ returns to the title).\n- **Tunnel walkout** (`tunnel`): both teams line up in the tunnel, then walk out onto the pitch in two lines with the\n  referee. The anthem plays. The handshake line: each player passes the other line, arm out. Captains and the referee\n  at the centre circle, then the coin toss (a sprite flip). This scene also works as the AI Hub card (§6.28).\n- **Ending** (`ending`): the trophy ceremony (a podium on the pitch, the Europhoria Cup (§8.2) lifted by Daz with all\n  the Kippers jumping, confetti and fireworks, the anthem), then the parade (Kipperton harbour by day: the team on top\n  of a fishing trawler on wheels driving along the harbour road, the crowd on both sides throwing scarves, gulls), then\n  the closing tabloid, then the credits roll (names scrolling over the parade, the About credits).\n\n### 6.25 Training\n\nScene `training`: a list of 9 drills (§7.6), each with a completion tick. The coach (Mags, then Sandra for\ndefending) explains each step in a short modal dialog, then the drill runs on the training ground with a goal and\ncounters on the HUD (\"PASSES 3/5\"). Success: a fanfare and the next step. A drill's last step completes it (saved).\nDummies are footballers driven by `ScriptController`s (static, slow-walking, or attacking).\n\n### 6.26 Penalties mode\n\nA shootout from the start (`match { shootoutOnly: true }`) between two picked teams in a picked stadium. 1 player\n(against the CPU) or 2 (versus): each human takes his side's kicks and keeps goal for his side. Best of 5, then sudden\ndeath. Results as §6.23.\n\n### 6.27 Local multiplayer\n\n- 1–4 players: each joined input (`game.players`) picks a side on the PLAYERS screen: a big row of controller icons,\n  each in its player's colour, moved left (HOME), centre (CPU, which means sitting out) or right (AWAY), then ✕ for\n  ready. At least one human must be on a side. Co-op (humans on the same side) and versus both work.\n- Each human controls one footballer at a time and switches on his own. Two humans on a side never hold the same\n  footballer: switching skips held ones. Each human has his own prompts (their device) and colour tag.\n- One shared screen: the broadcast camera follows the ball. When humans are far apart, it widens toward them\n  (`cam.frame` with a zoom range of .9–1.25).\n- The pause shows who paused (the engine does: \"P2 PAUSED\").\n\n### 6.28 Online: AI Hub sessions (shared-world)\n\nRead the protocol (github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub `lib/hub/README.md`) whole before building this. The flow:\n\n1. `session.js` is the first script (§3.3). `AIHub.active` is true from the first line in a session. Then the game\n   creates `E.Game` with `corner: false` and `menu: { quit: false }`, skips the title and the attract mode, and every\n   scene has `pausable: false`.\n2. Boot goes to scene `hubwait` (\"CONNECTING…\" over the stadium backdrop) and runs\n   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`. With `null`, go to the title\n   and run as a normal game.\n3. **Set up from the shared seed** (the same on every copy): `const R = AIHub.rng('setup')`: the two teams (from the 6),\n   the stadium (from the 5), its weather. Sides: players in seat order alternate HOME (ids at even positions in\n   `info.players`) and AWAY. With 3 players, the side with 1 human gets the **underdog boost**: Euphoria gain ×1.5.\n   Each human controls one footballer of his side. The half length fits the round:\n   `min(90, (info.limitMs/1000 − 50)/2)` seconds, and at least 45.\n4. **The card:** scene `tunnel` in card mode: the two teams in the tunnel, the hub players' names in their seat\n   colours (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) with ✓ for those in `card.ready`; \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the\n   other side before the final whistle\"; this device's controls (glyph prompts); the time left from `card.left`\n   (\"PAUSED\" when `card.paused`); \"READY ✕/Enter\" and \"MORE TIME △/T\" buttons (also tapped or clicked). Enter, ✕ or a\n   click on Ready calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △, T or a click on More time calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (again to\n   take it back). Nothing on the card changes the round; it has no menus. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the match is built,\n   with no key press.\n5. **Start:** on `start`, go to `match` in session mode. A 3-2-1 countdown follows `AIHub.time()` (negative); play\n   begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n6. **Host** (`AIHub.isHost`): runs the sim. Remote humans' footballers use `RemoteController`s fed by their input\n   messages (Appendix B: stick, held bits, cumulative press counters so a lost packet never loses a press; neutral\n   after 500 ms without input). It sends a snapshot 14 times a second (unreliable, under 1,100 bytes) and coalesced\n   events at most 5 times a second (reliable). That keeps it at 19 messages a second or fewer, under the limit of 20.\n7. **Client:** sends its Intent 15 times a second (unreliable) and rare reliable messages (the Save Duel press with its\n   `AIHub.time()`, the celebration pick). It renders 100 ms behind the newest snapshot, interpolating positions (and\n   extrapolating up to 150 ms when snapshots are late). It runs rig animation, crowd, audio and commentary locally from\n   the snapshot state and the host's events. The client's own player is drawn where the host says (no prediction).\n   Instead, every button press gives instant local feedback: the glyph flashes, a kick sound, rumble.\n8. **Save Duel online:** the host sends `duel` with its start time. The defending client shows the ring on the same\n   timeline and sends its press time. The host resolves when the press arrives, or 300 ms after the window closes\n   (a miss).\n9. **Server mode** (`AIHub.server`, the host has no player of its own): run the host code with no local player, no\n   camera and no input; draw nothing.\n10. **Leaving:** on `leave`, that player's footballer goes back to the CPU. The round goes on (the hub voids it only if\n    the host leaves).\n11. **Time-up:** on `time-up`, the host calls `finish` at once with the current score.\n12. **Finish** (the host, once; at full time or on time-up):\n    `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`. `standings`: the winning side's players (still in the round)\n    tied first, the other side's second; a draw is one group with everyone. `scores`: each player's side's goals.\n    `stats`: per player `{ Goals, Shots, Tackles }`. `awards`: `[{ id, title: 'Player of the Match', detail }]` for the\n    human with the best match rating. Before it, send a last reliable snapshot with `over: 1`, so every copy shows the\n    same final score.\n13. **End:** on `end` (any reason), stop taking input, stop sending, stop all sound (music, the crowd engine, voices),\n    and show \"FULL TIME\" with the score, or \"ROUND VOID\" for `void` or `host-left`, \"YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT\" for\n    `sat-out`. The hub draws its results over it.\n14. **Rules:** no other network access; no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`/`window.open`; no names typed by players (names\n    come from `info.players` and are drawn with `E.font`, never inserted as HTML); Options while Create (button 8) is\n    held is the hub's, so ignore it. In a session, Options (or Esc) alone opens **our own** canvas overlay, SESSION\n    SETTINGS (volume, music, effects, voices, crowd, button symbols; built with `EF.UI`), not the engine's menu, so\n    nothing pauses: the match goes on, on the host above all, and the player's footballer goes to the CPU while the\n    overlay is open. Dev mode, the attract mode, saves and the cup do not exist in sessions. A draw at full time\n    stands in a session (no extra time or shootout), so a round fits its minutes.\n\n### 6.29 Attract mode\n\n- **The idle watcher** runs on `title` and every front-end and cup menu screen (not in matches, training or story\n  dialogs). Any input resets it: a key, a mouse move of more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, a touch, a pad button, or a\n  stick past the dead zone. After **10.0 s** without input it goes to `attract`. In tests: `game.advance(9.9)` leaves\n  the title showing; `game.advance(0.2)` more starts the attract mode.\n- **The attract scene** is a director script (`game.script`) over a real AI-versus-AI match that **cheats freely**: it\n  places players and the ball, sets the Euphoria, forces outcomes (the save fails, the volley goes in), and turns on\n  everyone's infinite stamina. Segments, about 90 s per loop:\n  1. **MATCHDAY LIVE** (30 s): a random stadium (it cycles through all 5 over loops). The captain is given the ball 230\n     from goal with the gauge full: Europhoria, the super strike, the Save Duel (it fails), the goal, a celebration,\n     the replay.\n  2. **SET-PIECE SPECIAL** (15 s): a corner, then a bicycle kick goal (forced).\n  3. **THE DARK ARTS** (15 s): Lucchetto: a dive in the box, the penalty, VAR CHECK, \"PENALTY STANDS\", the goal; then a\n     Simulation booking.\n  4. **SHOOTOUT** (15 s): 3 kicks a side, including a Panenka.\n  5. **WEATHER REPORT** (10 s): 2.5 s cuts: rain at the Smokehouse, the snow and the orange ball, fog and flares,\n     fireworks in the Euphorium.\n  6. **TITLE CARD** (5 s): the logo, \"PRESS START\", the cup records (fastest cup win, biggest win).\n- A banner \"DEMO · PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (with the right glyph) stays at the bottom. Commentary and the crowd play as in a\n  match.\n- **Any input** (the watcher's list) goes straight back to `title`, with the focus on the first tile. The press that\n  exits is swallowed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it does not also pick a menu item.\n- On touch-only devices it runs the same way; a tap goes back to the title.\n\n### 6.30 Dev mode\n\n- **Reach it:** the pause menu's \"Dev mode\" item, the backquote key (`` ` ``) or F1 in any scene (call\n  `preventDefault()` on F1's keydown, or Chrome opens its help page), or `?dev=1`. It is never available in AI Hub\n  sessions. Opening it from the pause menu resumes the game (`game.resume()`) and opens the panel over the running\n  scene. The panel takes the input while it is open; the match keeps running behind it, with every human's footballer\n  handed to the CPU, so slider changes can be watched live. A **Freeze** toggle stops the sim instead.\n- **The panel:** a canvas drawer on the right 40% of the screen, translucent (`E.ui.box` with alpha .9), 4 tabs (L1/R1,\n  Q/E, or click): TUNE, CHEATS, WARP, INFO. Rows are navigated with the d-pad or stick; left/right changes a value\n  (holding speeds it up); ✕ toggles or runs; ○, Esc or F1 closes. The mouse hovers, clicks and drags sliders.\n  - **TUNE:** every `EF.T` slider (Appendix A), grouped (Movement, Ball, Passing & Shooting, Keepers, Defending &\n    Rules, Euphoria, AI, Match). Each shows its value, its default and a ↺ when changed. At the top: **RESET ALL TO\n    DEFAULTS**; on each row, □ resets that one. Changes apply at once and are kept in `E.store('ef:tuning')`, so they\n    survive a reload until reset. A dev-panel badge shows on the HUD while any value differs from its default.\n  - **CHEATS:** infinite stamina (per side), Euphoria always full (per side), invincible keeper (per side), the CPU\n    controls everyone (watch mode), \"pure football\" (no Euphoria, supers or events), freeze the clock, a goal for home\n    / away, set the clock to 44' / 89', slow motion (0.25×) and step one frame (while frozen), show hitboxes and\n    contact capsules, show the AI (formation spots, roles, the pass lanes it scores, its decision text over the\n    carrier), show the ball's predicted path and the air-ball window, show `rig.debug` skeletons, mute the crowd.\n  - **WARP:** go to any scene and part: every deep link (§4.4), each cup round's pre-match beat, half time, extra time,\n    a shootout, the results, the ending, the album, about; trigger now: a corner, a free kick, a penalty, a matchday\n    event (pick one), a super strike, a Save Duel, a foul with a yellow or a red, a dive, VAR, a celebration (pick\n    one), a replay; unlock everything (the cup's rounds, stickers, balls); reset the save. Two galleries: ANIMATION\n    (every move of §8.3 on a loop, on a chosen rig, in every view, at 1×, 0.25× or frame by frame; deep link\n    `#dev/anim/<move>`) and SOUND TEST (every SFX, song, chant and voice, with sliders for the speaker profiles).\n  - **INFO:** the version and build, the seed, the scene and mode, `game.debug.snapshot()` pretty-printed, counts\n    (bodies, particles, fans, lights, rigs drawn), the frame time (`game.stats`), the hub role when relevant.\n- Dev mode never changes a save unless WARP's unlock or reset is used (it asks first, with its own confirm row).\n\n### 6.31 Saves, settings, unlocks, stickers\n\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` with `write = () => ({ data: EF.Save.data(), place: roundName, level: roundIndex })` and `read`.\n  It autosaves after each cup match and at the start of each round. CUP RUN → CONTINUE loads `saves.latest()`. Data\n  (versioned, with `migrate`): `{ v: 1, cup: { round, results: [{ opp, score, pens }], flags: { loyal } , teamTalks },\n  stickers: { id: true | 'shiny' }, unlocks: { balls: [] }, records: { fastestCup, biggestWin }, drills: { id: true } }`.\n- **Our settings** (`EF.SETTINGS` in `new E.Game({ menu: { settings } })`; group Game unless noted): difficulty (Easy /\n  Normal / Hard / Europhoric), half length (1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), pass assist (Off / Low / High), shot assist\n  (On / Off), switching (Auto / Assisted / Manual), cards (Off / Normal / Strict), draws in Kick-About (Allowed / Golden\n  goal / Penalties), prompts (Always / While learning / Off), commentary (On / Off), replays (On / Off), camera\n  (Broadcast / Classic / Aerial), radar (On / Off); group Sound: Voices (slider .8), Crowd (slider .8); group\n  Controller: Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox, §2.3). The engine supplies the rest (volume, music, effects, reduce\n  motion, shake, flashes, screen filter, zoom, rebinding).\n- **Unlocks** (\"items\"): balls for Kick-About: Classic (white panels), Winter Orange (automatic in snow), The Golden\n  Ball (win the cup), Old Leather (finish all 5 Gaffer's Challenges). Matches have no pickups: football stays\n  football.\n- **Stickers:** §7.5. Earning one shows a toast with the sticker sliding in (sound: shimmer).\n\n### 6.32 About and credits\n\nThe About pages render `EF.ABOUT` (§3.3) in this order: Source Information (every field TASK.md lists: Date, Source,\nPlan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model,\nUsage), Testing Feedback (4 answers), Engine Feedback (6 answers), Prompt Feedback (4 answers), then the credits.\n\"unknown\" stays \"unknown\". The test suite checks that every field is present and non-empty (§11.3).\n\n### 6.33 Touch-only detection\n\n`EF.touchOnly()` is true when `?touchonly=1` is set, or when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches` and not\n`matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad is connected (`navigator.getGamepads()`). It becomes false\nfor the rest of the visit on the first `keydown` or `gamepadconnected`. While it is true: the title shows the notice\nand the SETTINGS button; menus still answer taps (to reach settings and about); play cannot start (the tiles show\n\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" when tapped); the attract mode runs.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content\n\nIn a football game the usual content words map like this. **Levels** are the 5 cup rounds, each in its own stadium\nwith its own weather and events (§7.2), plus the training ground. **Enemies** are the 5 opposing clubs, each with its\nown tactics and gimmick; the final's Olympique Opulence is the boss team, with a boss keeper and a boss captain\n(§7.1). The referees are the neutral hazard. **Items** are the unlockable balls, the stickers and the team-talk buffs;\nthere are no pickups in matches (§6.31). **Story beats** are in §7.3.\n\nTone everywhere: British football broadcasting and tabloid back pages, turned up. That means puns (fish puns for the\nKippers), commentary clichés, deadpan replies, affectionate and never mean. National stereotypes are off-limits: the\nopponents' jokes come from their **football philosophies**, their food, weather and stadiums. All names are original;\nnone is a real club, player or person. Text is ASCII except the accented letters §5.5 adds.\n\n### 7.1 Teams\n\nEach team: name, short code, nickname, city, stadium, kits (home, away, keeper), crest, formation, tactic, chant,\nsignature celebration, 5 players (number, name, position, build, size, hair, skin, hair colour, stats, captain's super).\nKit colours give rig colours: `cloth` (shirt), `pants` (shorts), `boot`, `belt` (= shorts), `trim` (socks and collar),\n`glove` (keepers), plus `kit: { pattern, color2, number, numberColor }` (§5.2).\n\n**KIPPERTON ATHLETIC** — \"The Kippers\", KIP. A fishing town on the cold north coast. Home: the Smokehouse. Kit: tangerine\n`#f08a24` and navy `#1c2a5a` hoops, navy shorts, tangerine socks; away: white with a tangerine sash. Crest: a navy shield\nwith a smoked kipper crossed over an anchor. Formation 2-1-1 (the team talk can change it). Tactic `plucky` (balanced:\npress .55, line .45, tempo .7, passRisk .5). Chant \"KIP-PER-TON!\". Celebration: the fish slap. Manager: MAGS MULLIGAN\n(a fishmonger turned manager: flat cap, scarf, a voice like a foghorn).\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Build / size / hair | Key stats | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | WALLY CRABB | GK | bulky 1.2, bald | keep 76, weight 80 | 41, a part-time lighthouse keeper; huge gloves |\n| 4 | SANDRA \"THE HARBOUR WALL\" OKAFOR | DEF | bulky 1.2, short | tackle 88, weight 95, temper 40 | barges like a trawler |\n| 6 | AGGIE NOWAK | MID | heroic 1.12, ponytail | pass 90, skill 70 | the brains; Polish grandmother in the stands |\n| 7 | TOMMY \"TWINKLETOES\" TRAN | FWD | heroic 1.08, spiky | pace 95, skill 92 | step-overs for breakfast |\n| 9 | DAZ PILCHARD (captain) | FWD | heroic 1.15, short | shoot 90, pace 80 | super **THE SMOKED KIPPER** (path `wobble`, smoke trail, the ball briefly shaped like a fish) |\n\n**AFC HOOFINGTON** — \"The Hoofers\", HOO (Qualifying Round). Brown `#6a4a2a` and amber `#e8a830` stripes. Crest: a\nmuddy boot. Formation 2-2. Tactic `routeone` (longBall .6, press .4, line .4, tempo .5, foul .25). Chant: a\nfoghorn-low \"HOOOOF!\" on every clearance. Celebration: Cheering_Two_Hands.\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|","numLines":350,"startLine":1000,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q8vxRoWcNqYPVGBmngpKqj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
