{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FWrmvtzPEejKGPZcsAicn2","type":"tool_result","content":"1350\t| 1 | ALF STOPPARD | GK | long kicks only |\n1351\t| 3 | GAZ HOOPER | DEF | heads everything |\n1352\t| 5 | DUNCAN DUNSTABLE | DEF | bulky; weight 92 |\n1353\t| 8 | KEV LUMP | MID | \"Lump it!\" |\n1354\t| 9 | NORMAN \"THE NODDER\" NEEDHAM (captain) | FWD | headers 95; super **ROW Z RETURN** (`meteor`: a hoof into the sky that comes down onto the goal) |\n1355\t\n1356\t**REAL PASAPASA** — \"Los Pasitos\", RPP (Round of 16). White `#f4f2ec` with lilac `#9a7ad0` trim; away lilac. Crest: a\n1357\tsun over two arrows passing. Formation 1-2-1. Tactic `keepball` (shortBias .9, passRisk .2, tempo .85, press .55,\n1358\tdribble .25). Chant: \"OLÉ!\" rising with every pass; white handkerchiefs waved. Celebration: the corner-flag dance.\n1359\t\n1360\t| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n1361\t|---|---|---|---|\n1362\t| 1 | PACO PORTERO | GK | |\n1363\t| 4 | RAFA RONDO | DEF | |\n1364\t| 6 | TITO TOQUE | MID | one touch, always |\n1365\t| 8 | IKER INTERIOR | MID | |\n1366\t| 10 | PEPITO PASARELA (captain) | MID | chibi build 1.0 (tiny); super **EL PASODOBLE** (`zigzag`: the ball dances 3 steps in rhythm) |\n1367\t\n1368\t**SV STAHLPRESSE 04** — \"Die Pressen\", SVS (Quarter-final). Steel grey `#6a7078` and hazard orange `#ff7a1a` halves.\n1369\tCrest: a cog with a hammer. Formation 1-2-1, high line. Tactic `gegenpress` (press .9, pressers 2, line .7, tempo 1,\n1370\tstamina use high). Chant: a drum and \"HEY! HEY! HEY!\". Celebration: the robot.\n1371\t\n1372\t| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n1373\t|---|---|---|---|\n1374\t| 1 | MANNI MAUER | GK | |\n1375\t| 2 | FRANZI FLEISS | DEF | never stops running |\n1376\t| 5 | UWE UMSCHALT | MID | transitions |\n1377\t| 7 | JURGEN JAGD (JÜRGEN once §5.5 lands) | FWD | the hunter |\n1378\t| 9 | KLAUS HAMMERSCHMIDT (captain) | FWD | bulky 1.25; super **DER HAMMERSCHLAG** (`hammer`: 3 forge-hammer bounces, each shaking the screen) |\n1379\t\n1380\t**AC LUCCHETTO** — \"I Lucchetti\", the Padlocks, ACL (Semi-final). Burgundy `#7a1a2a` with silver `#c8ccd4`; away silver.\n1381\tCrest: a padlock in a laurel wreath. Formation 2-1-1 played deep, switching to 3-1 (the MID drops into the back line)\n1382\twhen they lead after 60', which is also when the bus arrives. Tactic `catenaccio` (line .15, press .3, foul .6, dive .5,\n1383\tlongBall .35 on the counter). Chant: a slow minor hum and a curva drum; flares. Celebration: the badge kiss.\n1384\t\n1385\t| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n1386\t|---|---|---|---|\n1387\t| 1 | ROCCO RIPARO | GK | |\n1388\t| 3 | DINO DIFESA | DEF | |\n1389\t| 5 | MARCO MARCATURA | DEF | man-marks your best player |\n1390\t| 7 | FABIO FALLO | MID | the diver (temper 90): goes down in the box at the first touch |\n1391\t| 10 | SALVATORE SERRATURA (captain) | FWD | the lone counter-attacker; super **LA CHIAVE** (the key; `around`: it curves round every body in its way) |\n1392\t\n1393\t**OLYMPIQUE OPULENCE** — \"Les Milliardaires\", OPU (Final; the boss team). Gold `#e8c040` and black `#141414`\n1394\tstripes. Crest: a crown on a stack of coins. Formation 1-2-1, attacking. Tactic `galacticos`. Owner: BARON VON\n1395\tBULLION. Chant: polite golf claps (they're paid to be there) and a hired brass band. Celebration: the helicopter.\n1396\t\n1397\t| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n1398\t|---|---|---|---|\n1399\t| 1 | GUNNAR \"THE VAULT\" VAULT | GK | **the boss keeper**: bulky, size 2.0, reach +40%, catches anything under 300 |\n1400\t| 4 | CASPIAN CASH | DEF | |\n1401\t| 8 | BENTLEY BLING | MID | skill 90 |\n1402\t| 11 | SERGEI SOVEREIGN | FWD | pace 96 |\n1403\t| 10 | MAXIMILIEN D'OR (captain) | FWD | vain superstar; Golden Moment (§6.13); super **LA BOTTE D'OR** (`split`: 3 golden balls, one real) |\n1404\t\n1405\t**Referees** (registry `referee`): ARTHUR HALTWHISTLE (strictness 1.3, gullibility .2; the qualifying round and the\n1406\tfinal: \"the best in Europe\"), PIERRE PATIENCE (.7, .5; round of 16), INGRID IRONSIDE (1.1, .3; quarter-final),\n1407\tSERGIO SEVERO (1.2, .7, varHappy .9; semi-final: dramatic, falls for everything, loves VAR). Kick-About picks one at\n1408\trandom.\n1409\t\n1410\t**Formations** (registry `formation`; `u, v` as in §6.13; `drop` is the role a red card removes):\n1411\t\n1412\t| Id | Roles and base spots `[u, v]` | drop |\n1413\t|---|---|---|\n1414\t| `2-2` | GK [.03,.5]; DEFL [.22,.3]; DEFR [.22,.7]; FWDL [.60,.32]; FWDR [.60,.68] | FWDR |\n1415\t| `1-2-1` | GK; DEF [.22,.5]; MIDL [.42,.28]; MIDR [.42,.72]; FWD [.64,.5] | MIDR |\n1416\t| `2-1-1` | GK; DEFL [.22,.32]; DEFR [.22,.68]; MID [.45,.5]; FWD [.68,.5] | MID |\n1417\t| `3-1` | GK; DEFL [.16,.25]; DEF [.13,.5]; DEFR [.16,.75]; FWD [.55,.5] | DEFL |\n1418\t\n1419\tEach role also gets `att`, `def`, `pull` and `uRange`. Defenders: att [+.14, 0], def [0, 0], pull [.45, .55], uRange\n1420\t[.08, .62]. Midfielders: att [+.12, ±.06 outward], def [−.12, ∓.04], pull [.55, .45], uRange [.15, .85]. Forwards:\n1421\tatt [+.18, 0], def [−.12, 0], pull [.5, .6], uRange [.35, .95]. Tune them by watching AI-versus-AI matches with the AI\n1422\toverlay on (§6.30).\n1423\t\n1424\t### 7.2 Stadiums\n1425\t\n1426\t| Id | Name, city | Time / weather | Pitch | Stands and skyline | Crowd | Events |\n1427\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1428\t| `smokehouse` | THE SMOKEHOUSE, Kipperton | dusk → night, rain .7, wind .4 | wet, mud in the goalmouths, 6 puddles, worn centre | a small main stand with a corrugated roof (3 tiers), terraces with fishing nets behind each goal (2 tiers); skyline: smokehouse chimneys trailing smoke, the harbour, a lighthouse with a sweeping beam, gulls | 600, 80% home (tangerine and navy), a brass band | seagull, floodlight flicker, Kipper Keith |\n1429\t| `pasapasa` | ESTADIO PASAPASA, Solera | sunny afternoon | hard and dry (friction .8), perfect stripes | a white-walled bowl (5 tiers) with terracotta roofs; skyline: palms, a cathedral dome, hills | 1,400, white handkerchiefs | beach ball |\n1430\t| `stahlpresse` | STAHLPRESSE ARENA, Eisenhutte | night, snow .6 | snow, lines brushed clear, orange ball | a steep steel arena (5 tiers) under a roof truss; skyline: steelworks chimneys with glowing furnaces, steam, snowy mountains | 1,600, a scarf wall, drums | Steel Stag pitch invader, floodlight flicker |\n1431\t| `lucchetto` | STADIO LUCCHETTO, Castelfortezza | dusk → night; fog from the 2nd half | grass, a little uneven (random small deflections) | an old bowl (4 tiers) with a steep curva end; skyline: medieval walls, a bell tower, cypress trees | 1,200, flares, the curva drum | flare smoke |\n1432\t| `euphorium` | THE EUPHORIUM, Aurelia | night, clear | perfect | a huge golden dome stadium (6 tiers), LED rings, a jumbotron above the north stand; skyline: the dome's ribs, searchlights, lasers | 1,600, mixed, confetti cannons | drone, fireworks |\n1433\t| `rec` | KIPPERTON REC (training) | overcast morning | patchy | no stands: a fence, a few parents on a bench, the sea wall; cones, dummies, rebound boards | 8 | none |\n1434\t\n1435\tEach stadium also lists: its board sponsor texts (fictional and funny: \"SMOKY JOE'S KIPPERS\", \"GULL INSURANCE: WE\n1436\tCOVER EVERYTHING\", \"PIE-O-MATIC\", \"EUROPHORIA COLA\", \"BULLION BANK: MONEY TALKS\", \"STAHLPRESSE: WE PRESS HARDER\",\n1437\t\"CASTELFORTEZZA LOCKSMITHS\"), its light setup, its floor palette and its music override.\n1438\t\n1439\t### 7.3 The story (Cup Run beats)\n1440\t\n1441\tThe premise: the Continental Federation meant to invite KINGSBRIDGE ALBION to the EUROPHORIA CUP, Europe's grandest\n1442\tknockout competition. A clerk typed KIPPERTON instead, and the rules say an invitation is an invitation. Kipperton\n1443\tAthletic (population 3,112; floodlights powered by fish oil; fourteen pounds in the kitty) are going to Europe in a\n1444\tminibus with three good tyres.\n1445\t\n1446\t**Prologue** (`prologue`)\n1447\t- Tabloid, THE DAILY ROAR: **\"FISH OUT OF WATER!\"** — \"Typo sends tiny Kipperton into the Europhoria Cup. 'Rules are\n1448\t  rules,' shrugs the Federation.\"\n1449\t- Talk at the Smokehouse:\n1450\t  - MAGS: \"Right, you lot. Fourteen quid in the kitty, a minibus with three good tyres, and a letter that says EUROPE.\"\n1451\t  - DAZ: \"Gaffer, do they have chips in Europe?\"\n1452\t  - MAGS: \"They have EVERYTHING in Europe, Darren. Including teams that'll eat us for breakfast.\"\n1453\t  - SANDRA: \"Let 'em try. I've got an appetite and all.\"\n1454\t  - MAGS: \"That's the spirit. First up, at home: AFC Hoofington. Route-one merchants. Keep your heads up. Literally.\"\n1455\t  - Choice: [ \"LET'S PLAY\" ] / [ \"TRAINING FIRST\" ] (the second goes to Training, then back to the cup).\n1456\t\n1457\t**Qualifying Round** — vs AFC Hoofington at the Smokehouse (rain, dusk). Referee Haltwhistle.\n1458\t- Pre: **\"THE LONG AND THE SHORT OF IT\"** — \"Hoofington's aerial bombardment heads for Kipperton's puddles.\"\n1459\t- NEEDHAM (on a portrait card): \"We don't pass, love. We 'oof.\"\n1460\t- Challenge: **Score a header.**\n1461\t- Win: **\"KIP KIP HOORAY!\"**; loss: **\"BATTERED!\"**\n1462\t- After: MAGS: \"Not bad. Not good. But not bad.\" TREV (a commentary card): \"A proper cold night, and they've warmed it up.\"\n1463\t\n1464\t**Round of 16** — vs Real Pasapasa at Estadio Pasapasa (sun). Referee Patience.\n1465\t- Travel: the minibus heads south, with a postcard: \"WISH YOU WERE HERE (IT'S HOT)\".\n1466\t- Pre: **\"PASS THE PARCEL\"** — \"Kippers must stop the passing masters... if they can find the ball.\"\n1467\t- PEPITO: \"You will chase the ball until you are dizzy, little fishes.\"\n1468\t- Challenge: **Win the ball back 5 times.**\n1469\t- Win: **\"SOLE-DESTROYING FOR SOLERA!\"**; loss: **\"PASSED OUT\"**\n1470\t- After: AGGIE: \"I counted. They made 412 passes.\" MAGS: \"And we made two goals. Football's a funny old game.\"\n1471\t\n1472\t**Quarter-final** — vs SV Stahlpresse 04 at the Stahlpresse Arena (night, snow). Referee Ironside.\n1473\t- Travel: snow chains on the minibus; the map turns white.\n1474\t- Pre: **\"PRESSED FOR TIME\"** — \"The Steel Machine never stops running. Kipperton's bus barely starts.\"\n1475\t- KLAUS: \"We run. You run. We run more.\"\n1476\t- Challenge: **Nutmeg an opponent.**\n1477\t- Win: **\"KIPPERS MELT THE STEEL!\"**; loss: **\"CRUSHED\"**\n1478\t- After: TOMMY: \"Did you see his face when it went through his legs?\" SANDRA: \"Did you see mine? Frozen solid.\"\n1479\t\n1480\t**Semi-final** — vs AC Lucchetto at Stadio Lucchetto (dusk, then fog). Referee Severo.\n1481\t- Pre: **\"PADLOCK AND KEY\"** — \"Can Kipperton crack Europe's meanest defence? Locksmiths on standby.\"\n1482\t- SALVATORE: \"Nobody scores against Lucchetto. Nobody. We lock the door and we eat the key.\"\n1483\t- MAGS (before the match): \"They'll dive, they'll moan, and if they go ahead they'll park the bus. Don't fall for any\n1484\t  of it.\"\n1485\t- Challenge: **Score from a free kick.**\n1486\t- Win: **\"THEY PARKED THE BUS — WE STOLE IT!\"**; loss: **\"LOCKED OUT\"**\n1487\t\n1488\t**Before the final** (`villain`) — a hotel lobby, night.\n1489\t- BARON VON BULLION: \"Mister Pilchard. Fifty million. A gold-plated jet ski. And all the caviar you can eat.\"\n1490\t- Choice: [ \"I'M A KIPPER, MATE. ALWAYS.\" ] → flag `loyal`: the final starts with Euphoria +20 and the sticker LOYAL\n1491\t  KIPPER. / [ \"...DOES THE JET SKI COME IN ORANGE?\" ] → DAZ: \"Only joking, Gaffer! Kipper till I die.\" MAGS: \"You\n1492\t  nearly gave me a heart attack.\" (Euphoria +10.)\n1493\t\n1494\t**Final** — vs Olympique Opulence at the Euphorium (night, fireworks). Referee Haltwhistle.\n1495\t- Pre: **\"DAVID VS GOLDIATH\"** — \"Fish-oil floodlights meet the richest club on Earth.\"\n1496\t- MAXIMILIEN: \"I have three Golden Boots. You have... boots.\"\n1497\t- Challenge: **Score a Super Strike.**\n1498\t- Win: the ending (§6.24): the ceremony; the parade; **\"THE PLAICE TO BE: KIPPERS ARE KINGS OF EUROPE!\"**; an epilogue\n1499\t  line: \"Kingsbridge Albion have demanded a recount.\" Credits.\n1500\t- Loss: **\"SO CLOSE! Golden boys break Kipper hearts\"**, then CONTINUE? (retry the final).\n1501\t\n1502\t**Team talks** (registry `teamtalk`; MAGS says one line from a pool of 3 for each):\n1503\t- **HAIRDRYER** (\"Get out there and TERRIFY them!\"): +10% speed and tackle strength for the first 15 game minutes; the\n1504\t  referee's strictness +20%.\n1505\t- **ARM ROUND THE SHOULDER** (\"Just enjoy it. Your mum's watching.\"): stamina regen +25% for the match; Euphoria starts\n1506\t  at +15.\n1507\t- **TACTICS BOARD** (\"Here's the plan.\"): pick the formation (2-2 / 1-2-1 / 2-1-1); pass accuracy +10%.\n1508\t\n1509\t**Gaffer's Challenges** (registry `challenge`): the 5 above. Each is an event condition (for example `header` events\n1510\twith `goal` within 0.5 s by a Kipperton player). Completing one shows a toast during the match, gives a shiny sticker\n1511\tafterwards, and all 5 unlock the Old Leather ball.\n1512\t\n1513\t### 7.4 Commentary pools\n1514\t\n1515\tWrite at least **300 lines** in total, at least **12 per major event** (goal, shot saved, near miss and woodwork,\n1516\ttackle, foul, card, dive, super strike, Save Duel, skill move, header and volley, kickoff, half time, full time,\n1517\tweather, matchday events, VAR, penalty, shootout), with banter pairs (`reply`) in about a third of them. Write\n1518\toriginal lines only: no famous real commentary quotes. Samples to set the voice:\n1519\t\n1520\t- **kickoff:** BARRY \"And we're underway at {$stadium}! Lovely evening for it, Trev.\" / TREV \"It's raining sideways,\n1521\t  Barry.\"\n1522\t- **goal:** BARRY \"OH, YOU BEAUTY! {$player} has absolutely LEATHERED it!\"; \"GET IN! Back of the net from {$player}!\"\n1523\t  / TREV \"Keeper had no chance. None. Nada. Zilch.\"; BARRY \"{$team} lead, and the away end is a washing machine!\"\n1524\t- **goal, the Kippers:** BARRY \"OH MY COD! KIPPERTON HAVE SCORED!\"; \"That's a plaice in history for {$player}!\"\n1525\t- **near miss:** BARRY \"OHHH! Inches! INCHES!\" / TREV \"He'll see that one in his sleep.\"\n1526\t- **woodwork:** BARRY \"DOINK! Off the woodwork!\" / TREV \"You could hear that in the car park.\"\n1527\t- **header:** BARRY \"Rises like a salmon! A kipper, actually, but you get the idea.\"\n1528\t- **bicycle:** BARRY \"AN OVERHEAD KICK! ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!\" / TREV \"I tried that once. Spent a week in traction.\"\n1529\t- **nutmeg:** BARRY \"Through the legs! He'll hear about that in the canteen.\"\n1530\t- **slide that launches:** BARRY \"He's taken man, ball, and most of the grass!\" / TREV \"That's a booking in any\n1531\t  country.\"\n1532\t- **dive:** BARRY \"Oh, he's gone down like a sack of spuds!\" / TREV \"There was more contact at my wedding, Barry.\"\n1533\t- **simulation booked:** TREV \"Yellow card for the amateur dramatics. Quite right.\"\n1534\t- **card:** BARRY \"The referee reaches for his pocket... and it's YELLOW!\"\n1535\t- **VAR:** BARRY \"Here we go. VAR. Put the kettle on.\" / TREV \"Put two on.\"\n1536\t- **super strike:** BARRY \"WHAT HAS HE DONE TO THAT BALL?!\" / TREV \"That's not football. That's sorcery.\"\n1537\t- **Save Duel perfect:** BARRY \"AND THE KEEPER'S GOT IT! FINGERTIPS! UNBELIEVABLE!\"\n1538\t- **the bus:** BARRY \"They've only gone and LITERALLY parked the bus!\" / TREV \"Has it got a ticket?\"\n1539\t- **half time:** BARRY \"That's the half-time whistle. Time for a pie, Trev?\" / TREV \"Two pies, Barry.\"\n1540\t- **full time, a Kipperton win:** BARRY \"They'll be dancing on the harbour wall in Kipperton tonight!\"\n1541\t- **seagull:** BARRY \"And a seagull has taken possession!\" / TREV \"Better first touch than some I've seen.\"\n1542\t- **rain:** TREV \"Proper weather, this. Separates the men from the boys. And the boys from their boots.\"\n1543\t\n1544\tThe PA has 20 lines; tabloids have the headlines in §7.3; each story speaker has 5 or more lines for their beats.\n1545\t\n1546\t### 7.5 Stickers\n1547\t\n1548\t51 stickers in the album:\n1549\t- 30 players (5 a team, earned by playing them, the Kippers from the start);\n1550\t- 6 crests (earned by playing them);\n1551\t- 5 stadiums (earned by playing there);\n1552\t- 5 shiny Gaffer's Challenges;\n1553\t- 5 specials: MAGS MULLIGAN (finish the prologue), KIPPER KEITH (tackle the invader), BARRY & TREV (hear 50 lines),\n1554\t  THE BUS (score past it), LOYAL KIPPER (the loyal answer).\n1555\t\n1556\tEach sticker: `{ id, kind, ref, name, how }`. The album shows \"how\" under a silhouette.\n1557\t\n1558\t### 7.6 Training drills (registry `drill`)\n1559\t\n1560\t| # | Id | Title | Teaches | Steps (each with Mags's or Sandra's lines) |\n1561\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1562\t| 1 | `move` | ON YOUR MARKS | run, sprint, stamina | weave through 6 cones; sprint the straight; recover your stamina |\n1563\t| 2 | `passing` | PASS MASTER | pass, through ball, one-two | 5 passes to moving teammates; 2 through balls; 1 one-two |\n1564\t| 3 | `shooting` | HIT THE TARGET | power, aim, the sweet spot, curl, chip | hit the 4 corner targets; 1 Screamer; curl one round a dummy; chip the keeper |\n1565\t| 4 | `air` | HEADS UP | lobs, crosses, headers, volleys, bicycle | cross from the wing; score a header; score a volley; bonus: a bicycle kick |\n1566\t| 5 | `skills` | SHOW BOAT | step-over, nutmeg, spin, rainbow, knock-on | beat 4 dummies, one with each move |\n1567\t| 6 | `defending` | THE HARBOUR WALL | poke, slide, barge, switching, interceptions | win the ball 3 times without fouling; switch to the free man; intercept 2 passes |\n1568\t| 7 | `setpieces` | DEAD BALLS | corners, free kicks, penalties, keeping in penalties | score from a corner; bend a free kick over the wall; score a penalty; save a penalty |\n1569\t| 8 | `euphoria` | FEED THE CROWD | Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strike, Save Duel | fill the gauge with tricks and passes; trigger Europhoria; score a Super Strike; win a Save Duel |\n1570\t| 9 | `theatrics` | THE DARK ARTS | dives and the referee | win a foul with a dive after contact; get booked for a dive with nobody near (it's on purpose: \"now you know\") |\n1571\t\n1572\t### 7.7 Matchday events\n1573\t\n1574\t§6.20 lists the 6 events and their stadiums. Each has 3 or more commentary lines and its own sound.\n1575\t\n1576\t### 7.8 Chants and songs\n1577\t\n1578\t- KIPPERTON: \"KIP-PER-TON!\" (G4 G4 C5), 3 claps, repeated; then \"WE'RE GOING UP THE COAST\" on the anthem's first\n1579\t  phrase.\n1580\t- HOOFINGTON: a long low \"HOOOOOF!\" (G2 sliding up to C3) on each long ball.\n1581\t- PASAPASA: \"O-LÉ!\" (E5 C5), one per pass of a chain; handkerchiefs.\n1582\t- STAHLPRESSE: drum `k . k . k k k .` and \"HEY! HEY! HEY!\" (A4 A4 A4).\n1583\t- LUCCHETTO: a slow minor hum (A3 C4 E4 D4 C4), the curva drum.\n1584\t- OPULENCE: polite golf claps, and a brass band playing 4 bars of the anthem out of tune (detuned +30 cents).\n1585\t- Song sketches: Appendix D.\n1586\t\n1587\t---\n1588\t\n1589\t## 8. Art and animation\n1590\t\n1591\t### 8.1 The look\n1592\t\n1593\t- The engine's native style, at its best (the API card's Look target): `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`; HD Humanoid rigs\n1594\t  with real palettes from `E.tones`; textured floors; props on every screen; lights in every scene; title fonts with\n1595\t  extrusion; effects on every hit.\n1596\t- **Players:** `E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, build: 'heroic' | 'bulky' | 'chibi', size: 1.08–1.25 (the boss keeper 2.0),\n1597\t  hair, sleeves: 'short', colors, kit })`. The `cap` hat only for Mags; a `band` (headband) for a few players.\n1598\t  Keepers: their own kit colours and `glove`. The referee: black, with yellow trim. Shaded with `E.tones`; outlines on.\n1599\t  At the default zoom 1.25, players are about 28 px tall.\n1600\t- **The pitch:** mown stripes 32 wide (alternating light and dark), grain noise, worn patches (the goalmouths and the\n1601\t  centre circle by stadium), painted lines, mud and snow and puddles by tag, and a wet sheen (lighter dither in rain).\n1602\t- **Readability:** the ball always has a shadow (smaller and fainter with height, as the kit does); humans have colour\n1603\t  tags; the radar uses shapes as well as colours; text over the pitch has outlines.\n1604\t- **Budget:** TASK.md treats performance as unlimited. Add the detail, fans, effects, lights and shadows each scene\n1605\t  needs. Do not spend time on frame-rate targets or optimisation.\n1606\t\n1607\t### 8.2 Assets to make (new) and to take (library)\n1608\t\n1609\tNew, made in code for this game:\n1610\t- **Goals:** posts and bar (2-px white bars), side and back nets (the dithered mesh with ripple), the net floor shadow.\n1611\t- **Corner flags:** a pole and a 3-frame waving flag (`E.anim`) in the home colours.\n1612\t- **Floodlight pylons:** a custom shape: a lattice tower (lines), a lamp bank (glow material), a light cone (§6.19).\n1613\t- **Stands:** TileMap tiers with seat-row textures (the floor texture on the tier tops in the stadium's seat colours);\n1614\t  roofs (corrugated, a truss, the dome's ribs) drawn as `r.queue` polygons; vomitories (dark gaps) every 8 tiles.\n1615\t- **Ad boards:** the far boards' faces show scrolling LED text (sponsors; \"GOAL!\" after goals; team colours at\n1616\t  Europhoria).\n1617\t- **Jumbotron** (the Euphorium): a frame and a screen showing the score, the crest, \"REPLAY\" and \"GOAL!\" animations.\n1618\t- **Dugouts, the fourth official's LED board, photographers with flashing cameras** (south apron).\n1619\t- **Crests:** a painter for shapes (shield, roundel, circle), fields, rings, and charges (kipper, anchor, boot, sun,\n1620\t  arrows, cog, hammer, padlock, laurel, crown, coins), drawn at 12, 24 and 64 px.\n1621\t- **Balls:** 4-frame sprites for Classic, Winter Orange, Golden and Old Leather; super-strike variants (the smoked\n1622\t  kipper shape, a golden glow).\n1623\t- **Cards, the whistle, the coin, a kipper (the fish-slap prop), a pie** (half-time jokes), sprites.\n1624\t- **The team bus** (Lucchetto livery), **the trawler-on-wheels** (the parade), **the minibus \"The Old Trout\"** (the\n1625\t  travel map), **the podium**, **the Europhoria Cup** (a big-eared silver cup on a plinth: a shape of turned profiles,\n1626\t  metal material).\n1627\t- **Tifos:** one per team, a large banner painted by code over a stand section (the crest and a slogan: \"KIPPER ARMY\",\n1628\t  \"OLÉ OLÉ\", \"STAHL!\", \"LA CHIAVE SIAMO NOI\", \"MONEY TALKS\").\n1629\t- **Fans:** the sprite fans (§6.18); the mascots (Kipper Keith: a Humanoid with a fish-head sprite over his head\n1630\t  joint; the Steel Stag: a stag head with antlers); stewards in hi-vis.\n1631\t- **The tabloid page, the travel map, the bracket cards, the sticker frames:** UI art in code.\n1632\t- **Weather and pyro overlays:** fog layers, flare smoke, confetti, fireworks (particles).\n1633\t\n1634\tFrom the engine's library (generic props, `node tools/asset-find.mjs`): benches (`bench`, `kenney-holiday:bench`) for\n1635\tthe dugouts and the training ground; `lamppost` and `kenney-graveyard:lightpost-double` on the harbour road; `fence`\n1636\tand `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge` at the rec ground; `kenney-holiday:snowman` outside the Stahlpresse Arena;\n1637\t`kenney-fantasy-town:stall-red` market stalls (the pie stand, the Kipperton harbour); `kenney-pirate:flag` on the\n1638\ttrawler; palms (`r.prop('palm')`) at Solera; `crate`, `barrel` and `sign` at the harbour. Load an asset set with its\n1639\tscript before `game.js` and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-holiday'])`, or cut the few entries the game uses into\n1640\ta set of its own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`.\n1641\t\n1642\t### 8.3 Animation\n1643\t\n1644\tThree sources, all on the engine's Humanoid rig: (a) the engine's own animation (gait from velocity, `E.MOVES`-style\n1645\tattack specs, poses, expressions); (b) mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (set `rig.mocap` each step,\n1646\t`rig.mocapW` to fade, `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` for the arms over the legs); (c) procedural recipes: the tilt state\n1647\t(§5.3) and joint post-processing (wrap `rig.solvePose`, as the API card shows).\n1648\t\n1649\t**Cut the clip set** (run in the scratch clone of the engine repository):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"31e327b0-1f44-4704-a047-9d531d413819","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:06.489Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":"| 1 | ALF STOPPARD | GK | long kicks only |\n| 3 | GAZ HOOPER | DEF | heads everything |\n| 5 | DUNCAN DUNSTABLE | DEF | bulky; weight 92 |\n| 8 | KEV LUMP | MID | \"Lump it!\" |\n| 9 | NORMAN \"THE NODDER\" NEEDHAM (captain) | FWD | headers 95; super **ROW Z RETURN** (`meteor`: a hoof into the sky that comes down onto the goal) |\n\n**REAL PASAPASA** — \"Los Pasitos\", RPP (Round of 16). White `#f4f2ec` with lilac `#9a7ad0` trim; away lilac. Crest: a\nsun over two arrows passing. Formation 1-2-1. Tactic `keepball` (shortBias .9, passRisk .2, tempo .85, press .55,\ndribble .25). Chant: \"OLÉ!\" rising with every pass; white handkerchiefs waved. Celebration: the corner-flag dance.\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PACO PORTERO | GK | |\n| 4 | RAFA RONDO | DEF | |\n| 6 | TITO TOQUE | MID | one touch, always |\n| 8 | IKER INTERIOR | MID | |\n| 10 | PEPITO PASARELA (captain) | MID | chibi build 1.0 (tiny); super **EL PASODOBLE** (`zigzag`: the ball dances 3 steps in rhythm) |\n\n**SV STAHLPRESSE 04** — \"Die Pressen\", SVS (Quarter-final). Steel grey `#6a7078` and hazard orange `#ff7a1a` halves.\nCrest: a cog with a hammer. Formation 1-2-1, high line. Tactic `gegenpress` (press .9, pressers 2, line .7, tempo 1,\nstamina use high). Chant: a drum and \"HEY! HEY! HEY!\". Celebration: the robot.\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | MANNI MAUER | GK | |\n| 2 | FRANZI FLEISS | DEF | never stops running |\n| 5 | UWE UMSCHALT | MID | transitions |\n| 7 | JURGEN JAGD (JÜRGEN once §5.5 lands) | FWD | the hunter |\n| 9 | KLAUS HAMMERSCHMIDT (captain) | FWD | bulky 1.25; super **DER HAMMERSCHLAG** (`hammer`: 3 forge-hammer bounces, each shaking the screen) |\n\n**AC LUCCHETTO** — \"I Lucchetti\", the Padlocks, ACL (Semi-final). Burgundy `#7a1a2a` with silver `#c8ccd4`; away silver.\nCrest: a padlock in a laurel wreath. Formation 2-1-1 played deep, switching to 3-1 (the MID drops into the back line)\nwhen they lead after 60', which is also when the bus arrives. Tactic `catenaccio` (line .15, press .3, foul .6, dive .5,\nlongBall .35 on the counter). Chant: a slow minor hum and a curva drum; flares. Celebration: the badge kiss.\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | ROCCO RIPARO | GK | |\n| 3 | DINO DIFESA | DEF | |\n| 5 | MARCO MARCATURA | DEF | man-marks your best player |\n| 7 | FABIO FALLO | MID | the diver (temper 90): goes down in the box at the first touch |\n| 10 | SALVATORE SERRATURA (captain) | FWD | the lone counter-attacker; super **LA CHIAVE** (the key; `around`: it curves round every body in its way) |\n\n**OLYMPIQUE OPULENCE** — \"Les Milliardaires\", OPU (Final; the boss team). Gold `#e8c040` and black `#141414`\nstripes. Crest: a crown on a stack of coins. Formation 1-2-1, attacking. Tactic `galacticos`. Owner: BARON VON\nBULLION. Chant: polite golf claps (they're paid to be there) and a hired brass band. Celebration: the helicopter.\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | GUNNAR \"THE VAULT\" VAULT | GK | **the boss keeper**: bulky, size 2.0, reach +40%, catches anything under 300 |\n| 4 | CASPIAN CASH | DEF | |\n| 8 | BENTLEY BLING | MID | skill 90 |\n| 11 | SERGEI SOVEREIGN | FWD | pace 96 |\n| 10 | MAXIMILIEN D'OR (captain) | FWD | vain superstar; Golden Moment (§6.13); super **LA BOTTE D'OR** (`split`: 3 golden balls, one real) |\n\n**Referees** (registry `referee`): ARTHUR HALTWHISTLE (strictness 1.3, gullibility .2; the qualifying round and the\nfinal: \"the best in Europe\"), PIERRE PATIENCE (.7, .5; round of 16), INGRID IRONSIDE (1.1, .3; quarter-final),\nSERGIO SEVERO (1.2, .7, varHappy .9; semi-final: dramatic, falls for everything, loves VAR). Kick-About picks one at\nrandom.\n\n**Formations** (registry `formation`; `u, v` as in §6.13; `drop` is the role a red card removes):\n\n| Id | Roles and base spots `[u, v]` | drop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `2-2` | GK [.03,.5]; DEFL [.22,.3]; DEFR [.22,.7]; FWDL [.60,.32]; FWDR [.60,.68] | FWDR |\n| `1-2-1` | GK; DEF [.22,.5]; MIDL [.42,.28]; MIDR [.42,.72]; FWD [.64,.5] | MIDR |\n| `2-1-1` | GK; DEFL [.22,.32]; DEFR [.22,.68]; MID [.45,.5]; FWD [.68,.5] | MID |\n| `3-1` | GK; DEFL [.16,.25]; DEF [.13,.5]; DEFR [.16,.75]; FWD [.55,.5] | DEFL |\n\nEach role also gets `att`, `def`, `pull` and `uRange`. Defenders: att [+.14, 0], def [0, 0], pull [.45, .55], uRange\n[.08, .62]. Midfielders: att [+.12, ±.06 outward], def [−.12, ∓.04], pull [.55, .45], uRange [.15, .85]. Forwards:\natt [+.18, 0], def [−.12, 0], pull [.5, .6], uRange [.35, .95]. Tune them by watching AI-versus-AI matches with the AI\noverlay on (§6.30).\n\n### 7.2 Stadiums\n\n| Id | Name, city | Time / weather | Pitch | Stands and skyline | Crowd | Events |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `smokehouse` | THE SMOKEHOUSE, Kipperton | dusk → night, rain .7, wind .4 | wet, mud in the goalmouths, 6 puddles, worn centre | a small main stand with a corrugated roof (3 tiers), terraces with fishing nets behind each goal (2 tiers); skyline: smokehouse chimneys trailing smoke, the harbour, a lighthouse with a sweeping beam, gulls | 600, 80% home (tangerine and navy), a brass band | seagull, floodlight flicker, Kipper Keith |\n| `pasapasa` | ESTADIO PASAPASA, Solera | sunny afternoon | hard and dry (friction .8), perfect stripes | a white-walled bowl (5 tiers) with terracotta roofs; skyline: palms, a cathedral dome, hills | 1,400, white handkerchiefs | beach ball |\n| `stahlpresse` | STAHLPRESSE ARENA, Eisenhutte | night, snow .6 | snow, lines brushed clear, orange ball | a steep steel arena (5 tiers) under a roof truss; skyline: steelworks chimneys with glowing furnaces, steam, snowy mountains | 1,600, a scarf wall, drums | Steel Stag pitch invader, floodlight flicker |\n| `lucchetto` | STADIO LUCCHETTO, Castelfortezza | dusk → night; fog from the 2nd half | grass, a little uneven (random small deflections) | an old bowl (4 tiers) with a steep curva end; skyline: medieval walls, a bell tower, cypress trees | 1,200, flares, the curva drum | flare smoke |\n| `euphorium` | THE EUPHORIUM, Aurelia | night, clear | perfect | a huge golden dome stadium (6 tiers), LED rings, a jumbotron above the north stand; skyline: the dome's ribs, searchlights, lasers | 1,600, mixed, confetti cannons | drone, fireworks |\n| `rec` | KIPPERTON REC (training) | overcast morning | patchy | no stands: a fence, a few parents on a bench, the sea wall; cones, dummies, rebound boards | 8 | none |\n\nEach stadium also lists: its board sponsor texts (fictional and funny: \"SMOKY JOE'S KIPPERS\", \"GULL INSURANCE: WE\nCOVER EVERYTHING\", \"PIE-O-MATIC\", \"EUROPHORIA COLA\", \"BULLION BANK: MONEY TALKS\", \"STAHLPRESSE: WE PRESS HARDER\",\n\"CASTELFORTEZZA LOCKSMITHS\"), its light setup, its floor palette and its music override.\n\n### 7.3 The story (Cup Run beats)\n\nThe premise: the Continental Federation meant to invite KINGSBRIDGE ALBION to the EUROPHORIA CUP, Europe's grandest\nknockout competition. A clerk typed KIPPERTON instead, and the rules say an invitation is an invitation. Kipperton\nAthletic (population 3,112; floodlights powered by fish oil; fourteen pounds in the kitty) are going to Europe in a\nminibus with three good tyres.\n\n**Prologue** (`prologue`)\n- Tabloid, THE DAILY ROAR: **\"FISH OUT OF WATER!\"** — \"Typo sends tiny Kipperton into the Europhoria Cup. 'Rules are\n  rules,' shrugs the Federation.\"\n- Talk at the Smokehouse:\n  - MAGS: \"Right, you lot. Fourteen quid in the kitty, a minibus with three good tyres, and a letter that says EUROPE.\"\n  - DAZ: \"Gaffer, do they have chips in Europe?\"\n  - MAGS: \"They have EVERYTHING in Europe, Darren. Including teams that'll eat us for breakfast.\"\n  - SANDRA: \"Let 'em try. I've got an appetite and all.\"\n  - MAGS: \"That's the spirit. First up, at home: AFC Hoofington. Route-one merchants. Keep your heads up. Literally.\"\n  - Choice: [ \"LET'S PLAY\" ] / [ \"TRAINING FIRST\" ] (the second goes to Training, then back to the cup).\n\n**Qualifying Round** — vs AFC Hoofington at the Smokehouse (rain, dusk). Referee Haltwhistle.\n- Pre: **\"THE LONG AND THE SHORT OF IT\"** — \"Hoofington's aerial bombardment heads for Kipperton's puddles.\"\n- NEEDHAM (on a portrait card): \"We don't pass, love. We 'oof.\"\n- Challenge: **Score a header.**\n- Win: **\"KIP KIP HOORAY!\"**; loss: **\"BATTERED!\"**\n- After: MAGS: \"Not bad. Not good. But not bad.\" TREV (a commentary card): \"A proper cold night, and they've warmed it up.\"\n\n**Round of 16** — vs Real Pasapasa at Estadio Pasapasa (sun). Referee Patience.\n- Travel: the minibus heads south, with a postcard: \"WISH YOU WERE HERE (IT'S HOT)\".\n- Pre: **\"PASS THE PARCEL\"** — \"Kippers must stop the passing masters... if they can find the ball.\"\n- PEPITO: \"You will chase the ball until you are dizzy, little fishes.\"\n- Challenge: **Win the ball back 5 times.**\n- Win: **\"SOLE-DESTROYING FOR SOLERA!\"**; loss: **\"PASSED OUT\"**\n- After: AGGIE: \"I counted. They made 412 passes.\" MAGS: \"And we made two goals. Football's a funny old game.\"\n\n**Quarter-final** — vs SV Stahlpresse 04 at the Stahlpresse Arena (night, snow). Referee Ironside.\n- Travel: snow chains on the minibus; the map turns white.\n- Pre: **\"PRESSED FOR TIME\"** — \"The Steel Machine never stops running. Kipperton's bus barely starts.\"\n- KLAUS: \"We run. You run. We run more.\"\n- Challenge: **Nutmeg an opponent.**\n- Win: **\"KIPPERS MELT THE STEEL!\"**; loss: **\"CRUSHED\"**\n- After: TOMMY: \"Did you see his face when it went through his legs?\" SANDRA: \"Did you see mine? Frozen solid.\"\n\n**Semi-final** — vs AC Lucchetto at Stadio Lucchetto (dusk, then fog). Referee Severo.\n- Pre: **\"PADLOCK AND KEY\"** — \"Can Kipperton crack Europe's meanest defence? Locksmiths on standby.\"\n- SALVATORE: \"Nobody scores against Lucchetto. Nobody. We lock the door and we eat the key.\"\n- MAGS (before the match): \"They'll dive, they'll moan, and if they go ahead they'll park the bus. Don't fall for any\n  of it.\"\n- Challenge: **Score from a free kick.**\n- Win: **\"THEY PARKED THE BUS — WE STOLE IT!\"**; loss: **\"LOCKED OUT\"**\n\n**Before the final** (`villain`) — a hotel lobby, night.\n- BARON VON BULLION: \"Mister Pilchard. Fifty million. A gold-plated jet ski. And all the caviar you can eat.\"\n- Choice: [ \"I'M A KIPPER, MATE. ALWAYS.\" ] → flag `loyal`: the final starts with Euphoria +20 and the sticker LOYAL\n  KIPPER. / [ \"...DOES THE JET SKI COME IN ORANGE?\" ] → DAZ: \"Only joking, Gaffer! Kipper till I die.\" MAGS: \"You\n  nearly gave me a heart attack.\" (Euphoria +10.)\n\n**Final** — vs Olympique Opulence at the Euphorium (night, fireworks). Referee Haltwhistle.\n- Pre: **\"DAVID VS GOLDIATH\"** — \"Fish-oil floodlights meet the richest club on Earth.\"\n- MAXIMILIEN: \"I have three Golden Boots. You have... boots.\"\n- Challenge: **Score a Super Strike.**\n- Win: the ending (§6.24): the ceremony; the parade; **\"THE PLAICE TO BE: KIPPERS ARE KINGS OF EUROPE!\"**; an epilogue\n  line: \"Kingsbridge Albion have demanded a recount.\" Credits.\n- Loss: **\"SO CLOSE! Golden boys break Kipper hearts\"**, then CONTINUE? (retry the final).\n\n**Team talks** (registry `teamtalk`; MAGS says one line from a pool of 3 for each):\n- **HAIRDRYER** (\"Get out there and TERRIFY them!\"): +10% speed and tackle strength for the first 15 game minutes; the\n  referee's strictness +20%.\n- **ARM ROUND THE SHOULDER** (\"Just enjoy it. Your mum's watching.\"): stamina regen +25% for the match; Euphoria starts\n  at +15.\n- **TACTICS BOARD** (\"Here's the plan.\"): pick the formation (2-2 / 1-2-1 / 2-1-1); pass accuracy +10%.\n\n**Gaffer's Challenges** (registry `challenge`): the 5 above. Each is an event condition (for example `header` events\nwith `goal` within 0.5 s by a Kipperton player). Completing one shows a toast during the match, gives a shiny sticker\nafterwards, and all 5 unlock the Old Leather ball.\n\n### 7.4 Commentary pools\n\nWrite at least **300 lines** in total, at least **12 per major event** (goal, shot saved, near miss and woodwork,\ntackle, foul, card, dive, super strike, Save Duel, skill move, header and volley, kickoff, half time, full time,\nweather, matchday events, VAR, penalty, shootout), with banter pairs (`reply`) in about a third of them. Write\noriginal lines only: no famous real commentary quotes. Samples to set the voice:\n\n- **kickoff:** BARRY \"And we're underway at {$stadium}! Lovely evening for it, Trev.\" / TREV \"It's raining sideways,\n  Barry.\"\n- **goal:** BARRY \"OH, YOU BEAUTY! {$player} has absolutely LEATHERED it!\"; \"GET IN! Back of the net from {$player}!\"\n  / TREV \"Keeper had no chance. None. Nada. Zilch.\"; BARRY \"{$team} lead, and the away end is a washing machine!\"\n- **goal, the Kippers:** BARRY \"OH MY COD! KIPPERTON HAVE SCORED!\"; \"That's a plaice in history for {$player}!\"\n- **near miss:** BARRY \"OHHH! Inches! INCHES!\" / TREV \"He'll see that one in his sleep.\"\n- **woodwork:** BARRY \"DOINK! Off the woodwork!\" / TREV \"You could hear that in the car park.\"\n- **header:** BARRY \"Rises like a salmon! A kipper, actually, but you get the idea.\"\n- **bicycle:** BARRY \"AN OVERHEAD KICK! ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!\" / TREV \"I tried that once. Spent a week in traction.\"\n- **nutmeg:** BARRY \"Through the legs! He'll hear about that in the canteen.\"\n- **slide that launches:** BARRY \"He's taken man, ball, and most of the grass!\" / TREV \"That's a booking in any\n  country.\"\n- **dive:** BARRY \"Oh, he's gone down like a sack of spuds!\" / TREV \"There was more contact at my wedding, Barry.\"\n- **simulation booked:** TREV \"Yellow card for the amateur dramatics. Quite right.\"\n- **card:** BARRY \"The referee reaches for his pocket... and it's YELLOW!\"\n- **VAR:** BARRY \"Here we go. VAR. Put the kettle on.\" / TREV \"Put two on.\"\n- **super strike:** BARRY \"WHAT HAS HE DONE TO THAT BALL?!\" / TREV \"That's not football. That's sorcery.\"\n- **Save Duel perfect:** BARRY \"AND THE KEEPER'S GOT IT! FINGERTIPS! UNBELIEVABLE!\"\n- **the bus:** BARRY \"They've only gone and LITERALLY parked the bus!\" / TREV \"Has it got a ticket?\"\n- **half time:** BARRY \"That's the half-time whistle. Time for a pie, Trev?\" / TREV \"Two pies, Barry.\"\n- **full time, a Kipperton win:** BARRY \"They'll be dancing on the harbour wall in Kipperton tonight!\"\n- **seagull:** BARRY \"And a seagull has taken possession!\" / TREV \"Better first touch than some I've seen.\"\n- **rain:** TREV \"Proper weather, this. Separates the men from the boys. And the boys from their boots.\"\n\nThe PA has 20 lines; tabloids have the headlines in §7.3; each story speaker has 5 or more lines for their beats.\n\n### 7.5 Stickers\n\n51 stickers in the album:\n- 30 players (5 a team, earned by playing them, the Kippers from the start);\n- 6 crests (earned by playing them);\n- 5 stadiums (earned by playing there);\n- 5 shiny Gaffer's Challenges;\n- 5 specials: MAGS MULLIGAN (finish the prologue), KIPPER KEITH (tackle the invader), BARRY & TREV (hear 50 lines),\n  THE BUS (score past it), LOYAL KIPPER (the loyal answer).\n\nEach sticker: `{ id, kind, ref, name, how }`. The album shows \"how\" under a silhouette.\n\n### 7.6 Training drills (registry `drill`)\n\n| # | Id | Title | Teaches | Steps (each with Mags's or Sandra's lines) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `move` | ON YOUR MARKS | run, sprint, stamina | weave through 6 cones; sprint the straight; recover your stamina |\n| 2 | `passing` | PASS MASTER | pass, through ball, one-two | 5 passes to moving teammates; 2 through balls; 1 one-two |\n| 3 | `shooting` | HIT THE TARGET | power, aim, the sweet spot, curl, chip | hit the 4 corner targets; 1 Screamer; curl one round a dummy; chip the keeper |\n| 4 | `air` | HEADS UP | lobs, crosses, headers, volleys, bicycle | cross from the wing; score a header; score a volley; bonus: a bicycle kick |\n| 5 | `skills` | SHOW BOAT | step-over, nutmeg, spin, rainbow, knock-on | beat 4 dummies, one with each move |\n| 6 | `defending` | THE HARBOUR WALL | poke, slide, barge, switching, interceptions | win the ball 3 times without fouling; switch to the free man; intercept 2 passes |\n| 7 | `setpieces` | DEAD BALLS | corners, free kicks, penalties, keeping in penalties | score from a corner; bend a free kick over the wall; score a penalty; save a penalty |\n| 8 | `euphoria` | FEED THE CROWD | Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strike, Save Duel | fill the gauge with tricks and passes; trigger Europhoria; score a Super Strike; win a Save Duel |\n| 9 | `theatrics` | THE DARK ARTS | dives and the referee | win a foul with a dive after contact; get booked for a dive with nobody near (it's on purpose: \"now you know\") |\n\n### 7.7 Matchday events\n\n§6.20 lists the 6 events and their stadiums. Each has 3 or more commentary lines and its own sound.\n\n### 7.8 Chants and songs\n\n- KIPPERTON: \"KIP-PER-TON!\" (G4 G4 C5), 3 claps, repeated; then \"WE'RE GOING UP THE COAST\" on the anthem's first\n  phrase.\n- HOOFINGTON: a long low \"HOOOOOF!\" (G2 sliding up to C3) on each long ball.\n- PASAPASA: \"O-LÉ!\" (E5 C5), one per pass of a chain; handkerchiefs.\n- STAHLPRESSE: drum `k . k . k k k .` and \"HEY! HEY! HEY!\" (A4 A4 A4).\n- LUCCHETTO: a slow minor hum (A3 C4 E4 D4 C4), the curva drum.\n- OPULENCE: polite golf claps, and a brass band playing 4 bars of the anthem out of tune (detuned +30 cents).\n- Song sketches: Appendix D.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art and animation\n\n### 8.1 The look\n\n- The engine's native style, at its best (the API card's Look target): `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`; HD Humanoid rigs\n  with real palettes from `E.tones`; textured floors; props on every screen; lights in every scene; title fonts with\n  extrusion; effects on every hit.\n- **Players:** `E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, build: 'heroic' | 'bulky' | 'chibi', size: 1.08–1.25 (the boss keeper 2.0),\n  hair, sleeves: 'short', colors, kit })`. The `cap` hat only for Mags; a `band` (headband) for a few players.\n  Keepers: their own kit colours and `glove`. The referee: black, with yellow trim. Shaded with `E.tones`; outlines on.\n  At the default zoom 1.25, players are about 28 px tall.\n- **The pitch:** mown stripes 32 wide (alternating light and dark), grain noise, worn patches (the goalmouths and the\n  centre circle by stadium), painted lines, mud and snow and puddles by tag, and a wet sheen (lighter dither in rain).\n- **Readability:** the ball always has a shadow (smaller and fainter with height, as the kit does); humans have colour\n  tags; the radar uses shapes as well as colours; text over the pitch has outlines.\n- **Budget:** TASK.md treats performance as unlimited. Add the detail, fans, effects, lights and shadows each scene\n  needs. Do not spend time on frame-rate targets or optimisation.\n\n### 8.2 Assets to make (new) and to take (library)\n\nNew, made in code for this game:\n- **Goals:** posts and bar (2-px white bars), side and back nets (the dithered mesh with ripple), the net floor shadow.\n- **Corner flags:** a pole and a 3-frame waving flag (`E.anim`) in the home colours.\n- **Floodlight pylons:** a custom shape: a lattice tower (lines), a lamp bank (glow material), a light cone (§6.19).\n- **Stands:** TileMap tiers with seat-row textures (the floor texture on the tier tops in the stadium's seat colours);\n  roofs (corrugated, a truss, the dome's ribs) drawn as `r.queue` polygons; vomitories (dark gaps) every 8 tiles.\n- **Ad boards:** the far boards' faces show scrolling LED text (sponsors; \"GOAL!\" after goals; team colours at\n  Europhoria).\n- **Jumbotron** (the Euphorium): a frame and a screen showing the score, the crest, \"REPLAY\" and \"GOAL!\" animations.\n- **Dugouts, the fourth official's LED board, photographers with flashing cameras** (south apron).\n- **Crests:** a painter for shapes (shield, roundel, circle), fields, rings, and charges (kipper, anchor, boot, sun,\n  arrows, cog, hammer, padlock, laurel, crown, coins), drawn at 12, 24 and 64 px.\n- **Balls:** 4-frame sprites for Classic, Winter Orange, Golden and Old Leather; super-strike variants (the smoked\n  kipper shape, a golden glow).\n- **Cards, the whistle, the coin, a kipper (the fish-slap prop), a pie** (half-time jokes), sprites.\n- **The team bus** (Lucchetto livery), **the trawler-on-wheels** (the parade), **the minibus \"The Old Trout\"** (the\n  travel map), **the podium**, **the Europhoria Cup** (a big-eared silver cup on a plinth: a shape of turned profiles,\n  metal material).\n- **Tifos:** one per team, a large banner painted by code over a stand section (the crest and a slogan: \"KIPPER ARMY\",\n  \"OLÉ OLÉ\", \"STAHL!\", \"LA CHIAVE SIAMO NOI\", \"MONEY TALKS\").\n- **Fans:** the sprite fans (§6.18); the mascots (Kipper Keith: a Humanoid with a fish-head sprite over his head\n  joint; the Steel Stag: a stag head with antlers); stewards in hi-vis.\n- **The tabloid page, the travel map, the bracket cards, the sticker frames:** UI art in code.\n- **Weather and pyro overlays:** fog layers, flare smoke, confetti, fireworks (particles).\n\nFrom the engine's library (generic props, `node tools/asset-find.mjs`): benches (`bench`, `kenney-holiday:bench`) for\nthe dugouts and the training ground; `lamppost` and `kenney-graveyard:lightpost-double` on the harbour road; `fence`\nand `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge` at the rec ground; `kenney-holiday:snowman` outside the Stahlpresse Arena;\n`kenney-fantasy-town:stall-red` market stalls (the pie stand, the Kipperton harbour); `kenney-pirate:flag` on the\ntrawler; palms (`r.prop('palm')`) at Solera; `crate`, `barrel` and `sign` at the harbour. Load an asset set with its\nscript before `game.js` and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-holiday'])`, or cut the few entries the game uses into\na set of its own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`.\n\n### 8.3 Animation\n\nThree sources, all on the engine's Humanoid rig: (a) the engine's own animation (gait from velocity, `E.MOVES`-style\nattack specs, poses, expressions); (b) mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (set `rig.mocap` each step,\n`rig.mocapW` to fade, `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` for the arms over the legs); (c) procedural recipes: the tilt state\n(§5.3) and joint post-processing (wrap `rig.solvePose`, as the API card shows).\n\n**Cut the clip set** (run in the scratch clone of the engine repository):","numLines":300,"startLine":1350,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FWrmvtzPEejKGPZcsAicn2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2pZNMK2zEoqZ5ad1fW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KRgELwmeKJGrTH4AMxoX3J","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1650,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11472,"cache_read_input_tokens":72899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11472},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"d7b54434-a88b-447d-8752-a8e98e0be5a7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:09.694Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2pZ7iptiSycqTqb9Ht","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KRgELwmeKJGrTH4AMxoX3J":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1650,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KRgELwmeKJGrTH4AMxoX3J","type":"tool_result","content":"1650\t\n1651\t```sh\n1652\tnode tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n1653\t  examples/cmu-lib/CMU_10.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_11.js \\\n1654\t  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Roll,Victory,Cheer_One_arm,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dance_Simple,Angry,Backflip,Help_Two_Arms,Death_C,Dodge_left,Dodge_right,Greeting,Cartwheel,Jump_Twist,Breakdance_Helicopter,Shrug,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,Get_Up_From_Side,Run_Quick_Stop,Wave_Hello,10_02,10_05,11_01\" \\\n1655\t  --name EF --title \"Europhoria Football\" --out <dev folder>/mocap/ef-clips.js \\\n1656\t  --credit \"Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0); Mesh2Motion (CC0); CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (mocap.cs.cmu.edu), free for all uses; created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.\"\n1657\t```\n1658\t\n1659\tIf a name is in more than one set, the tool says so: prefix it `SET:`. If a clip's name differs, check the set's\n1660\tcatalog (`src/mocap/catalogs/*.json`) and fix the list. Expect about 150–250 KB. The CMU soccer takes play only a\n1661\twindow around the kick: find the contact time once (the frame where the right foot's forward reach peaks), store it in\n1662\t`EF.Anim.CLIPS`, and sample from `contact − 0.45 s` to `contact + 0.35 s`.\n1663\t\n1664\t| Moment | Source | How |\n1665\t|---|---|---|\n1666\t| idle, jog, run, sprint | engine | the gait from velocity; `sprint: true` adds the lean |\n1667\t| dribble touch | engine spec | `touch: { rel, kick: true, a0: .2, a1: 0, z0: .08, z1: .12, reach: 4, wind: .03, active: .04, recover: .08 }` every stride |\n1668\t| pass | engine spec | `pass: { rel, kick: true, a0: .6, a1: -.1, z0: .15, z1: .2, reach: 6, wind: .08, active: .08, recover: .16, twist: .4 }` (inside foot) |\n1669\t| shot | spec, plus mocap for power ≥ .8 | `shot: { rel, kick: true, a0: .05, a1: 0, z0: .3, z1: 1.1, reach: 7, wind: .12, active: .1, recover: .26, lean: -.25, lunge: 2 }`; at high power blend `10_02`'s kick window in over the spec (`mocapW` 1, then fading to 0 in the recovery) |\n1670\t| penalty run-up and kick | mocap | `11_01` (the run-up and kick), with root motion supplied by the body |\n1671\t| chip / lob | spec | `chip: { a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: 1.4, reach: 5.5, lean: -.4 }` |\n1672\t| volley | spec | `volley: { a0: .4, a1: -.2, z0: .9, z1: 1.2, reach: 7, hop: 2, lean: -.4, twist: .6 }` |\n1673\t| header | procedural | `air: true` with a z arc; tilt forward 20° (axis `right`); the head snaps forward at contact (post-process `J.head`) |\n1674\t| diving header | procedural | tilt +75° about `right` (pivot hips, lift 6), arms back; lands with `down` 0.5 s; up with `Get_Up_Face_Down` |\n1675\t| bicycle kick | procedural | tilt −140° about `right` (pivot hips, lift up to 14 at contact), with `axekick`-style kick: `{ kick: true, a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: 2.2, z1: 1.5, reach: 6 }`; lands on the back (`down`); up with `Get_Up_From_Back` |\n1676\t| slide tackle | mocap | `Slide_Start` → `Slide_Loop` → `Slide_Exit` (the body supplies the travel) |\n1677\t| poke tackle | spec | `poke: { kick: true, a0: .3, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: .1, reach: 7.5, lunge: 3, wind: .05, active: .08, recover: .15 }` |\n1678\t| barge | engine move | `bash`, with a lean |\n1679\t| launched by a slide | procedural | tilt about `forward` spinning 1.5 turns over 0.6 s while the body flies (vz 120), stars; then `down: 1`; up with `LayToIdle` or `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n1680\t| knocked back | mocap | `Hit_Knockback`, then `LayToIdle` |\n1681\t| wrong-footed | mocap | `Dodge_left` / `Dodge_right` at `mocapW` .7, with `hurt` |\n1682\t| step-over | spec | two quick `kick` specs sweeping across the ball (`a0` from ±.9 to ∓.3), 0.15 s apart |\n1683\t| spin turn | engine | `rig.spin` from 0 to 2π over 0.45 s |\n1684\t| rainbow flick | spec | heel flick: `{ kick: true, a0: 3.0, a1: 2.6, z0: .1, z1: 1.3, reach: 4 }` (behind, upward) |\n1685\t| skid stop | mocap | `Run_Quick_Stop` (upper body, `mocapMask: 'upper'`) on hard stops |\n1686\t| theatrical dive | procedural + mocap | launch forward (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 8), land, 2 sideways rolls (tilt about `forward` spinning 2 turns while sliding 30), lie clutching a shin (`down: 1`, `expr: 'wince'`, hands to `J.kneeR`); if booked, up with `Shrug` |\n1687\t| protests | mocap | `Angry`, `Help_Two_Arms`, `Shrug` (upper) |\n1688\t| tired | procedural | lean 30°, hands to the knees (post-process `J.handL`/`J.handR` toward `J.kneeL`/`J.kneeR`) at stoppages when stamina is under 25 |\n1689\t| keeper set | engine | `pose: 'guard'`, crouch .3 |\n1690\t| keeper dive | procedural | tilt ±(70–95)° about `forward` (pivot feet), lifted 2 (low) to 14 (high) on an arc; lateral speed 260 easing to 0; hands IK'd (`E.ik3`) to the ball's point; then `down` on the side; up with `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n1691\t| keeper catch / parry / tip | procedural / engine | hands to the chest (catch); `jab` toward the ball (parry); one arm up with a jump (tip) |\n1692\t| keeper throw | mocap | `OverhandThrow`; an underarm roll as a spec with the arm low |\n1693\t| smother | procedural | a low forward dive (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 2) |\n1694\t| celebrations | mocap + procedural | knee slide: `Slide_Loop` with arms out (post-process); `Backflip`; `Cartwheel`; aeroplane: run with the arms horizontal (post-process) and a lean into the turn; robot: `Dance_Simple` at 0.6× speed with the arms bent square (post-process); shirt over head: `hood: true` with the hood in the shirt colour plus `Cheering_Two_Hands`; corner-flag dance: `Dance_Simple`; badge kiss: `Greeting`; helicopter: `Breakdance_Helicopter`; fish slap: two players face each other, alternating `jab` with a kipper sprite in the hand; pile-on: teammates `Victory` / `Cheer_One_arm` |\n1695\t| referee | engine + procedural | whistle (hand to mouth), points to the spot (`point: true`), the card raised high (hand above the head; the card sprite at `rig.hand('R')`), advantage (both arms forward), the VAR rectangle (both hands trace a box), hand to the ear; knocked over by the ball (`Fall_On_Face`, then up) |\n1696\t| manager | mocap | pacing (gait), `Angry` (conceding), `Victory` (scoring), `Help_Two_Arms` (instructions), `Cheering_Two_Hands` |\n1697\t| tunnel and handshakes | engine + procedural | a walk; an arm forward (`point: true`) as the lines pass |\n1698\t| crowd front rows | engine | classic-style rigs with `pose: 'cheer'`, `wave`, arms down for boos |\n1699\t\n1700\tCheck every attack and every procedural move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (§11.7): a wind-up, a strike, and a settle\n1701\twithout jerks or backward sweeps.\n1702\t\n1703\t---\n1704\t\n1705\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1706\t\n1707\tEach milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tools/test.mjs`), the build working, and a short note in the dev\n1708\tfolder's `PROGRESS.md`. Do them in order: each one builds on the last, and the risky parts come early.\n1709\t\n1710\t**M0 — Setup (½ day).** The dev folder; the engine copied; `vendor/` filled; `package.json`; `tools/build.mjs`\n1711\tproducing `build/game.js`, the dev page and the deliverable; `tools/test.mjs` with its vm loader and one smoke test;\n1712\tthe SPORTS kit's game (`kits/sports.js`) copied in as a single first fragment (its own IIFE wrapper removed, since the\n1713\tbuild adds one) and running through the pipeline (proof: its `run(600)` hash is the same twice). From M1 on it is\n1714\treplaced, piece by piece, by the fragments of §4.2.\n1715\t*Done when:* `node tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs` passes, and `node tools/check.mjs` on the deliverable shows\n1716\tthe kit's cage match.\n1717\t\n1718\t**M1 — The football sandbox (the feel).** The broadcast view; the pitch geometry and TileMap (§6.1); the ball (§6.2);\n1719\t5-a-side footballers with movement, stamina and dribbling (§6.3); pass, through, lob, one-two (§6.4); shooting with\n1720\tthe meter, sweet spot, aim, curl and chip (§6.5, without air moves); possession; goals; kickoffs; a temporary formation\n1721\tAI (the kit's, widened to 5); the camera director (§6.14); the score bug and power meter; `EF.T` with the TUNE tab only\n1722\t(a minimal dev panel); the Intent architecture with `HumanController`, `BotController` and `ScriptController`.\n1723\t*Done when:* a human can play a goal-scoring match against the CPU that already feels good; the physics unit tests\n1724\tpass (§11.3).\n1725\t\n1726\t**M2 — Characters and animation (risky; early).** Engine changes §5.2 (kit patterns) and §5.3 (tilt); the clip set\n1727\tcut and loaded; every animation row of §8.3 for outfield players and keepers; kits for all 6 teams.\n1728\t*Done when:* filmstrips of the pass, the shot, the slide, the launched victim, the keeper's low and high dives, the\n1729\theader, the bicycle kick, the dive and 3 celebrations look right (§11.7).\n1730\t\n1731\t**M3 — The rest of football.** Air moves (§6.5), skill moves (§6.6), defending (§6.7), keepers in full (§6.8), the\n1732\trules machine (§6.12: the clock, stoppage, halves, extra time, the shootout), set pieces (§6.11), the referee, fouls,\n1733\tadvantage, cards, theatrics and VAR (§6.10).\n1734\t*Done when:* the rules and set-piece tests pass, and an AI-versus-AI match produces corners, free kicks, cards and\n1735\tpenalties.\n1736\t\n1737\t**M4 — Team AI and balance.** TeamBrains with formations, tactics and gimmicks (§6.13, §7.1); difficulty; the AI overlay\n1738\tin dev mode; the soak test (§11.4) tuned to its targets.\n1739\t*Done when:* 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches per tactic pair meet the soak targets.\n1740\t\n1741\t**M5 — The over-the-top layer.** Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes (all 7 paths), the Save Duel (§6.9); the bus;\n1742\tcelebrations (§6.21); cinematics.\n1743\t*Done when:* every super strike's test passes and the Save Duel's timing windows are exact.\n1744\t\n1745\t**M6 — Presentation.** The 6 stadiums (§7.2) with stands, skylines, lights and weather (§6.19); the crowd view and mood\n1746\t(§6.18); matchday events (§6.20); replays (§6.15); the HUD in full (§6.16); the commentary director and its lines\n1747\t(§6.17, §7.4); audio in full: songs, SFX, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices (§6.22, engine changes §5.1, §5.4,\n1748\t§5.5).\n1749\t*Done when:* screenshots of each stadium at its time of day look right, and the audio smoke test plays without\n1750\terrors.\n1751\t\n1752\t**M7 — Front end and 10-foot UI.** The UI kit (§6.23), glyphs and prompts (§2.3), title, Kick-About setup with the\n1753\tcontroller side picker (§6.27), results, settings integration (§6.31), touch-only (§6.33), About (§6.32).\n1754\t*Done when:* every screen can be used with a pad only, a keyboard only, and a mouse only (scripted UI tests, §11.3).\n1755\t\n1756\t**M8 — The Cup Run.** The beat player and its step kinds, tabloids, the travel map, team talks, challenges, stickers,\n1757\tthe album, saves, the ending with the ceremony, the parade and the credits (§6.24, §7.3, §7.5).\n1758\t*Done when:* the scripted full playthrough passes (§11.5).\n1759\t\n1760\t**M9 — Training and Penalties.** The 9 drills (§6.25, §7.6) and Penalties mode (§6.26).\n1761\t*Done when:* each drill's scripted solve passes.\n1762\t\n1763\t**M10 — Attract and dev mode.** The idle watcher and the attract director (§6.29); dev mode in full (§6.30).\n1764\t*Done when:* the attract tests pass (it starts at 10.0 s, shows every segment, and any input exits) and every WARP\n1765\tentry runs without errors.\n1766\t\n1767\t**M11 — AI Hub online.** §6.28 in full; the fake-hub loopback tests (§11.6), then the real harness in Chromium.\n1768\t*Done when:* `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for 2 players, for 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5,\n1769\tfor the host-leave scenario, and for the server scenario.\n1770\t\n1771\t**M12 — Bundle, polish, hand-back.** The final build; the full test pass; the look notes from `tools/check.mjs` acted\n1772\ton; screenshots reviewed; `exit-interview.json` written and validated; the About pages generated from it; the chat\n1773\treply (§12).\n1774\t\n1775\t---\n1776\t\n1777\t## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1778\t\n1779\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1780\t|---|---|---|\n1781\t| **Football-specific animation** (keeper dives, bicycle kicks, diving headers, dives) | The rig has no such moves; a bad dive ruins the game's look | M2 is early. Build the tilt state first, on one rig, in a test scene (`#dev` with an animation gallery: every move on a loop, every view). Filmstrip each move. Fallbacks: the built-in `flip` roll and `down`, sideways `Dodge_*_RM`, `Dive_Roll` from CMU |\n1782\t| **Kit patterns in the engine's torso painter** | It is drawn code inside the rig | A self-contained change behind `o.kit`; fallback: solid shirts with trim and no numbers (§5.2) |\n1783\t| **AI quality with 10 players** | Bad AI makes matches dull or broken: clumps, stuck players, no shots | A parametric formation model and utility scoring (§6.13), not ad hoc rules; the AI overlay; the soak test with numeric targets (§11.4) from M4 on |\n1784\t| **The feel of ball control** | Sticky ball versus loose ball; passes that miss | Dev sliders from M1; unit tests for pass accuracy; play it often from M1 |\n1785\t| **Netcode under latency and loss** | Shared-world football has a contested ball | Host authority with interpolation, input counters that survive loss, and the rate budget (§6.28, Appendix B). The sim/presentation split is in place from M1. Build a loopback fake hub with latency, jitter and loss in Node first (§11.6), then the real harness |\n1786\t| **Hub protocol details** (the card, ready, server mode, time-up, end) | The hub keeps a game that fails its check out of sessions | Follow the README's checklist line by line; run the harness's automatic check for every scenario it lists (§11.6) |\n1787\t| **Audio synthesis** (the crowd and babble) | WebAudio code is easy to get wrong, and silent in tests | One audio smoke page (`#dev` → sound test: every SFX, song, chant and voice on a list); headless no-ops tested; one screenshot-free check that no audio errors reach `game.errors` |\n1788\t| **Many systems, one IIFE** | Name clashes, load-order bugs | Numbered fragments with one namespace; the content validator; the full playthrough test |\n1789\t| **Scope** | It is a lot of game | Data-driven content; the milestone order puts the core first; each milestone ends playable. The list in §12 is the scope: build all of it, but do the core well before the extras are polished |\n1790\t| **Determinism** (tests and replays) | `Math.random` in sim code breaks proofs | A lint test greps `src/` for `Math.random` outside cosmetic code; the determinism test (§11.4) |\n1791\t| **Bundle correctness** | `</script>` in inlined code; the order of hub metas and `session.js` | The build checks both; a test parses the deliverable's `<head>` order (§11.8) |\n1792\t\n1793\t---\n1794\t\n1795\t## 11. Testing\n1796\t\n1797\t### 11.1 The one command\n1798\t\n1799\t`node tools/test.mjs` runs every suite and prints **only failures** (one line each: `FAIL <suite> <test>: <detail>`) and\n1800\tone last line: `Europhoria tests: <passed> passed, <failed> failed (<seconds> s)`. It exits with 1 on any failure.\n1801\t`node tools/test.mjs <suite> [...]` runs only the named suites, so after a change you rerun only the suites that cover\n1802\tit. The suites: `unit`, `rules`, `ai`, `content`, `ui`, `saves`, `attract`, `dev`, `playthrough`, `determinism`,\n1803\t`hubsim` (Node), then `browser`, `hub` (Playwright; skipped with a note if Chromium is missing). Don't use subagents or\n1804\tworkflows to review or judge anything: the tests and screenshots are the judges.\n1805\t\n1806\t### 11.2 Headless harness\n1807\t\n1808\t`tools/lib/load.mjs` creates a vm context with the stand-ins the kits' test uses (`window` = the context,\n1809\t`addEventListener` as a no-op, `location: { hash, search }`), plus `matchMedia` (returns `{ matches: false,\n1810\taddEventListener() {} }`), `navigator` (`{ maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`), and `performance`. It runs\n1811\t`vendor/session.js` first (in Node it stays inactive: no parent frame), then the engine, the mocap scripts, the clip\n1812\tset and `build/game.js`. It returns `{ E, game, EF, I: game.input, snap: () => game.debug.snapshot() }`.\n1813\t`game.advance(seconds)` steps exactly. `input.tap` and `input.hold` press actions. `EF.test` gives the setup hooks:\n1814\t`startMatch({ home, away, stadium, seed, halfLength, humans })`, `giveBall(side, idx, x, y)`, `place(id, x, y)`,\n1815\t`setEuphoria(side, v)`, `forceShot(...)`, `simUntil(predicate, maxSeconds)`, `cheat(name, on)`.\n1816\t\n1817\t`game.debug.snapshot()` returns `{ scene, part, mode, half, clock, minute, stoppage, score, ball: [x, y, z], owner,\n1818\thumans: [{ p, id, name, x, y, state }], euphoria: [a, b], europhoria, cards, sentOff, setpiece, shootout, stadium,\n1819\tweather, cup: { round, results }, attract: { active, segment, idle }, dev: { open, changed }, hub: { active, role,\n1820\tsent, received }, ui: { screen, focus }, errors: game.errors.length }`. `game.debug.teleport(x, y, z)` moves the\n1821\tcontrolled footballer. Every test also checks that `game.errors` stayed empty.\n1822\t\n1823\t### 11.3 Unit and system tests (Node)\n1824\t\n1825\t- **unit/ball:** a pass at a moving receiver arrives within 8 units of him, for 50 seeded cases; curl turns a shot by\n1826\t  the expected angle, ±10%; bounces off the boards keep within the bounce factor; each post and the bar reflect; the\n1827\t  goal-line test with the ball over the line by r − 1 (no goal) and r + 1 (goal); a ball over the bar gives no goal;\n1828\t  the net stops the ball within 0.5 s; each surface's friction order (mud < snow < grass < hard < wet in rolling\n1829\t  distance, shortest to longest).\n1830\t- **unit/input:** `Input.halfKeys(EF.KEYS, 'left')` puts `pass … dive` on F G H R T Y V B and `'right'` puts them on\n1831\t  . / , L ; ' K M; the `switch` + `skill` chord fires `euphoria` on a half keyboard and on a pad (L1 + R1); Space\n1832\t  fires it on a full keyboard; mouse buttons do nothing while mouse aim is off.\n1833\t- **unit/footballer:** sprint drains and regains stamina at the set rates; turning with the ball slows him; each skill\n1834\t  move's success rule at the probability extremes (with a fixed rng); the air-ball window chooses header, volley,\n1835\t  bicycle or diving header by height and facing; the receiver picked by the stick direction for 8 directions;\n1836\t  pass-assist cones.\n1837\t- **unit/keeper:** save chance falls as shot speed rises and as the target moves to the corners; a catch under 260 well\n1838\t  reached; parries go away from the goal centre; tips over the bar give corners.\n1839\t- **rules:** the corner versus goal kick by last touch; the crowd throw-back side; a foul from behind is a foul and one\n1840\t  from the front with the ball first is not; severities give yellow, red, and a second yellow → red; a sent-off side\n1841\t  plays with 3 and drops the formation's `drop` role; advantage plays on when possession stays; a penalty for a foul in\n1842\t  the box; VAR overturns only soft penalties; the clock maps 2:00 real time to 45 game minutes; stoppage time is within\n1843\t  1–5; extra time is golden goal; the shootout ends early when a side can't catch up and goes to sudden death after 5\n1844\t  each; the shirt-over-head celebration gives a yellow.\n1845\t- **euphoria:** every gain in the table; decay; thresholds; Europhoria lasts 8 s; one super a Europhoria; each super path\n1846\t  reaches the goal mouth from 230 out with no errors (7 cases); Save Duel windows: a press at the target ±59 ms is\n1847\t  PERFECT, ±61 ms is GOOD, ±141 ms is MISS.\n1848\t- **ai:** players reach their formation spots within 1.5 s when the ball is placed (each formation, each phase); the\n1849\t  pressing count matches the tactic; the ball carrier never stands still for more than 2 s; the bus appears for\n1850\t  Lucchetto when leading after 60' and not otherwise; Opulence's Golden Moment fires at 80' when behind or level.\n1851\t- **content:** `EF.validate()` reports nothing; every team has 5 players with one captain and one GK; every captain has\n1852\t  a registered super; every stadium's events exist; every beat's team, stadium and photo exist; every drill's steps\n1853\t  run; every text uses only characters the font can draw; every commentary pool for a major event has at least 12\n1854\t  lines; at least 300 lines in total; every sticker is reachable (its `how` refers to an event that exists).\n1855\t- **ui:** with only pad actions (`input.tap('down')`, `'confirm'`, `'cancel'`) a script can reach every screen from the\n1856\t  title and back. With only the mouse (`input.feed('move', x, y)` and clicks at a widget's centre) every menu item can\n1857\t  be focused by hover and picked by click. The keyboard (`press('ArrowDown')`, `press('Enter')`) does the same.\n1858\t  `EF.prompt` gives PlayStation icons for pad codes by default and Xbox after `game.settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`;\n1859\t  keycaps when `lastDevice` is the keyboard; mouse icons when it is the mouse. Touch-only (`?touchonly=1`): the title\n1860\t  shows the notice and the SETTINGS button, and the play tiles cannot start a match.\n1861\t- **saves:** a write/read round trip; a migration from a v0 shape; CONTINUE resumes at the right round; dev unlocks only\n1862\t  after their confirm.\n1863\t- **attract:** at the title, `advance(9.9)` leaves it on the title; `advance(0.2)` more starts `attract`; during the\n1864\t  attract run every segment shows (snapshot `attract.segment` over 95 s: all 6); `input.tap('confirm')`, a key press, a\n1865\t  mouse move and a pad axis each return to the title, and that press does not pick a menu item.\n1866\t- **dev:** every slider changes `EF.T` and a match responds (for example `runSpeed` 120 → a sprint covers more ground in\n1867\t  1 s); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; every WARP entry runs with no errors; dev mode cannot open when the\n1868\t  fake hub says `active`.\n1869\t\n1870\t### 11.4 Balance soak and determinism\n1871\t\n1872\t- **soak** (part of `ai`, tagged slow; run it after AI changes): 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches at a half length of\n1873\t  60 s, for each of 4 pairings (each tactic once against Kipperton at Normal). Targets per match on average: 2–7 goals,\n1874\t  8–20 shots, 55–85% pass completion, possession 35–65% for each side, at least 1 corner and 1 free kick in 4 matches,\n1875\t  no player stuck (no movement for more than 4 s in play), no ball stuck (not moving and not owned for more than 3 s in\n1876\t  play). It reports the averages, so tuning has numbers to work with.\n1877\t- **determinism:** a scripted match (the kit's `proof()` pattern: a seed, scripted inputs for 1,800 steps) hashed twice\n1878\t  gives the same hash. Then a replay re-run gives the same final state hash as the live run.\n1879\t- **lint:** no `Math.random` in sim files (`10-`..`18-`, `20-`); no `ctx.arc`, `ctx.stroke`, `ctx.fillText` or canvas\n1880\t  gradients on the game buffer; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, `fetch`, `WebSocket` or `RTCPeerConnection`.\n1881\t\n1882\t### 11.5 The scripted playthrough (the whole game)\n1883\t\n1884\t`playthrough` runs the whole game headless, as a player would, through the real scenes and the real input. It drives\n1885\tthe human with a **bot**: the kit's approach (`SPORTS.bot()`) of asking the CPU brain what it would do and giving\n1886\tthat as the stick and buttons, plus scripted forcing where a beat needs it. Half length 30 s; difficulty Easy; the\n1887\t\"Euphoria always full\" cheat is off.\n1888\t\n1889\t1. The title, then CUP RUN, NEW CUP RUN; the prologue's beats are advanced with `confirm`; LET'S PLAY.\n1890\t2. For each round: the bracket, the tabloid, the travel map, the talk, a team talk (cycling the 3 kinds over the\n1891\t   rounds), the challenge card, the tunnel. Then the match, played by the bot to the final whistle. If the bot loses or\n1892\t   draws, `EF.test` grants a win through the real path: it plays on with the \"Euphoria always full\" and \"invincible\n1893\t   keeper\" cheats, and records that it did so. Then the results, stickers, the autosave, and the post-match beats.\n1894\t3. The semi-final must show the bus at least once (forced: a Lucchetto lead after 60' by the dev goal cheat). The\n1895\t   villain beat takes the loyal choice.\n1896\t4. The final, then the ending: the ceremony, the parade, the tabloid, the credits, then the title.\n1897\t5. Then: CONTINUE is gone or points to a finished cup; the album shows the earned stickers; Kick-About with 2 local\n1898\t   players (one on each side) plays 20 s; PENALTIES plays a full shootout; TRAINING solves drill 1 by script; ABOUT\n1899\t   pages through to the end; the attract mode starts after 10 s idle and exits on a key.\n1900\t6. Checks along the way: the snapshot's scene at every step; no errors; the save after each round; each round's\n1901\t   challenge events seen; at least one corner, one free kick, one card, one super strike and one replay over the run.\n1902\t\n1903\tTarget time: under 2 minutes headless. It is the slowest suite, so run it after changes to flow, scenes, the cup, saves\n1904\tor content.\n1905\t\n1906\t### 11.6 Online tests\n1907\t\n1908\t- **hubsim (Node):** a fake hub (`tools/lib/fakehub.mjs`) implements the client API (`connect`, `ready`, `answer`, `on`,\n1909\t  `send`, `time`, `finish`, `progress`, `rng`, `active`, `isHost`, `server`, `players`) between 2–4 vm contexts, with a\n1910\t  network of set latency, jitter and loss. It steps all copies in lockstep with `game.advance`. Checks: each copy reaches\n1911\t  the card with no key press and calls `ready()`; `answer('ready')` on Enter; the match starts on `start` and play waits\n1912\t  for time ≥ 0; the host's message rate stays at 20/s or under, with bursts under 40, and every message is under 16 KB\n1913\t  (snapshots under 1,100 bytes); with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, a client's drawn ball stays within 24\n1914\t  units of the host's 95% of the time; a press is never lost (counters); a goal on the host shows on every client within\n1915\t  0.5 s; `leave` hands a footballer to the CPU; `time-up` makes the host finish at once; `finish`'s standings put the\n1916\t  winners first and tie a draw; the server mode runs with no local player and draws nothing; on `end`, input, sending and\n1917\t  sound stop; host-left shows ROUND VOID.\n1918\t- **hub (Playwright):** the real harness. Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/harness/`. Start a\n1919\t  server for the **work root**, bound to localhost on a port the OS picks, in the background, and remember its PID:\n1920\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <work root>`. Read the port from its first output line\n1921\t  (\"Serving HTTP on 127.0.0.1 port N\"). Fetch\n1922\t  `http://127.0.0.1:N/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174834.html` and check that its\n1923\t  `<title>` is \"Europhoria Football\" before trusting any result (another process could hold the port). Then open, in\n1924\t  turn:\n1925\t  - `http://127.0.0.1:N/<dev folder>/tools/harness/harness.html?game=/<game>.html&players=2&auto=1`\n1926\t  - `...&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1927\t  - `...&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n1928\t  - `...&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n1929\t\n1930\t  Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Print the failed\n1931\t  checklist lines on failure. Then open the game alone (no session) and check that it reaches the title with no errors.\n1932\t  Stop the server with `kill <PID>` (only that PID; never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`).\n1933\t\n1934\t### 11.7 Browser checks and screenshots (only for what a script can't check)\n1935\t\n1936\t- `browser` suite: `node tools/check.mjs <deliverable>` (errors, coverage, the look notes; act on every look note), at\n1937\t  1280×720, at 1920×1080, and at 390×844@3 with `?touchonly=1`. Deep links: `#match`, `#match/euphorium`,\n1938\t  `#match/stahlpresse`, `#cup/r1`, `#ending`, `#album`, `#about`, `#attract`. It also checks that the page made no\n1939\t  external requests.\n1940\t- **Filmstrips** (`tools/filmstrip.mjs ... --seed 1 --crop ...`), each looked at by eye after the animation code\n1941\t  changes: pass, shot (low and high power), volley, header, bicycle kick, diving header, slide, poke, barge, the\n1942\t  launched victim, the get-ups, the keeper's low dive, high dive, catch, parry, tip and throw, the theatrical dive, each\n1943\t  skill move, each celebration, the referee's card and VAR, a super strike of each path. Use the dev gallery's deep\n1944\t  links (`#dev/anim/<move>`) so each strip starts on the move.\n1945\t- **Screenshots** by eye: each stadium at its time of day, in each camera view; the title; every front-end screen\n1946\t  (10-foot legibility: compare the text size to §6.23's minimums at 1920×1080); the tabloid; the album; the HUD during\n1947\t  Europhoria; fog; rain; snow.\n1948\t\n1949\t### 11.8 Bundle checks (part of `browser`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"79247641-3d80-4a08-b7d2-090f6703f741","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:09.845Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n```sh\nnode tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n  examples/cmu-lib/CMU_10.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_11.js \\\n  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Roll,Victory,Cheer_One_arm,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dance_Simple,Angry,Backflip,Help_Two_Arms,Death_C,Dodge_left,Dodge_right,Greeting,Cartwheel,Jump_Twist,Breakdance_Helicopter,Shrug,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,Get_Up_From_Side,Run_Quick_Stop,Wave_Hello,10_02,10_05,11_01\" \\\n  --name EF --title \"Europhoria Football\" --out <dev folder>/mocap/ef-clips.js \\\n  --credit \"Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0); Mesh2Motion (CC0); CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (mocap.cs.cmu.edu), free for all uses; created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.\"\n```\n\nIf a name is in more than one set, the tool says so: prefix it `SET:`. If a clip's name differs, check the set's\ncatalog (`src/mocap/catalogs/*.json`) and fix the list. Expect about 150–250 KB. The CMU soccer takes play only a\nwindow around the kick: find the contact time once (the frame where the right foot's forward reach peaks), store it in\n`EF.Anim.CLIPS`, and sample from `contact − 0.45 s` to `contact + 0.35 s`.\n\n| Moment | Source | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| idle, jog, run, sprint | engine | the gait from velocity; `sprint: true` adds the lean |\n| dribble touch | engine spec | `touch: { rel, kick: true, a0: .2, a1: 0, z0: .08, z1: .12, reach: 4, wind: .03, active: .04, recover: .08 }` every stride |\n| pass | engine spec | `pass: { rel, kick: true, a0: .6, a1: -.1, z0: .15, z1: .2, reach: 6, wind: .08, active: .08, recover: .16, twist: .4 }` (inside foot) |\n| shot | spec, plus mocap for power ≥ .8 | `shot: { rel, kick: true, a0: .05, a1: 0, z0: .3, z1: 1.1, reach: 7, wind: .12, active: .1, recover: .26, lean: -.25, lunge: 2 }`; at high power blend `10_02`'s kick window in over the spec (`mocapW` 1, then fading to 0 in the recovery) |\n| penalty run-up and kick | mocap | `11_01` (the run-up and kick), with root motion supplied by the body |\n| chip / lob | spec | `chip: { a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: 1.4, reach: 5.5, lean: -.4 }` |\n| volley | spec | `volley: { a0: .4, a1: -.2, z0: .9, z1: 1.2, reach: 7, hop: 2, lean: -.4, twist: .6 }` |\n| header | procedural | `air: true` with a z arc; tilt forward 20° (axis `right`); the head snaps forward at contact (post-process `J.head`) |\n| diving header | procedural | tilt +75° about `right` (pivot hips, lift 6), arms back; lands with `down` 0.5 s; up with `Get_Up_Face_Down` |\n| bicycle kick | procedural | tilt −140° about `right` (pivot hips, lift up to 14 at contact), with `axekick`-style kick: `{ kick: true, a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: 2.2, z1: 1.5, reach: 6 }`; lands on the back (`down`); up with `Get_Up_From_Back` |\n| slide tackle | mocap | `Slide_Start` → `Slide_Loop` → `Slide_Exit` (the body supplies the travel) |\n| poke tackle | spec | `poke: { kick: true, a0: .3, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: .1, reach: 7.5, lunge: 3, wind: .05, active: .08, recover: .15 }` |\n| barge | engine move | `bash`, with a lean |\n| launched by a slide | procedural | tilt about `forward` spinning 1.5 turns over 0.6 s while the body flies (vz 120), stars; then `down: 1`; up with `LayToIdle` or `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n| knocked back | mocap | `Hit_Knockback`, then `LayToIdle` |\n| wrong-footed | mocap | `Dodge_left` / `Dodge_right` at `mocapW` .7, with `hurt` |\n| step-over | spec | two quick `kick` specs sweeping across the ball (`a0` from ±.9 to ∓.3), 0.15 s apart |\n| spin turn | engine | `rig.spin` from 0 to 2π over 0.45 s |\n| rainbow flick | spec | heel flick: `{ kick: true, a0: 3.0, a1: 2.6, z0: .1, z1: 1.3, reach: 4 }` (behind, upward) |\n| skid stop | mocap | `Run_Quick_Stop` (upper body, `mocapMask: 'upper'`) on hard stops |\n| theatrical dive | procedural + mocap | launch forward (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 8), land, 2 sideways rolls (tilt about `forward` spinning 2 turns while sliding 30), lie clutching a shin (`down: 1`, `expr: 'wince'`, hands to `J.kneeR`); if booked, up with `Shrug` |\n| protests | mocap | `Angry`, `Help_Two_Arms`, `Shrug` (upper) |\n| tired | procedural | lean 30°, hands to the knees (post-process `J.handL`/`J.handR` toward `J.kneeL`/`J.kneeR`) at stoppages when stamina is under 25 |\n| keeper set | engine | `pose: 'guard'`, crouch .3 |\n| keeper dive | procedural | tilt ±(70–95)° about `forward` (pivot feet), lifted 2 (low) to 14 (high) on an arc; lateral speed 260 easing to 0; hands IK'd (`E.ik3`) to the ball's point; then `down` on the side; up with `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n| keeper catch / parry / tip | procedural / engine | hands to the chest (catch); `jab` toward the ball (parry); one arm up with a jump (tip) |\n| keeper throw | mocap | `OverhandThrow`; an underarm roll as a spec with the arm low |\n| smother | procedural | a low forward dive (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 2) |\n| celebrations | mocap + procedural | knee slide: `Slide_Loop` with arms out (post-process); `Backflip`; `Cartwheel`; aeroplane: run with the arms horizontal (post-process) and a lean into the turn; robot: `Dance_Simple` at 0.6× speed with the arms bent square (post-process); shirt over head: `hood: true` with the hood in the shirt colour plus `Cheering_Two_Hands`; corner-flag dance: `Dance_Simple`; badge kiss: `Greeting`; helicopter: `Breakdance_Helicopter`; fish slap: two players face each other, alternating `jab` with a kipper sprite in the hand; pile-on: teammates `Victory` / `Cheer_One_arm` |\n| referee | engine + procedural | whistle (hand to mouth), points to the spot (`point: true`), the card raised high (hand above the head; the card sprite at `rig.hand('R')`), advantage (both arms forward), the VAR rectangle (both hands trace a box), hand to the ear; knocked over by the ball (`Fall_On_Face`, then up) |\n| manager | mocap | pacing (gait), `Angry` (conceding), `Victory` (scoring), `Help_Two_Arms` (instructions), `Cheering_Two_Hands` |\n| tunnel and handshakes | engine + procedural | a walk; an arm forward (`point: true`) as the lines pass |\n| crowd front rows | engine | classic-style rigs with `pose: 'cheer'`, `wave`, arms down for boos |\n\nCheck every attack and every procedural move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (§11.7): a wind-up, a strike, and a settle\nwithout jerks or backward sweeps.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tools/test.mjs`), the build working, and a short note in the dev\nfolder's `PROGRESS.md`. Do them in order: each one builds on the last, and the risky parts come early.\n\n**M0 — Setup (½ day).** The dev folder; the engine copied; `vendor/` filled; `package.json`; `tools/build.mjs`\nproducing `build/game.js`, the dev page and the deliverable; `tools/test.mjs` with its vm loader and one smoke test;\nthe SPORTS kit's game (`kits/sports.js`) copied in as a single first fragment (its own IIFE wrapper removed, since the\nbuild adds one) and running through the pipeline (proof: its `run(600)` hash is the same twice). From M1 on it is\nreplaced, piece by piece, by the fragments of §4.2.\n*Done when:* `node tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs` passes, and `node tools/check.mjs` on the deliverable shows\nthe kit's cage match.\n\n**M1 — The football sandbox (the feel).** The broadcast view; the pitch geometry and TileMap (§6.1); the ball (§6.2);\n5-a-side footballers with movement, stamina and dribbling (§6.3); pass, through, lob, one-two (§6.4); shooting with\nthe meter, sweet spot, aim, curl and chip (§6.5, without air moves); possession; goals; kickoffs; a temporary formation\nAI (the kit's, widened to 5); the camera director (§6.14); the score bug and power meter; `EF.T` with the TUNE tab only\n(a minimal dev panel); the Intent architecture with `HumanController`, `BotController` and `ScriptController`.\n*Done when:* a human can play a goal-scoring match against the CPU that already feels good; the physics unit tests\npass (§11.3).\n\n**M2 — Characters and animation (risky; early).** Engine changes §5.2 (kit patterns) and §5.3 (tilt); the clip set\ncut and loaded; every animation row of §8.3 for outfield players and keepers; kits for all 6 teams.\n*Done when:* filmstrips of the pass, the shot, the slide, the launched victim, the keeper's low and high dives, the\nheader, the bicycle kick, the dive and 3 celebrations look right (§11.7).\n\n**M3 — The rest of football.** Air moves (§6.5), skill moves (§6.6), defending (§6.7), keepers in full (§6.8), the\nrules machine (§6.12: the clock, stoppage, halves, extra time, the shootout), set pieces (§6.11), the referee, fouls,\nadvantage, cards, theatrics and VAR (§6.10).\n*Done when:* the rules and set-piece tests pass, and an AI-versus-AI match produces corners, free kicks, cards and\npenalties.\n\n**M4 — Team AI and balance.** TeamBrains with formations, tactics and gimmicks (§6.13, §7.1); difficulty; the AI overlay\nin dev mode; the soak test (§11.4) tuned to its targets.\n*Done when:* 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches per tactic pair meet the soak targets.\n\n**M5 — The over-the-top layer.** Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes (all 7 paths), the Save Duel (§6.9); the bus;\ncelebrations (§6.21); cinematics.\n*Done when:* every super strike's test passes and the Save Duel's timing windows are exact.\n\n**M6 — Presentation.** The 6 stadiums (§7.2) with stands, skylines, lights and weather (§6.19); the crowd view and mood\n(§6.18); matchday events (§6.20); replays (§6.15); the HUD in full (§6.16); the commentary director and its lines\n(§6.17, §7.4); audio in full: songs, SFX, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices (§6.22, engine changes §5.1, §5.4,\n§5.5).\n*Done when:* screenshots of each stadium at its time of day look right, and the audio smoke test plays without\nerrors.\n\n**M7 — Front end and 10-foot UI.** The UI kit (§6.23), glyphs and prompts (§2.3), title, Kick-About setup with the\ncontroller side picker (§6.27), results, settings integration (§6.31), touch-only (§6.33), About (§6.32).\n*Done when:* every screen can be used with a pad only, a keyboard only, and a mouse only (scripted UI tests, §11.3).\n\n**M8 — The Cup Run.** The beat player and its step kinds, tabloids, the travel map, team talks, challenges, stickers,\nthe album, saves, the ending with the ceremony, the parade and the credits (§6.24, §7.3, §7.5).\n*Done when:* the scripted full playthrough passes (§11.5).\n\n**M9 — Training and Penalties.** The 9 drills (§6.25, §7.6) and Penalties mode (§6.26).\n*Done when:* each drill's scripted solve passes.\n\n**M10 — Attract and dev mode.** The idle watcher and the attract director (§6.29); dev mode in full (§6.30).\n*Done when:* the attract tests pass (it starts at 10.0 s, shows every segment, and any input exits) and every WARP\nentry runs without errors.\n\n**M11 — AI Hub online.** §6.28 in full; the fake-hub loopback tests (§11.6), then the real harness in Chromium.\n*Done when:* `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for 2 players, for 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5,\nfor the host-leave scenario, and for the server scenario.\n\n**M12 — Bundle, polish, hand-back.** The final build; the full test pass; the look notes from `tools/check.mjs` acted\non; screenshots reviewed; `exit-interview.json` written and validated; the About pages generated from it; the chat\nreply (§12).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Football-specific animation** (keeper dives, bicycle kicks, diving headers, dives) | The rig has no such moves; a bad dive ruins the game's look | M2 is early. Build the tilt state first, on one rig, in a test scene (`#dev` with an animation gallery: every move on a loop, every view). Filmstrip each move. Fallbacks: the built-in `flip` roll and `down`, sideways `Dodge_*_RM`, `Dive_Roll` from CMU |\n| **Kit patterns in the engine's torso painter** | It is drawn code inside the rig | A self-contained change behind `o.kit`; fallback: solid shirts with trim and no numbers (§5.2) |\n| **AI quality with 10 players** | Bad AI makes matches dull or broken: clumps, stuck players, no shots | A parametric formation model and utility scoring (§6.13), not ad hoc rules; the AI overlay; the soak test with numeric targets (§11.4) from M4 on |\n| **The feel of ball control** | Sticky ball versus loose ball; passes that miss | Dev sliders from M1; unit tests for pass accuracy; play it often from M1 |\n| **Netcode under latency and loss** | Shared-world football has a contested ball | Host authority with interpolation, input counters that survive loss, and the rate budget (§6.28, Appendix B). The sim/presentation split is in place from M1. Build a loopback fake hub with latency, jitter and loss in Node first (§11.6), then the real harness |\n| **Hub protocol details** (the card, ready, server mode, time-up, end) | The hub keeps a game that fails its check out of sessions | Follow the README's checklist line by line; run the harness's automatic check for every scenario it lists (§11.6) |\n| **Audio synthesis** (the crowd and babble) | WebAudio code is easy to get wrong, and silent in tests | One audio smoke page (`#dev` → sound test: every SFX, song, chant and voice on a list); headless no-ops tested; one screenshot-free check that no audio errors reach `game.errors` |\n| **Many systems, one IIFE** | Name clashes, load-order bugs | Numbered fragments with one namespace; the content validator; the full playthrough test |\n| **Scope** | It is a lot of game | Data-driven content; the milestone order puts the core first; each milestone ends playable. The list in §12 is the scope: build all of it, but do the core well before the extras are polished |\n| **Determinism** (tests and replays) | `Math.random` in sim code breaks proofs | A lint test greps `src/` for `Math.random` outside cosmetic code; the determinism test (§11.4) |\n| **Bundle correctness** | `</script>` in inlined code; the order of hub metas and `session.js` | The build checks both; a test parses the deliverable's `<head>` order (§11.8) |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing\n\n### 11.1 The one command\n\n`node tools/test.mjs` runs every suite and prints **only failures** (one line each: `FAIL <suite> <test>: <detail>`) and\none last line: `Europhoria tests: <passed> passed, <failed> failed (<seconds> s)`. It exits with 1 on any failure.\n`node tools/test.mjs <suite> [...]` runs only the named suites, so after a change you rerun only the suites that cover\nit. The suites: `unit`, `rules`, `ai`, `content`, `ui`, `saves`, `attract`, `dev`, `playthrough`, `determinism`,\n`hubsim` (Node), then `browser`, `hub` (Playwright; skipped with a note if Chromium is missing). Don't use subagents or\nworkflows to review or judge anything: the tests and screenshots are the judges.\n\n### 11.2 Headless harness\n\n`tools/lib/load.mjs` creates a vm context with the stand-ins the kits' test uses (`window` = the context,\n`addEventListener` as a no-op, `location: { hash, search }`), plus `matchMedia` (returns `{ matches: false,\naddEventListener() {} }`), `navigator` (`{ maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`), and `performance`. It runs\n`vendor/session.js` first (in Node it stays inactive: no parent frame), then the engine, the mocap scripts, the clip\nset and `build/game.js`. It returns `{ E, game, EF, I: game.input, snap: () => game.debug.snapshot() }`.\n`game.advance(seconds)` steps exactly. `input.tap` and `input.hold` press actions. `EF.test` gives the setup hooks:\n`startMatch({ home, away, stadium, seed, halfLength, humans })`, `giveBall(side, idx, x, y)`, `place(id, x, y)`,\n`setEuphoria(side, v)`, `forceShot(...)`, `simUntil(predicate, maxSeconds)`, `cheat(name, on)`.\n\n`game.debug.snapshot()` returns `{ scene, part, mode, half, clock, minute, stoppage, score, ball: [x, y, z], owner,\nhumans: [{ p, id, name, x, y, state }], euphoria: [a, b], europhoria, cards, sentOff, setpiece, shootout, stadium,\nweather, cup: { round, results }, attract: { active, segment, idle }, dev: { open, changed }, hub: { active, role,\nsent, received }, ui: { screen, focus }, errors: game.errors.length }`. `game.debug.teleport(x, y, z)` moves the\ncontrolled footballer. Every test also checks that `game.errors` stayed empty.\n\n### 11.3 Unit and system tests (Node)\n\n- **unit/ball:** a pass at a moving receiver arrives within 8 units of him, for 50 seeded cases; curl turns a shot by\n  the expected angle, ±10%; bounces off the boards keep within the bounce factor; each post and the bar reflect; the\n  goal-line test with the ball over the line by r − 1 (no goal) and r + 1 (goal); a ball over the bar gives no goal;\n  the net stops the ball within 0.5 s; each surface's friction order (mud < snow < grass < hard < wet in rolling\n  distance, shortest to longest).\n- **unit/input:** `Input.halfKeys(EF.KEYS, 'left')` puts `pass … dive` on F G H R T Y V B and `'right'` puts them on\n  . / , L ; ' K M; the `switch` + `skill` chord fires `euphoria` on a half keyboard and on a pad (L1 + R1); Space\n  fires it on a full keyboard; mouse buttons do nothing while mouse aim is off.\n- **unit/footballer:** sprint drains and regains stamina at the set rates; turning with the ball slows him; each skill\n  move's success rule at the probability extremes (with a fixed rng); the air-ball window chooses header, volley,\n  bicycle or diving header by height and facing; the receiver picked by the stick direction for 8 directions;\n  pass-assist cones.\n- **unit/keeper:** save chance falls as shot speed rises and as the target moves to the corners; a catch under 260 well\n  reached; parries go away from the goal centre; tips over the bar give corners.\n- **rules:** the corner versus goal kick by last touch; the crowd throw-back side; a foul from behind is a foul and one\n  from the front with the ball first is not; severities give yellow, red, and a second yellow → red; a sent-off side\n  plays with 3 and drops the formation's `drop` role; advantage plays on when possession stays; a penalty for a foul in\n  the box; VAR overturns only soft penalties; the clock maps 2:00 real time to 45 game minutes; stoppage time is within\n  1–5; extra time is golden goal; the shootout ends early when a side can't catch up and goes to sudden death after 5\n  each; the shirt-over-head celebration gives a yellow.\n- **euphoria:** every gain in the table; decay; thresholds; Europhoria lasts 8 s; one super a Europhoria; each super path\n  reaches the goal mouth from 230 out with no errors (7 cases); Save Duel windows: a press at the target ±59 ms is\n  PERFECT, ±61 ms is GOOD, ±141 ms is MISS.\n- **ai:** players reach their formation spots within 1.5 s when the ball is placed (each formation, each phase); the\n  pressing count matches the tactic; the ball carrier never stands still for more than 2 s; the bus appears for\n  Lucchetto when leading after 60' and not otherwise; Opulence's Golden Moment fires at 80' when behind or level.\n- **content:** `EF.validate()` reports nothing; every team has 5 players with one captain and one GK; every captain has\n  a registered super; every stadium's events exist; every beat's team, stadium and photo exist; every drill's steps\n  run; every text uses only characters the font can draw; every commentary pool for a major event has at least 12\n  lines; at least 300 lines in total; every sticker is reachable (its `how` refers to an event that exists).\n- **ui:** with only pad actions (`input.tap('down')`, `'confirm'`, `'cancel'`) a script can reach every screen from the\n  title and back. With only the mouse (`input.feed('move', x, y)` and clicks at a widget's centre) every menu item can\n  be focused by hover and picked by click. The keyboard (`press('ArrowDown')`, `press('Enter')`) does the same.\n  `EF.prompt` gives PlayStation icons for pad codes by default and Xbox after `game.settings.set('glyphs', 'xbox')`;\n  keycaps when `lastDevice` is the keyboard; mouse icons when it is the mouse. Touch-only (`?touchonly=1`): the title\n  shows the notice and the SETTINGS button, and the play tiles cannot start a match.\n- **saves:** a write/read round trip; a migration from a v0 shape; CONTINUE resumes at the right round; dev unlocks only\n  after their confirm.\n- **attract:** at the title, `advance(9.9)` leaves it on the title; `advance(0.2)` more starts `attract`; during the\n  attract run every segment shows (snapshot `attract.segment` over 95 s: all 6); `input.tap('confirm')`, a key press, a\n  mouse move and a pad axis each return to the title, and that press does not pick a menu item.\n- **dev:** every slider changes `EF.T` and a match responds (for example `runSpeed` 120 → a sprint covers more ground in\n  1 s); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; every WARP entry runs with no errors; dev mode cannot open when the\n  fake hub says `active`.\n\n### 11.4 Balance soak and determinism\n\n- **soak** (part of `ai`, tagged slow; run it after AI changes): 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches at a half length of\n  60 s, for each of 4 pairings (each tactic once against Kipperton at Normal). Targets per match on average: 2–7 goals,\n  8–20 shots, 55–85% pass completion, possession 35–65% for each side, at least 1 corner and 1 free kick in 4 matches,\n  no player stuck (no movement for more than 4 s in play), no ball stuck (not moving and not owned for more than 3 s in\n  play). It reports the averages, so tuning has numbers to work with.\n- **determinism:** a scripted match (the kit's `proof()` pattern: a seed, scripted inputs for 1,800 steps) hashed twice\n  gives the same hash. Then a replay re-run gives the same final state hash as the live run.\n- **lint:** no `Math.random` in sim files (`10-`..`18-`, `20-`); no `ctx.arc`, `ctx.stroke`, `ctx.fillText` or canvas\n  gradients on the game buffer; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, `fetch`, `WebSocket` or `RTCPeerConnection`.\n\n### 11.5 The scripted playthrough (the whole game)\n\n`playthrough` runs the whole game headless, as a player would, through the real scenes and the real input. It drives\nthe human with a **bot**: the kit's approach (`SPORTS.bot()`) of asking the CPU brain what it would do and giving\nthat as the stick and buttons, plus scripted forcing where a beat needs it. Half length 30 s; difficulty Easy; the\n\"Euphoria always full\" cheat is off.\n\n1. The title, then CUP RUN, NEW CUP RUN; the prologue's beats are advanced with `confirm`; LET'S PLAY.\n2. For each round: the bracket, the tabloid, the travel map, the talk, a team talk (cycling the 3 kinds over the\n   rounds), the challenge card, the tunnel. Then the match, played by the bot to the final whistle. If the bot loses or\n   draws, `EF.test` grants a win through the real path: it plays on with the \"Euphoria always full\" and \"invincible\n   keeper\" cheats, and records that it did so. Then the results, stickers, the autosave, and the post-match beats.\n3. The semi-final must show the bus at least once (forced: a Lucchetto lead after 60' by the dev goal cheat). The\n   villain beat takes the loyal choice.\n4. The final, then the ending: the ceremony, the parade, the tabloid, the credits, then the title.\n5. Then: CONTINUE is gone or points to a finished cup; the album shows the earned stickers; Kick-About with 2 local\n   players (one on each side) plays 20 s; PENALTIES plays a full shootout; TRAINING solves drill 1 by script; ABOUT\n   pages through to the end; the attract mode starts after 10 s idle and exits on a key.\n6. Checks along the way: the snapshot's scene at every step; no errors; the save after each round; each round's\n   challenge events seen; at least one corner, one free kick, one card, one super strike and one replay over the run.\n\nTarget time: under 2 minutes headless. It is the slowest suite, so run it after changes to flow, scenes, the cup, saves\nor content.\n\n### 11.6 Online tests\n\n- **hubsim (Node):** a fake hub (`tools/lib/fakehub.mjs`) implements the client API (`connect`, `ready`, `answer`, `on`,\n  `send`, `time`, `finish`, `progress`, `rng`, `active`, `isHost`, `server`, `players`) between 2–4 vm contexts, with a\n  network of set latency, jitter and loss. It steps all copies in lockstep with `game.advance`. Checks: each copy reaches\n  the card with no key press and calls `ready()`; `answer('ready')` on Enter; the match starts on `start` and play waits\n  for time ≥ 0; the host's message rate stays at 20/s or under, with bursts under 40, and every message is under 16 KB\n  (snapshots under 1,100 bytes); with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, a client's drawn ball stays within 24\n  units of the host's 95% of the time; a press is never lost (counters); a goal on the host shows on every client within\n  0.5 s; `leave` hands a footballer to the CPU; `time-up` makes the host finish at once; `finish`'s standings put the\n  winners first and tie a draw; the server mode runs with no local player and draws nothing; on `end`, input, sending and\n  sound stop; host-left shows ROUND VOID.\n- **hub (Playwright):** the real harness. Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/harness/`. Start a\n  server for the **work root**, bound to localhost on a port the OS picks, in the background, and remember its PID:\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <work root>`. Read the port from its first output line\n  (\"Serving HTTP on 127.0.0.1 port N\"). Fetch\n  `http://127.0.0.1:N/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174834.html` and check that its\n  `<title>` is \"Europhoria Football\" before trusting any result (another process could hold the port). Then open, in\n  turn:\n  - `http://127.0.0.1:N/<dev folder>/tools/harness/harness.html?game=/<game>.html&players=2&auto=1`\n  - `...&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n  - `...&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n  - `...&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n\n  Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Print the failed\n  checklist lines on failure. Then open the game alone (no session) and check that it reaches the title with no errors.\n  Stop the server with `kill <PID>` (only that PID; never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`).\n\n### 11.7 Browser checks and screenshots (only for what a script can't check)\n\n- `browser` suite: `node tools/check.mjs <deliverable>` (errors, coverage, the look notes; act on every look note), at\n  1280×720, at 1920×1080, and at 390×844@3 with `?touchonly=1`. Deep links: `#match`, `#match/euphorium`,\n  `#match/stahlpresse`, `#cup/r1`, `#ending`, `#album`, `#about`, `#attract`. It also checks that the page made no\n  external requests.\n- **Filmstrips** (`tools/filmstrip.mjs ... --seed 1 --crop ...`), each looked at by eye after the animation code\n  changes: pass, shot (low and high power), volley, header, bicycle kick, diving header, slide, poke, barge, the\n  launched victim, the get-ups, the keeper's low dive, high dive, catch, parry, tip and throw, the theatrical dive, each\n  skill move, each celebration, the referee's card and VAR, a super strike of each path. Use the dev gallery's deep\n  links (`#dev/anim/<move>`) so each strip starts on the move.\n- **Screenshots** by eye: each stadium at its time of day, in each camera view; the title; every front-end screen\n  (10-foot legibility: compare the text size to §6.23's minimums at 1920×1080); the tabloid; the album; the HUD during\n  Europhoria; fog; rain; snow.\n\n### 11.8 Bundle checks (part of `browser`)","numLines":300,"startLine":1650,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KRgELwmeKJGrTH4AMxoX3J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2pommnMN1oufCvCB3J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PBZtW5JMEtF6cQwBMxVwa5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1950,"limit":210},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12576,"cache_read_input_tokens":84371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12576},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"cd66d46c-1152-4ea7-b7c9-fb8e6e963c31","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:13.052Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2poVQ5shVdrR3tRmSm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PBZtW5JMEtF6cQwBMxVwa5":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","offset":1950,"limit":210}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PBZtW5JMEtF6cQwBMxVwa5","type":"tool_result","content":"1950\t\n1951\tThe deliverable exists in the work root under its exact name. Its `<head>` starts with `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then\n1952\tthe `session.js` script, and that script is byte-identical to `vendor/session.js`. The hub metas are present with the\n1953\tvalues in §3.3, and `hub:session-howto` is at most 80 characters. No external URLs are loaded. It runs from `file://`.\n1954\t`exit-interview.json` parses, has every key of TASK.md's shape, has no empty value, uses a genre from the allowed list,\n1955\tand has 3–6 lowercase tags.\n1956\t\n1957\t---\n1958\t\n1959\t## 12. Definition of done and hand-back\n1960\t\n1961\t**Done means all of this is in and working, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features:**\n1962\t\n1963\t- [ ] The cup run: prologue, 5 rounds with their beats, team talks, challenges, the villain beat, the ending with the\n1964\t      ceremony, the parade and the credits; losing and CONTINUE; saves and CONTINUE.\n1965\t- [ ] Kick-About with all 6 teams and 5 stadiums, conditions, ball styles, 1–4 local players in co-op or versus.\n1966\t- [ ] Penalties mode; Training with 9 drills; the Sticker Album with 51 stickers; About & Credits.\n1967\t- [ ] Every mechanic of §6.3–§6.12 and §6.21; the team AI with 5 tactic profiles and gimmicks; 4 difficulties.\n1968\t- [ ] Euphoria, Europhoria, 7 super-strike paths, the Save Duel.\n1969\t- [ ] 6 stadiums with weather and lighting; crowd states, chants, the tifo and flares; 6 matchday events; replays; the\n1970\t      HUD; commentary with 300+ lines; the PA.\n1971\t- [ ] All audio in code: 15 songs, the SFX list, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices; no audio files.\n1972\t- [ ] Controls for pad (PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox in Settings), keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last\n1973\t      device; touch-only devices get the notice and the settings button.\n1974\t- [ ] The attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n1975\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu (and `` ` `` / F1): TUNE sliders with reset to defaults, CHEATS, WARP (with the\n1976\t      animation and sound galleries), INFO.\n1977\t- [ ] AI Hub shared-world sessions passing the harness in all 4 runs; the game unchanged outside sessions.\n1978\t- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` passes in full; the screenshots and filmstrips have been looked at.\n1979\t- [ ] The single HTML file in the work root; `exit-interview.json` beside it; `engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md` written.\n1980\t\n1981\t**Hand-back** (TASK.md's \"Source Information\" section and exit interview):\n1982\t\n1983\t1. Write `exit-interview.json` in the work root, in TASK.md's exact shape. Fill every value (write \"unknown\" where you\n1984\t   cannot confirm something), use plain text, and check that it parses. Suggested `aiHub` values: name \"Europhoria\n1985\t   Football\"; tagline \"Over-the-top arcade football\"; description \"A broke seaside club rides its fans' euphoria\n1986\t   through Europe's grandest cup: 5-a-side arcade football with super strikes, dives, VAR and a crowd that powers your\n1987\t   team.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"European football\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls \"Stick/WASD move\n1988\t   · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L lob · R1/E skill · R2/Shift sprint · L1+R1/Space Europhoria\"; tags e.g. [\"arcade\",\n1989\t   \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"retro\"].\n1990\t2. Source Information values: Date \"2026-11-03 17:48:34\"; Source \"European football (over the top arcade style)\";\n1991\t   Plan \"PLAN.md\"; Genre and Perspective \"arcade 5-a-side football with a story cup run; TV-broadcast side-on camera\n1992\t   (40°), with classic three-quarter and aerial options\"; Tech \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff package, modified: see\n1993\t   CHANGES-ENGINE.md), its mocap player and clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain\n1994\t   JavaScript; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\"; Art Direction \"my-3D2dge's native PS1-era pixel art with HD\n1995\t   Humanoid rigs; new kits, stadiums, crowds, crests, tabloids\"; Animation \"the engine's procedural Humanoid rig with\n1996\t   mocap clips through Mocap.drive and new procedural moves (body tilt)\"; Audio \"the engine's chip synth for music and\n1997\t   SFX, plus a WebAudio crowd engine, sung chants and Animalese-style babble voices; no audio files\"; Online \"AI Hub\n1998\t   Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 2–4 players\"; Testing, Research, Environment (\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux;\n1999\t   browser unknown\" unless known), Model, Usage: fill in from the build. For Research, the planning stage read the\n2000\t   engine's handoff docs (README, API.md, parts of AI_GUIDE.md, docs/ASSETS.md, docs/MOCAP.md), the SPORTS kit, the\n2001\t   template game and its test, the mocap catalogs, and the AI Hub's README, session.js, retrofit.md and arena example.\n2002\t   Add whatever the build stage reads.\n2003\t3. Rebuild so the About pages carry the same text (§3.3), and rerun the `browser` suite.\n2004\t4. Reply in chat with the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (the same answers as\n2005\t   the JSON), and a short summary.\n2006\t\n2007\t---\n2008\t\n2009\t## Appendix A: tuning defaults (dev sliders)\n2010\t\n2011\t| Key | Default | Min | Max | Step | Group | What it does |\n2012\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n2013\t| `runSpeed` | 88 | 60 | 130 | 1 | Movement | base run speed (u/s), before the pace stat |\n2014\t| `sprintMul` | 1.45 | 1.1 | 2.0 | .05 | Movement | sprint multiplier |\n2015\t| `accel` | 900 | 300 | 2000 | 50 | Movement | acceleration (u/s²) |\n2016\t| `staminaDrain` | 20 | 5 | 50 | 1 | Movement | per second of sprint |\n2017\t| `staminaRegen` | 14 | 5 | 40 | 1 | Movement | per second at rest |\n2018\t| `ballFriction` | 1.1 | .3 | 3 | .05 | Ball | rolling decay on grass |\n2019\t| `ballBounce` | .55 | .1 | .9 | .05 | Ball | restitution on grass |\n2020\t| `ballGravity` | 600 | 300 | 1000 | 10 | Ball | |\n2021\t| `trapSpeed` | 210 | 120 | 320 | 5 | Ball | the fastest ball trapped at 9 units |\n2022\t| `passSpeedMin` | 150 | 80 | 250 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | |\n2023\t| `passSpeedMax` | 300 | 200 | 450 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | |\n2024\t| `passAssistDeg` | 70 | 0 | 90 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | the High pass-assist cone |\n2025\t| `shotChargeTime` | .8 | .3 | 2 | .05 | Passing & Shooting | seconds to full power |\n2026\t| `shotSpeedMax` | 420 | 250 | 600 | 10 | Passing & Shooting | |\n2027\t| `curlStrength` | 3.2 | 0 | 8 | .1 | Passing & Shooting | aftertouch spin per second |\n2028\t| `keeperReaction` | .18 | .05 | .5 | .01 | Keepers | seconds |\n2029\t| `keeperReach` | 48 | 24 | 80 | 1 | Keepers | lateral dive reach |\n2030\t| `tackleReach` | 9 | 4 | 16 | .5 | Defending & Rules | |\n2031\t| `slideSpeed` | 190 | 100 | 300 | 5 | Defending & Rules | |\n2032\t| `foulStrictness` | 1 | 0 | 2 | .05 | Defending & Rules | × the referee's own |\n2033\t| `diveSuccess` | 1 | 0 | 2 | .05 | Defending & Rules | × the referee's gullibility |\n2034\t| `euphoriaGain` | 1 | 0 | 4 | .1 | Euphoria | × every gain |\n2035\t| `euphoriaDecay` | 1.5 | 0 | 6 | .1 | Euphoria | per second |\n2036\t| `europhoriaTime` | 8 | 3 | 20 | .5 | Euphoria | seconds |\n2037\t| `superSpeed` | 520 | 300 | 800 | 10 | Euphoria | |\n2038\t| `aiReaction` | .25 | .05 | .8 | .01 | AI | seconds between decisions (Normal; difficulty scales it) |\n2039\t| `aiAccuracy` | .8 | .3 | 1 | .05 | AI | |\n2040\t| `aiAggression` | .5 | 0 | 1 | .05 | AI | |\n2041\t| `halfLength` | 120 | 20 | 300 | 10 | Match | real seconds (Settings sets it; the slider overrides it while changed) |\n2042\t| `gameSpeed` | 1 | .25 | 2 | .05 | Match | `game.timeScale` |\n2043\t\n2044\t## Appendix B: network messages\n2045\t\n2046\tAll JSON. Numbers rounded (positions to integers, angles in hundredths of a radian).\n2047\t\n2048\t- **Client → host, `i` (input), unreliable, 15/s:**\n2049\t  `{ t: 'i', s: seq, at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), m: [mx100, my100], a: [ax100, ay100] | 0, h: heldBits, c: [pass, shoot, lob, through, skill, sw, dive, euphoria] }`.\n2050\t  `heldBits`: 1 sprint, 2 pass, 4 shoot, 8 lob, 16 through, 32 skill, 64 sw, 128 dive. `c` holds cumulative press\n2051\t  counts since the round started: the host takes `c[k] > last[k]` as a press, so a lost packet loses no presses. The\n2052\t  host keeps the newest by `s`.\n2053\t- **Client → host, reliable, rare:** `{ t: 'duel', id, at }` (the Save Duel press, in `AIHub.time()` ms);\n2054\t  `{ t: 'cel', k: 0..3 }` (the celebration pick); `{ t: 'menu', open: true|false }` (the settings overlay: the host\n2055\t  gives that footballer to the CPU while open).\n2056\t- **Host → all, `s` (snapshot), unreliable, 14/s, under 1,100 bytes:**\n2057\t  `{ t: 's', n, at, b: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, spin100, owner], p: [[x, y, z, vx, vy, f100, st, act, u100, flags], ×10],\n2058\t  r: [x, y, f100, st], m: [mode, clock10, minute, s0, s1, eu0, eu1, euSide, euT10, setpiece], c: [[hubId, footballerIdx], ...] }`.\n2059\t  `st` and `act` are small integer codes from a shared table; `flags` packs cards, glow, human-held and down.\n2060\t- **Host → all, `E` (events), reliable, at most 5/s:** `{ t: 'E', n, list: [[eventSeq, at, type, data], ...] }`,\n2061\t  coalescing the events of up to 200 ms: goal, whistle, card, VAR, commentary line ids (so every copy shows the same\n2062\t  lines), sfx cues, the super strike's start, the duel's start, celebrations, set-piece starts, half time, full time.\n2063\t  Clients apply each `eventSeq` once, in order.\n2064\t- **Host → all, last:** a reliable `s` with `over: 1`, then `AIHub.finish(...)`.\n2065\t\n2066\t## Appendix C: data shapes\n2067\t\n2068\t```js\n2069\tEF.def('team', 'kipperton', { name: 'KIPPERTON ATHLETIC', short: 'KIP', nick: 'THE KIPPERS', city: 'KIPPERTON',\n2070\t  stadium: 'smokehouse', formation: '2-1-1', tactic: 'plucky', chant: 'kipperton', celebration: 'fishslap',\n2071\t  crowd: { factor: 1 }, manager: 'mags',\n2072\t  kits: { home: { shirt: '#f08a24', color2: '#1c2a5a', pattern: 'hoops', shorts: '#1c2a5a', socks: '#f08a24', number: '#ffffff' },\n2073\t          away: { shirt: '#eef0f4', color2: '#f08a24', pattern: 'sash', shorts: '#eef0f4', socks: '#1c2a5a', number: '#1c2a5a' },\n2074\t          keeper: { shirt: '#3ac06a', color2: '#1a5a30', pattern: 'plain', shorts: '#1a1a1a', socks: '#3ac06a', glove: '#f4f4f0' } },\n2075\t  crest: { shape: 'shield', field: '#1c2a5a', ring: '#f08a24', charges: ['kipper', 'anchor'] },\n2076\t  players: [\n2077\t    { id: 'crabb', name: 'WALLY CRABB', num: 1, pos: 'GK', build: 'bulky', size: 1.2, hair: 'bald', skin: '#e0b090', hairColor: '#c8c8c8',\n2078\t      stats: { pace: 60, shoot: 30, pass: 55, tackle: 40, skill: 20, keep: 76, weight: 80, temper: 30 }, voice: { f0: 120, wave: 'pulse' } },\n2079\t    { id: 'pilchard', name: 'DAZ PILCHARD', num: 9, pos: 'FWD', captain: true, super: 'smoked-kipper', build: 'heroic', size: 1.15,\n2080\t      hair: 'short', skin: '#f0c8a8', hairColor: '#5a3a22', stats: { pace: 80, shoot: 90, pass: 70, tackle: 45, skill: 75, keep: 10, weight: 60, temper: 50 },\n2081\t      voice: { f0: 150, wave: 'saw' }, celebration: 'fishslap' } /* ...3 more */ ] });\n2082\t\n2083\tEF.def('formation', '1-2-1', { roles: {\n2084\t  GK: { base: [.03, .5], keeper: true },\n2085\t  DEF: { base: [.22, .5], att: [.14, 0], def: [0, 0], pull: [.45, .55], uRange: [.08, .62] },\n2086\t  MIDL: { base: [.42, .28], att: [.12, -.06], def: [-.12, .04], pull: [.55, .45], uRange: [.15, .85] },\n2087\t  MIDR: { base: [.42, .72], att: [.12, .06], def: [-.12, -.04], pull: [.55, .45], uRange: [.15, .85] },\n2088\t  FWD: { base: [.64, .5], att: [.18, 0], def: [-.12, 0], pull: [.5, .6], uRange: [.35, .95] } }, drop: 'MIDR' });\n2089\t\n2090\tEF.def('tactic', 'keepball', { press: .55, pressers: 1, line: .5, width: .6, tempo: .85, passRisk: .2, shortBias: .9,\n2091\t  longBall: .05, dribble: .25, skill: .3, shootRange: 170, shootBias: .8, foul: .1, dive: .1, euphoriaUse: 'attack', gimmick: 'keepball' });\n2092\t\n2093\tEF.def('referee', 'severo', { name: 'SERGIO SEVERO', strictness: 1.2, gullibility: .7, varHappy: .9, voice: { f0: 135, wave: 'saw' } });\n2094\t\n2095\tEF.def('stadium', 'smokehouse', { name: 'THE SMOKEHOUSE', city: 'KIPPERTON', capacity: 3112, time: 'dusk',\n2096\t  weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .7, wind: .4 }, surface: 'wet', mud: [[.06, .5, 40], [.94, .5, 40]], puddles: 6,\n2097\t  grass: ['#3f7a34', '#4a8a3c'], wear: .6, lines: '#e8ece0',\n2098\t  stands: { north: { tiers: 3, roof: 'corrugated', seats: '#3a3a48' }, west: { tiers: 2, kind: 'terrace' }, east: { tiers: 2, kind: 'terrace' } },\n2099\t  crowd: { size: 600, home: .8 }, skyline: [['chimney', .12, 90, { smoke: true }], ['lighthouse', .85, 120, { beam: true }]],\n2100\t  lights: { ambient: .55, floodlights: 4, color: '#fff0d0' }, boards: [\"SMOKY JOE'S KIPPERS\", 'GULL INSURANCE: WE COVER EVERYTHING', 'PIE-O-MATIC'],\n2101\t  events: ['seagull', 'floodlight', 'invader-keith'], music: null });\n2102\t\n2103\tEF.def('super', 'smoked-kipper', { name: 'THE SMOKED KIPPER', path: 'wobble', params: { amp: 18, freq: 7 }, trail: 'smoke',\n2104\t  color: '#f08a24', ball: 'kipper', sfx: 'super-kipper', lines: 'super-kipper' });\n2105\t\n2106\tEF.def('celebration', 'kneeslide', { name: 'KNEE SLIDE', clip: 'Slide_Loop', proc: 'armsOut', travel: { speed: 120, t: 1.1 },\n2107\t  euphoria: 8, crowd: 'roar' });\n2108\t\n2109\tEF.def('event', 'seagull', { stadiums: ['smokehouse'], chance: .6, when: { minute: [10, 80], ballLoose: true, notSetPiece: true },\n2110\t  start(m) { /* spawn the gull on the ball */ },\n2111\t  update(m, dt) { /* pin the ball; flap away when a player is within 10 */ return this.gone; },   // true when finished\n2112\t  lines: 'event-seagull' });\n2113\t\n2114\tEF.def('drill', 'passing', { title: 'PASS MASTER', coach: 'mags', stadium: 'rec', teaches: ['pass', 'through', 'oneTwo'],\n2115\t  setup(m) { /* two teammates, cones */ },\n2116\t  steps: [ { say: ['Five passes. Feet, not faces.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', count: 5 } },\n2117\t           { say: ['Now a through ball. Into space.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', where: { kind: 'through' }, count: 2 } },\n2118\t           { say: ['One-two. Give it and go.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', where: { kind: 'oneTwo' }, count: 1 } } ],\n2119\t  reward: { sticker: null } });\n2120\t\n2121\tEF.def('beat', 'r2-pre', { round: 2, steps: [\n2122\t  { kind: 'travel', to: 'solera', postcard: \"WISH YOU WERE HERE (IT'S HOT)\" },\n2123\t  { kind: 'tabloid', headline: 'PASS THE PARCEL', sub: 'Kippers must stop the passing masters... if they can find the ball.',\n2124\t    photo: { team: 'pasapasa', player: 'pasarela', pose: 'hips', expr: 'smile' } },\n2125\t  { kind: 'talk', lines: [['pasarela', 'You will chase the ball until you are dizzy, little fishes.']] },\n2126\t  { kind: 'teamtalk' }, { kind: 'challenge', id: 'recover5' }, { kind: 'tunnel' }, { kind: 'match' } ] });\n2127\t\n2128\t// EF.lines(pool, entries) is shorthand for EF.def('lines', pool, entries)\n2129\tEF.lines('goal', [\n2130\t  { who: 'barry', text: 'OH, YOU BEAUTY! {$player} has absolutely LEATHERED it!' },\n2131\t  { who: 'barry', text: 'GET IN! Back of the net from {$player}!', reply: { who: 'trev', text: 'Keeper had no chance. None. Nada. Zilch.' } },\n2132\t  { who: 'barry', text: 'OH MY COD! KIPPERTON HAVE SCORED!', when: m => m.lastGoal.team === 'kipperton' } ]);\n2133\t```\n2134\t\n2135\t## Appendix D: music sketches\n2136\t\n2137\tStarting points in the engine's song format (`audio.music(song)`); refine by ear. All of them are original.\n2138\t\n2139\t**`anthem`** (108 bpm, `steps: 2`, so each token is an eighth note; 8 bars, then loop):\n2140\t\n2141\t```js\n2142\t{ bpm: 108, steps: 2, tracks: [\n2143\t  { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse', vol: .12, notes:\n2144\t    'G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 D5 E5 - C5 - | A4 - D5 - F5 - A5 - | G5 - - - - - . . | E5 - G5 - C6 - B5 A5 | G5 - E5 - F5 - D5 - | C5 - E5 D5 C5 - B4 - | C5 - - - - - . .' },\n2145\t  { name: 'counter', wave: 'square', vol: .06, notes:\n2146\t    'E4 - E4 - G4 - C5 - | C5 - C5 B4 C5 - A4 - | F4 - F4 - A4 - D5 - | D5 - - - B4 - . . | C5 - E5 - G5 - G5 F5 | E5 - C5 - D5 - B4 - | A4 - C5 B4 A4 - G4 - | E4 - - - - - . .' },\n2147\t  { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes:\n2148\t    'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . | F2 . C3 . F2 . C3 . | D3 . A2 . D3 . A2 . | G2 . D3 . G2 . B2 . | C3 . G2 . E3 . C3 . | F2 . A2 . G2 . B2 . | A2 . F2 . G2 . G2 . | C3 . G2 . C3 . . .' },\n2149\t  { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h . s . h . | k . h k s . h h' } ] }\n2150\t```\n2151\t\n2152\t- **`europhoria`** (a layer, 140 bpm, `steps: 4`): drums `k . h k s . h . | k k h . s . h k`; bass on C2 and G2 in\n2153\t  sixteenths; brass stabs (saw, short `gate: .4`) on the off-beats: `. . C5 . . . E5 . | . . G5 . . . E5 .`. Start it\n2154\t  with the tracks `on: false` and bring them in with `audio.layer(name, 1, .4)` when Europhoria starts.\n2155\t- **`tension`** (60 bpm, `steps: 4`): a held minor chord (3 triangle tracks: A3, C4, E4, each held with `-` over 4\n2156\t  bars); the heartbeat as a lub-dub on every beat (drums `k k . .`, the second hit on a quieter second drum track).\n2157\t- **Kipperton chant** (a chant entry, 120 bpm): syllables `KIP PER TON` on `G4 G4 C5`, vowels `i e o`, then 3 claps;\n2158\t  repeated twice, then `WE'RE GO-ING UP THE COAST` on the anthem's first phrase.\n2159\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"6c146248-aeba-498c-b101-a34d41cac9ef","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:18:13.068Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nThe deliverable exists in the work root under its exact name. Its `<head>` starts with `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then\nthe `session.js` script, and that script is byte-identical to `vendor/session.js`. The hub metas are present with the\nvalues in §3.3, and `hub:session-howto` is at most 80 characters. No external URLs are loaded. It runs from `file://`.\n`exit-interview.json` parses, has every key of TASK.md's shape, has no empty value, uses a genre from the allowed list,\nand has 3–6 lowercase tags.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Definition of done and hand-back\n\n**Done means all of this is in and working, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features:**\n\n- [ ] The cup run: prologue, 5 rounds with their beats, team talks, challenges, the villain beat, the ending with the\n      ceremony, the parade and the credits; losing and CONTINUE; saves and CONTINUE.\n- [ ] Kick-About with all 6 teams and 5 stadiums, conditions, ball styles, 1–4 local players in co-op or versus.\n- [ ] Penalties mode; Training with 9 drills; the Sticker Album with 51 stickers; About & Credits.\n- [ ] Every mechanic of §6.3–§6.12 and §6.21; the team AI with 5 tactic profiles and gimmicks; 4 difficulties.\n- [ ] Euphoria, Europhoria, 7 super-strike paths, the Save Duel.\n- [ ] 6 stadiums with weather and lighting; crowd states, chants, the tifo and flares; 6 matchday events; replays; the\n      HUD; commentary with 300+ lines; the PA.\n- [ ] All audio in code: 15 songs, the SFX list, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices; no audio files.\n- [ ] Controls for pad (PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox in Settings), keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last\n      device; touch-only devices get the notice and the settings button.\n- [ ] The attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu (and `` ` `` / F1): TUNE sliders with reset to defaults, CHEATS, WARP (with the\n      animation and sound galleries), INFO.\n- [ ] AI Hub shared-world sessions passing the harness in all 4 runs; the game unchanged outside sessions.\n- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` passes in full; the screenshots and filmstrips have been looked at.\n- [ ] The single HTML file in the work root; `exit-interview.json` beside it; `engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md` written.\n\n**Hand-back** (TASK.md's \"Source Information\" section and exit interview):\n\n1. Write `exit-interview.json` in the work root, in TASK.md's exact shape. Fill every value (write \"unknown\" where you\n   cannot confirm something), use plain text, and check that it parses. Suggested `aiHub` values: name \"Europhoria\n   Football\"; tagline \"Over-the-top arcade football\"; description \"A broke seaside club rides its fans' euphoria\n   through Europe's grandest cup: 5-a-side arcade football with super strikes, dives, VAR and a crowd that powers your\n   team.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"European football\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls \"Stick/WASD move\n   · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L lob · R1/E skill · R2/Shift sprint · L1+R1/Space Europhoria\"; tags e.g. [\"arcade\",\n   \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"retro\"].\n2. Source Information values: Date \"2026-11-03 17:48:34\"; Source \"European football (over the top arcade style)\";\n   Plan \"PLAN.md\"; Genre and Perspective \"arcade 5-a-side football with a story cup run; TV-broadcast side-on camera\n   (40°), with classic three-quarter and aerial options\"; Tech \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff package, modified: see\n   CHANGES-ENGINE.md), its mocap player and clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain\n   JavaScript; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\"; Art Direction \"my-3D2dge's native PS1-era pixel art with HD\n   Humanoid rigs; new kits, stadiums, crowds, crests, tabloids\"; Animation \"the engine's procedural Humanoid rig with\n   mocap clips through Mocap.drive and new procedural moves (body tilt)\"; Audio \"the engine's chip synth for music and\n   SFX, plus a WebAudio crowd engine, sung chants and Animalese-style babble voices; no audio files\"; Online \"AI Hub\n   Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 2–4 players\"; Testing, Research, Environment (\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux;\n   browser unknown\" unless known), Model, Usage: fill in from the build. For Research, the planning stage read the\n   engine's handoff docs (README, API.md, parts of AI_GUIDE.md, docs/ASSETS.md, docs/MOCAP.md), the SPORTS kit, the\n   template game and its test, the mocap catalogs, and the AI Hub's README, session.js, retrofit.md and arena example.\n   Add whatever the build stage reads.\n3. Rebuild so the About pages carry the same text (§3.3), and rerun the `browser` suite.\n4. Reply in chat with the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (the same answers as\n   the JSON), and a short summary.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: tuning defaults (dev sliders)\n\n| Key | Default | Min | Max | Step | Group | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `runSpeed` | 88 | 60 | 130 | 1 | Movement | base run speed (u/s), before the pace stat |\n| `sprintMul` | 1.45 | 1.1 | 2.0 | .05 | Movement | sprint multiplier |\n| `accel` | 900 | 300 | 2000 | 50 | Movement | acceleration (u/s²) |\n| `staminaDrain` | 20 | 5 | 50 | 1 | Movement | per second of sprint |\n| `staminaRegen` | 14 | 5 | 40 | 1 | Movement | per second at rest |\n| `ballFriction` | 1.1 | .3 | 3 | .05 | Ball | rolling decay on grass |\n| `ballBounce` | .55 | .1 | .9 | .05 | Ball | restitution on grass |\n| `ballGravity` | 600 | 300 | 1000 | 10 | Ball | |\n| `trapSpeed` | 210 | 120 | 320 | 5 | Ball | the fastest ball trapped at 9 units |\n| `passSpeedMin` | 150 | 80 | 250 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | |\n| `passSpeedMax` | 300 | 200 | 450 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | |\n| `passAssistDeg` | 70 | 0 | 90 | 5 | Passing & Shooting | the High pass-assist cone |\n| `shotChargeTime` | .8 | .3 | 2 | .05 | Passing & Shooting | seconds to full power |\n| `shotSpeedMax` | 420 | 250 | 600 | 10 | Passing & Shooting | |\n| `curlStrength` | 3.2 | 0 | 8 | .1 | Passing & Shooting | aftertouch spin per second |\n| `keeperReaction` | .18 | .05 | .5 | .01 | Keepers | seconds |\n| `keeperReach` | 48 | 24 | 80 | 1 | Keepers | lateral dive reach |\n| `tackleReach` | 9 | 4 | 16 | .5 | Defending & Rules | |\n| `slideSpeed` | 190 | 100 | 300 | 5 | Defending & Rules | |\n| `foulStrictness` | 1 | 0 | 2 | .05 | Defending & Rules | × the referee's own |\n| `diveSuccess` | 1 | 0 | 2 | .05 | Defending & Rules | × the referee's gullibility |\n| `euphoriaGain` | 1 | 0 | 4 | .1 | Euphoria | × every gain |\n| `euphoriaDecay` | 1.5 | 0 | 6 | .1 | Euphoria | per second |\n| `europhoriaTime` | 8 | 3 | 20 | .5 | Euphoria | seconds |\n| `superSpeed` | 520 | 300 | 800 | 10 | Euphoria | |\n| `aiReaction` | .25 | .05 | .8 | .01 | AI | seconds between decisions (Normal; difficulty scales it) |\n| `aiAccuracy` | .8 | .3 | 1 | .05 | AI | |\n| `aiAggression` | .5 | 0 | 1 | .05 | AI | |\n| `halfLength` | 120 | 20 | 300 | 10 | Match | real seconds (Settings sets it; the slider overrides it while changed) |\n| `gameSpeed` | 1 | .25 | 2 | .05 | Match | `game.timeScale` |\n\n## Appendix B: network messages\n\nAll JSON. Numbers rounded (positions to integers, angles in hundredths of a radian).\n\n- **Client → host, `i` (input), unreliable, 15/s:**\n  `{ t: 'i', s: seq, at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), m: [mx100, my100], a: [ax100, ay100] | 0, h: heldBits, c: [pass, shoot, lob, through, skill, sw, dive, euphoria] }`.\n  `heldBits`: 1 sprint, 2 pass, 4 shoot, 8 lob, 16 through, 32 skill, 64 sw, 128 dive. `c` holds cumulative press\n  counts since the round started: the host takes `c[k] > last[k]` as a press, so a lost packet loses no presses. The\n  host keeps the newest by `s`.\n- **Client → host, reliable, rare:** `{ t: 'duel', id, at }` (the Save Duel press, in `AIHub.time()` ms);\n  `{ t: 'cel', k: 0..3 }` (the celebration pick); `{ t: 'menu', open: true|false }` (the settings overlay: the host\n  gives that footballer to the CPU while open).\n- **Host → all, `s` (snapshot), unreliable, 14/s, under 1,100 bytes:**\n  `{ t: 's', n, at, b: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, spin100, owner], p: [[x, y, z, vx, vy, f100, st, act, u100, flags], ×10],\n  r: [x, y, f100, st], m: [mode, clock10, minute, s0, s1, eu0, eu1, euSide, euT10, setpiece], c: [[hubId, footballerIdx], ...] }`.\n  `st` and `act` are small integer codes from a shared table; `flags` packs cards, glow, human-held and down.\n- **Host → all, `E` (events), reliable, at most 5/s:** `{ t: 'E', n, list: [[eventSeq, at, type, data], ...] }`,\n  coalescing the events of up to 200 ms: goal, whistle, card, VAR, commentary line ids (so every copy shows the same\n  lines), sfx cues, the super strike's start, the duel's start, celebrations, set-piece starts, half time, full time.\n  Clients apply each `eventSeq` once, in order.\n- **Host → all, last:** a reliable `s` with `over: 1`, then `AIHub.finish(...)`.\n\n## Appendix C: data shapes\n\n```js\nEF.def('team', 'kipperton', { name: 'KIPPERTON ATHLETIC', short: 'KIP', nick: 'THE KIPPERS', city: 'KIPPERTON',\n  stadium: 'smokehouse', formation: '2-1-1', tactic: 'plucky', chant: 'kipperton', celebration: 'fishslap',\n  crowd: { factor: 1 }, manager: 'mags',\n  kits: { home: { shirt: '#f08a24', color2: '#1c2a5a', pattern: 'hoops', shorts: '#1c2a5a', socks: '#f08a24', number: '#ffffff' },\n          away: { shirt: '#eef0f4', color2: '#f08a24', pattern: 'sash', shorts: '#eef0f4', socks: '#1c2a5a', number: '#1c2a5a' },\n          keeper: { shirt: '#3ac06a', color2: '#1a5a30', pattern: 'plain', shorts: '#1a1a1a', socks: '#3ac06a', glove: '#f4f4f0' } },\n  crest: { shape: 'shield', field: '#1c2a5a', ring: '#f08a24', charges: ['kipper', 'anchor'] },\n  players: [\n    { id: 'crabb', name: 'WALLY CRABB', num: 1, pos: 'GK', build: 'bulky', size: 1.2, hair: 'bald', skin: '#e0b090', hairColor: '#c8c8c8',\n      stats: { pace: 60, shoot: 30, pass: 55, tackle: 40, skill: 20, keep: 76, weight: 80, temper: 30 }, voice: { f0: 120, wave: 'pulse' } },\n    { id: 'pilchard', name: 'DAZ PILCHARD', num: 9, pos: 'FWD', captain: true, super: 'smoked-kipper', build: 'heroic', size: 1.15,\n      hair: 'short', skin: '#f0c8a8', hairColor: '#5a3a22', stats: { pace: 80, shoot: 90, pass: 70, tackle: 45, skill: 75, keep: 10, weight: 60, temper: 50 },\n      voice: { f0: 150, wave: 'saw' }, celebration: 'fishslap' } /* ...3 more */ ] });\n\nEF.def('formation', '1-2-1', { roles: {\n  GK: { base: [.03, .5], keeper: true },\n  DEF: { base: [.22, .5], att: [.14, 0], def: [0, 0], pull: [.45, .55], uRange: [.08, .62] },\n  MIDL: { base: [.42, .28], att: [.12, -.06], def: [-.12, .04], pull: [.55, .45], uRange: [.15, .85] },\n  MIDR: { base: [.42, .72], att: [.12, .06], def: [-.12, -.04], pull: [.55, .45], uRange: [.15, .85] },\n  FWD: { base: [.64, .5], att: [.18, 0], def: [-.12, 0], pull: [.5, .6], uRange: [.35, .95] } }, drop: 'MIDR' });\n\nEF.def('tactic', 'keepball', { press: .55, pressers: 1, line: .5, width: .6, tempo: .85, passRisk: .2, shortBias: .9,\n  longBall: .05, dribble: .25, skill: .3, shootRange: 170, shootBias: .8, foul: .1, dive: .1, euphoriaUse: 'attack', gimmick: 'keepball' });\n\nEF.def('referee', 'severo', { name: 'SERGIO SEVERO', strictness: 1.2, gullibility: .7, varHappy: .9, voice: { f0: 135, wave: 'saw' } });\n\nEF.def('stadium', 'smokehouse', { name: 'THE SMOKEHOUSE', city: 'KIPPERTON', capacity: 3112, time: 'dusk',\n  weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .7, wind: .4 }, surface: 'wet', mud: [[.06, .5, 40], [.94, .5, 40]], puddles: 6,\n  grass: ['#3f7a34', '#4a8a3c'], wear: .6, lines: '#e8ece0',\n  stands: { north: { tiers: 3, roof: 'corrugated', seats: '#3a3a48' }, west: { tiers: 2, kind: 'terrace' }, east: { tiers: 2, kind: 'terrace' } },\n  crowd: { size: 600, home: .8 }, skyline: [['chimney', .12, 90, { smoke: true }], ['lighthouse', .85, 120, { beam: true }]],\n  lights: { ambient: .55, floodlights: 4, color: '#fff0d0' }, boards: [\"SMOKY JOE'S KIPPERS\", 'GULL INSURANCE: WE COVER EVERYTHING', 'PIE-O-MATIC'],\n  events: ['seagull', 'floodlight', 'invader-keith'], music: null });\n\nEF.def('super', 'smoked-kipper', { name: 'THE SMOKED KIPPER', path: 'wobble', params: { amp: 18, freq: 7 }, trail: 'smoke',\n  color: '#f08a24', ball: 'kipper', sfx: 'super-kipper', lines: 'super-kipper' });\n\nEF.def('celebration', 'kneeslide', { name: 'KNEE SLIDE', clip: 'Slide_Loop', proc: 'armsOut', travel: { speed: 120, t: 1.1 },\n  euphoria: 8, crowd: 'roar' });\n\nEF.def('event', 'seagull', { stadiums: ['smokehouse'], chance: .6, when: { minute: [10, 80], ballLoose: true, notSetPiece: true },\n  start(m) { /* spawn the gull on the ball */ },\n  update(m, dt) { /* pin the ball; flap away when a player is within 10 */ return this.gone; },   // true when finished\n  lines: 'event-seagull' });\n\nEF.def('drill', 'passing', { title: 'PASS MASTER', coach: 'mags', stadium: 'rec', teaches: ['pass', 'through', 'oneTwo'],\n  setup(m) { /* two teammates, cones */ },\n  steps: [ { say: ['Five passes. Feet, not faces.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', count: 5 } },\n           { say: ['Now a through ball. Into space.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', where: { kind: 'through' }, count: 2 } },\n           { say: ['One-two. Give it and go.'], goal: { event: 'passDone', where: { kind: 'oneTwo' }, count: 1 } } ],\n  reward: { sticker: null } });\n\nEF.def('beat', 'r2-pre', { round: 2, steps: [\n  { kind: 'travel', to: 'solera', postcard: \"WISH YOU WERE HERE (IT'S HOT)\" },\n  { kind: 'tabloid', headline: 'PASS THE PARCEL', sub: 'Kippers must stop the passing masters... if they can find the ball.',\n    photo: { team: 'pasapasa', player: 'pasarela', pose: 'hips', expr: 'smile' } },\n  { kind: 'talk', lines: [['pasarela', 'You will chase the ball until you are dizzy, little fishes.']] },\n  { kind: 'teamtalk' }, { kind: 'challenge', id: 'recover5' }, { kind: 'tunnel' }, { kind: 'match' } ] });\n\n// EF.lines(pool, entries) is shorthand for EF.def('lines', pool, entries)\nEF.lines('goal', [\n  { who: 'barry', text: 'OH, YOU BEAUTY! {$player} has absolutely LEATHERED it!' },\n  { who: 'barry', text: 'GET IN! Back of the net from {$player}!', reply: { who: 'trev', text: 'Keeper had no chance. None. Nada. Zilch.' } },\n  { who: 'barry', text: 'OH MY COD! KIPPERTON HAVE SCORED!', when: m => m.lastGoal.team === 'kipperton' } ]);\n```\n\n## Appendix D: music sketches\n\nStarting points in the engine's song format (`audio.music(song)`); refine by ear. All of them are original.\n\n**`anthem`** (108 bpm, `steps: 2`, so each token is an eighth note; 8 bars, then loop):\n\n```js\n{ bpm: 108, steps: 2, tracks: [\n  { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse', vol: .12, notes:\n    'G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 D5 E5 - C5 - | A4 - D5 - F5 - A5 - | G5 - - - - - . . | E5 - G5 - C6 - B5 A5 | G5 - E5 - F5 - D5 - | C5 - E5 D5 C5 - B4 - | C5 - - - - - . .' },\n  { name: 'counter', wave: 'square', vol: .06, notes:\n    'E4 - E4 - G4 - C5 - | C5 - C5 B4 C5 - A4 - | F4 - F4 - A4 - D5 - | D5 - - - B4 - . . | C5 - E5 - G5 - G5 F5 | E5 - C5 - D5 - B4 - | A4 - C5 B4 A4 - G4 - | E4 - - - - - . .' },\n  { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes:\n    'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . | F2 . C3 . F2 . C3 . | D3 . A2 . D3 . A2 . | G2 . D3 . G2 . B2 . | C3 . G2 . E3 . C3 . | F2 . A2 . G2 . B2 . | A2 . F2 . G2 . G2 . | C3 . G2 . C3 . . .' },\n  { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h . s . h . | k . h k s . h h' } ] }\n```\n\n- **`europhoria`** (a layer, 140 bpm, `steps: 4`): drums `k . h k s . h . | k k h . s . h k`; bass on C2 and G2 in\n  sixteenths; brass stabs (saw, short `gate: .4`) on the off-beats: `. . C5 . . . E5 . | . . G5 . . . E5 .`. Start it\n  with the tracks `on: false` and bring them in with `audio.layer(name, 1, .4)` when Europhoria starts.\n- **`tension`** (60 bpm, `steps: 4`): a held minor chord (3 triangle tracks: A3, C4, E4, each held with `-` over 4\n  bars); the heartbeat as a lub-dub on every beat (drums `k k . .`, the second hit on a quieter second drum track).\n- **Kipperton chant** (a chant entry, 120 bpm): syllables `KIP PER TON` on `G4 G4 C5`, vowels `i e o`, then 3 claps;\n  repeated twice, then `WE'RE GO-ING UP THE COAST` on the anthem's first phrase.\n","numLines":210,"startLine":1950,"totalLines":2159}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PBZtW5JMEtF6cQwBMxVwa5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
