store.get\\|new E.Shell\\|game.menu(\\|game.script\\|game.tween\\|E.rng\\|game.note\\|input.rumble\\|r.glowDisc\\|px.blend\\|px.polyDither\\|E.font.width\\|E.font.wrap\\|game.cam.frame\\|cam.frame\\|game.hitFx\\|game.setZoom\\|game.rotateView\\|resetCamera\\|game.freeze\\|E.bootSplash\\|game.fail\\b\\|game.back\\|E.sprite\\b\\|E.recolor\\|E.anim\\b\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Look up core engine API names"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hdXsGgcB1VQDcypzjMD1U","type":"tool_result","content":"179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n216:- `E.recolor(spr, map)` †: a copy of a sprite with its colors swapped (palette swaps: the second player, a hurt flash, a stronger enemy): recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a', h: '#e0b040' }), each key a color or one of the sprite's own characters\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n361:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n362:- `E.font.wrap(s, maxW, o)`: split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n472:- `game.back()`: a step back, as a phone's back gesture asks for (the engine calls it for one; a back button of the game's own can): the open menu screen goes back one; else the scene's own back() takes it (it returns true when it did); else a scene in play pauses into the menu, and a paused one goes on. Returns false where there is nowhere to go (a title)\n477:- `game.fail(where, e)`: report an error in game code without stopping the game: logged once per place and message, kept in game.errors and shown on the error panel (the engine reports its own callbacks' errors this way): game.fail('power ' + id, err)\n481:- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n487:- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a tween or script (until it is done), a generator (run as a script of its own, and waited for), E.all([...]) or E.any([...]) (each of these). It runs at once to its first yield. Cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials, attract modes. Returns the Script\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize crisply at the new size; HUD text and overlays stay the same.\n504:- `game.start({ back })`: a scene's back() takes a phone's back gesture (game.back()) first: return true when it went back somewhere (a sub-menu closed)\n508:- `game.tween(target, to, seconds, o)` †: ease target's numbers to new values over seconds of game time: game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat (more plays; -1 forever), yoyo (every other play runs back), onDone(target), keep (outlive the scene) }). ease: a name in E.ease ('outQuad' by default) or a function of u 0..1. It starts from the values the target has once its delay is over. Returns the Tween: tween.done, tween.cancel()\n581:- `E.bootSplash(title = '')`: the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over\n586:- `new E.Script(game, fn, o = {}) → script` †: a script, made by game.script: done (it returned, or was cancelled), value (what it returned), cancel(); another script can yield it\n591:- `new E.Tween(game, target, to, seconds, o = {}) → tween` †: a tween, made by game.tween: done (it ended, or was cancelled), cancel(); a script can yield it\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id: sprite } } (sprites are E.sprite data; a color may be 'material:tone', tone deep | sh | base | lt | hi)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1504:- `mode7.sprite(spr, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: gather a sprite (E.sprite, or E.anim's frames at o.t, the game's time by default), its foot at the point: o.scale (world units a sprite pixel, 1), o.flip\n1581:- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"8da3660f-c164-4344-8c18-dc52e3be1da6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:22:42.205Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n216:- `E.recolor(spr, map)` †