{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5iQA9QU7ukvsLWEEWz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DkSBezWYUb7T61oQg3pYih","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739/engine; grep -n \"^- \\`r\\.\\|^- \\`new E.Backdrop\\|^- \\`bg.draw\\|^- \\`lights\\.\\|^- \\`game.lights\\|^- \\`r.queue\\|^- \\`E.ui\\.\\|^- \\`px\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -80","description":"List renderer, lights, ui and px API entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1337,"cache_read_input_tokens":483203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1337},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"99f90b23-fe55-4d2d-8f50-e07bbb8990a6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:56:46.280Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5iPtmgoCgYb6xLLasA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DkSBezWYUb7T61oQg3pYih":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739/engine; grep -n \"^- \\`r\\.\\|^- \\`new E.Backdrop\\|^- \\`bg.draw\\|^- \\`lights\\.\\|^- \\`game.lights\\|^- \\`r.queue\\|^- \\`E.ui\\.\\|^- \\`px\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -80","description":"List renderer, lights, ui and px API entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkSBezWYUb7T61oQg3pYih","type":"tool_result","content":"197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n198:- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n201:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n203:- `px.glow(g, e = 1)`: GPU lighting: what follows glows (0..1). No effect in Canvas mode, so call it freely.\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n208:- `px.reset(g)`: forget the color cache (after drawing on g with the canvas API directly)\n209:- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turned about its center: E.rotSprite), steps, scale (nearest-neighbour) }\n366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n367:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n368:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n369:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame unlit\n370:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n371:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n372:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n373:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n374:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n375:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n376:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n377:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n378:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n379:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n380:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n405:- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n406:- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n407:- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, ri\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is dr\n409:- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n410:- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n411:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk\n412:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n413:- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n414:- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n415:- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n416:- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n417:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n422:- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040',\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit }))\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lig\n428:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov\n432:- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..\n434:- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\n435:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n437:- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\n438:- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n441:- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n442:- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\n443:- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n445:- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\n446:- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\n447:- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\n448:- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\n449:- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\n531:- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in draw)\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea\n1156:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n1157:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1158:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1159:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"75ee2854-2ce8-4a42-b75a-e1e3bdb8a23b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:56:46.310Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n198:- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.dis