{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mh97vrjaWEGRVBpfFzj3nB","type":"tool_result","content":"1:SOURCE: European football (over the top arcade style)\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739.html]. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nThe title was picked the way TASK.md asks: 50 riffs on \"European football\" were brainstormed, then Python's\n`secrets.randbelow(50)` (OS entropy, not a seeded generator) chose index 0, **Europhoria Football** (Euro + euphoria).\nUse exactly this title everywhere: the title screen, `<title>`, the About screen, the AI Hub card, the exit interview.\nDo not pick again.\n| **Dev folder** | `EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174834/` inside the work root. All dev files go here. |\n| **Deliverable** | `EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174834.html` in the work root: one file, everything inlined, runs from `file://`. |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf