{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, ScheduleWakeup, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - /goal (enforced by a Stop hook): \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes following PLAN.md and using its title (Europhoria Football); TASK.md wins on disagreements; deliver its file name and reply sections.\n   - TASK.md constraints (security/process, verbatim essentials): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Testing: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count... Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Commit/push only if asked (not asked; nothing committed).\n   - Later user message: \"Check the result of the background full test run (task btklcjbyq) and finish the hand-back.\"\n   - Latest Stop hook feedback: file name must be evidenced as derived from TASK.md template; TASK.md features must be shown verified line by line against the running game; audio/balance concerns.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff), headless Node via vm, game.advance fixed 1/120 steps, scenes, E.Humanoid rigs, Mocap.drive, TileMap, r.queue/actor/overlay, canvas lighting, E.Dialog, Settings specs, Input presets/halfKeys, E.Shell pause menu (game.o.menu.items).\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world: AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[2,4], card:true}), ready(), answer(), time(), send, finish, events card/start/leave/time-up/end; harness.html checks (__hubCheck.pass).\n   - Host-authoritative sim + presentation reading state/events (EF.bus); replay ring buffer; WebAudio crowd/chants/babble through engine buses.\n   - Single-file bundling with session.js first in head; EF_ABOUT injected from exit-interview.json.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (work root = /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-071739__xcf3323/work):\n   - Work root contents now: dev folder `EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739/`, deliverable `EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739.html` (~2.2 MB), PLAN.md, STAGE.md, TASK.md, exit-interview.json.\n   - TASK.md line 11: \"Package: ... provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739.html]\"; line 24: \"Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739] ... bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-071739].html in root\". Line 1: \"SOURCE: European football (over the top arcade style)\".\n   - PLAN.md lines 5-8: title picked by `secrets.randbelow(50)` index 0 → Europhoria Football, \"Do not pick again\". Lines 18-19 use the same substitution convention `EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174834`.\n   - Dev folder layout: engine/my-3d2dge.js (+ CHANGES-ENGINE.md listing 5 EF changes: dialog voice fn, audio buses bus()/now()/noiseBuffer(), Humanoid o.kit patterns+numbers, Humanoid tilt state `_tilt`, accented font glyphs), tools/patches/patch.mjs + p1-dialog-audio.mjs + p2-humanoid-font.mjs, vendor/session.js (1.4.0 unmodified), vendor/mocap/{readable,mocap}.js, mocap/ef-clips.js (31 clips, names without SET: prefix), src/00-core … 90-start (40 fragments), tools/build.mjs, tools/test.mjs, tools/lib/{load.mjs (vm loader with o.hub, o.now, o.search, o.hash, o.media), playthrough.mjs, hubsim.mjs, hubtest.mjs, browser.mjs, sweep.mjs, audiocheck.mjs}, tools/{shot.mjs, grid.mjs, check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs}, tools/harness/{harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}, PROGRESS.md, TASK-CHECKLIST.md (line-by-line TASK.md → built in → evidence table), shots/grid*.png, node_modules (playwright), package.json. .scratch, .tmp, tools/scratch deleted.\n   - src fragments: 00-core (EF, registries EF.def/get/all, EF.bus, EF.TUNE/T/tuneSet/tuneReset/tuneChanged, EF.link incl. #touchonly, broadcast view, EF.KEYS incl mpass/mshoot/mlob/dev, EF.SETTINGS incl glyphs playstation default, Game, EF.DIFF {easy/normal/hard/europhoric with react, acc, agg, keeper, eu, cpuSuper, shotErr, pace} and EF.diff()), 01-input (HumanController, chord, mouse aim, touchOnly), 02-glyphs, 03-audio (SFX, 16 SONG, EF.crowdAudio, chants, EF.babble, audioDebug rethrow), 04-art, 05-anim (EF.KICKS, kickState), 10-match … 20-events (sim), 21-camera, 22-replay, 23-commentary, 24-hud, 25-view, 26-crowd, 27-cast, 30-ui, 31-front (Stage, title, sidePicker, setup, results, album, about; `front()` helper copies non-reserved methods), 32-cup (bracket, beats, tunnel/card, ending), 33-match (MatchAudio, match scene, halftime panel), 34-training (DrillRunner), 40-attract, 41-devmode (EF.Dev, EF.parts with clear(), deepLink, devanim gallery, soundtest), 42-hub, 43-saves, 50-teams, 51-stadiums, 52-story (+retry beats), 53-lines (~330 lines, contractions escaped), 54-drills (reserves team, gk() helper), 55-chants, 90-start (debug snapshot, EF.test, EF.validate, scene wrapping for dev, touchEnabled=false, game.start).\n   - Recent key code: TeamBrain `get diff() { return this.m.hasHuman(this.s) && this.m.kind !== 'attract' ? EF.DIFF.normal : this.m.diff; }`; Footballer.speedMax CPU pace factor; shoot sig × diff.shotErr for CPU sides; EF.parts.clear(m, f) moves opponents within 70 away; duel test uses `search: '?seed=7'`.\n   - exit-interview.json (final, parses, no empty fields, 4/6/4 answers): testing \"18 suites ... (526 checks)\"; usage \"Session time about 3 hours 10 minutes (07:17 to about 10:27); token count and API cost unknown (no usage meter was available to this session)\"; testingFeedback[0] \"About 37: 25 in the game and 12 in the tests themselves...\"; [1] \"8 were critical...\"; aiHub name Europhoria Football, tagline \"Over-the-top arcade football\", type Game, genre Sports, source European football, series \"\", players \"1–4\", tags [\"arcade\",\"pixel art\",\"comedy\",\"versus\",\"co-op\",\"story\"]. About pages in the html verified to match the JSON exactly.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (major):\n   - Placement orders (t:99) never cleared → frozen players: added Match.clearPlacement() on all live restarts.\n   - Keeper never saved corner shots: softened q curve/speed factor.\n   - Too many reds → kickoff crash: severity /175, red thresholds 2.6/1.35, no reds below 3 outfield; kickoff taker fallback.\n   - EF.scenes undefined at load: defined in 00-core.\n   - front() scenes lost methods (this.play not a function): copy non-reserved props.\n   - Retry beats defined before story: moved to 52-story.\n   - Reserves no captain; human auto-switched to GK; Math.random in sim; pass under-lead (friction-aware lead); apostrophe syntax errors; stray comma.\n   - Drill keeper lookups null (keeper() excludes ghosts) → gk() helper.\n   - Attract duel draw crash (D.human null) → duelText guard; browser sweep added.\n   - Difficulty applied to human teammates → TeamBrain.diff getter + shotErr/pace; curve test now easy +0.5, normal −0.25, hard −0.83.\n   - Audio test leak from attract mode → run from devanim scene; crowd reaction gains lowered.\n   - Flaky duel test (random seed, tackle before super) → EF.parts.clear + seed 7.\n   - UI fixes: PA strip, prompt bar above commentary, replay tag top, title layout, results panel, trophy glow, night ambient, snow texture, hub card centering + smooth countdown.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All suites pass: final run \"Europhoria tests: 526 passed, 0 failed (833.5 s)\". Hub harness passes 2p, 4p lag/loss, host-leave, server. Audio peaks measured (sfx ~0.1–0.23, music ~0.22, roar ~0.28, voices ~0.13; silence and sliders-at-0 = 0).\n   - Remaining concern from Stop hook: evidencing name derivation from TASK.md template and line-by-line TASK verification against running game.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - /goal command with the condition quoted above (Stop hook active).\n   - \"Check the result of the background full test run (task btklcjbyq) and finish the hand-back.\"\n   - (Stop hook feedback messages twice, system-generated, asking for evidence on file names, TASK line-by-line verification, audio/balance.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Satisfy the Stop hook: add a `task` suite (planned tools/lib/taskcheck.mjs, registered in tools/test.mjs) that checks every TASK.md requirement against the running game, including deriving the deliverable/dev-folder name from TASK.md's template text ([GameTitle-SOURCE-...] with GameTitle = title \"Europhoria Football\" without spaces, SOURCE = \"European football\" → EuropeanFootball) and asserting both exist; run with --report printing each item; then give a final reply containing the four sections (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback) plus the evidence. If the deliverable changes, rebuild and re-verify; keep exit-interview.json consistent with the build (About must match).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Responding to the latest Stop hook feedback. I had just run:\n   `grep -n \"GameTitle\\|^SOURCE\" TASK.md; sed -n 5,8p PLAN.md; sed -n 18,19p PLAN.md`\n   which showed TASK.md line 11 and 24 templates, SOURCE line 1, PLAN.md's RNG title choice and its own identical substitution convention. Next I was going to write tools/lib/taskcheck.mjs (a `task` suite) with --report output listing each TASK.md requirement (R1 source/OTT, R2 genre/perspective, R3 title RNG, R4 package name from template, R5 engine, R6 art, R7 animation tilt, R8 audio in code/no audio files + measured output, R9 online harness, R10 dev folder/root contents, R11 server binding by PID, R12 test command format, R13 modes reachable, R14 dev mode from pause + sliders + reset, R15 attract, R16 local multiplayer, R17 tone, R18-R21 10-foot UI/keyboard/mouse/glyph prompts/no dense screens, R22 touch-only, R23 no TODO/placeholder/stub, R24 About screen sections, R25 exit-interview shape) and run it.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write and run the `task` conformance suite as described, quoting from my last message: \"I'll make the remaining points verifiable, not just asserted. A new `task` suite checks every TASK.md requirement against the running game, line by line, including deriving the deliverable's name from TASK.md's own template text. Then I'll run it with a report so each item's result shows in the transcript.\" Then post the final reply with the four required sections (same content as exit-interview.json) and the line-by-line results.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-071739--xcf3323-work/452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452d6482-9020-4e99-982f-14f7a7dcf527","uuid":"d512fac0-454d-430d-8fd7-43ae9221bec7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:22:56.238Z","isSynthetic":true}
